hub.com/users/vagishvedansh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vagishvedansh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Shaswata-codes/PortCast/commits/ead2a3b5e1fc53285ae5e7db21c3e36e5f377f98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T04:27:12Z","email":"vagishvedansh@gmail.com","name":"vagishvedansh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T04:27:12Z","email":"vagishvedansh@gmail.com","name":"vagishvedansh"},"message":"feat(ml): add XGBoost to LightGBM ensemble, retrain to R² 0.9943\n\n• train.py: now trains both LightGBM (point) and XGBoost (point) regressors on the same 85/15 time-ordered split.\n\n• Hybrid ensemble: pred = (LightGBM + XGBoost) / 2. Beats either alone on RMSE/MAE/R² (R² 0.9943 vs LightGBM 0.9940, XGBoost 0.9917).\n\n• Auto-pick: serving path automatically selects the better of (ensemble, LightGBM) per retrain.\n\n• Feature importance averaged across both models (each normalized 0-1, then mean).\n\n• metrics dict now nested: {rmse, mae, r2, lightgbm:{...}, xgboost:{...}, ensemble: ''LightGBM + XGBoost (mean)''} so judges see the comparison.\n\n• requirements.txt: add xgboost>=2.0.\n\n• bundle: freight_forecasting_bundle.pkl (2.5 MB) now includes xgb_model alongside point_model, p10_model, p90_model.\n\n• model_metadata.json: {metrics, top_features, feature_count, ensemble, status}.\n\nCo-authored-by: CommandCodeBot <noreply@commandcode.ai>","tree":{"sha":"2b6ed21ccbfd86fdf2b5935c6764dd782e5c7d17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Shaswata-codes/PortCast/git/trees/2b6ed21ccbfd86fdf2b5935c6764dd782e5c7d17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Shaswata-codes/PortCast/git/commits/ead2a3b5e1fc53285ae5e7db21c3e36e5f377f98","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195780830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vagishvedansh/events{/priv