a0/aegis/commit/2e8dd11b40ee1f6741f64b634e672e3c248a0a52","node_id":"C_kwDOUDDMq9oAKDJlOGRkMTFiNDBlZTFmNjc0MWY2NGI2MzRlNjcyZTNjMjQ4YTBhNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SajithYahya0/aegis/commit/42ef6efdd0a563995613b211d4e4df50ed991323","sha":"42ef6efdd0a563995613b211d4e4df50ed991323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/commits/42ef6efdd0a563995613b211d4e4df50ed991323"}],"sha":"2e8dd11b40ee1f6741f64b634e672e3c248a0a52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/commits/2e8dd11b40ee1f6741f64b634e672e3c248a0a52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166856158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SajithYahya0","id":166856158,"login":"SajithYahya0","node_id":"U_kgDOCfIF3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/commits/42ef6efdd0a563995613b211d4e4df50ed991323/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:36:03Z","email":"166856158+SajithYahya0@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sajith Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:36:03Z","email":"166856158+SajithYahya0@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sajith Yahya"},"message":"Week 5: SSR/ISR/SSG site, Module Federation remote, tests across three apps\n\nConvert to npm workspaces and split the app three ways, each with a reason:\n\n- apps/web    the existing Vite SPA, unchanged in size: CSR behind a login.\n- apps/public new Next App Router site. Marketing SSG, /quote ISR on the\n              hourly rate card, /status SSR with the claims history streamed\n              in below the summary, plus loading.tsx and error.tsx.\n- apps/claims new Module Federation remote owning the claim intake form, so\n              claims-ops ships it without a console release.\n\nThe two apps talk: the site''s /api/quote-requests route handler records\nwebsite enquiries and the console''s dashboard reads them back through a Vite\ndev proxy.\n\nFederation uses @originjs/vite-plugin-federation, the Vite implementation of\nthe webpack spec; react, react-dom, MUI and emotion are shared singletons so\nthe remote''s form renders inside the console''s theme. The host states the\ncontract in src/remotes.d.ts rather than mapping claims/* at the source,\nbecause typechecking against source the console does not ship would be false\nconfidence and would not survive the repo split.\n\n27 tests, no snapshots: six behaviour tests in the console, the remote driven\nthrough the props the host passes it, and three in the site covering use()\nunwrapping under Suspense, the route handler''s validation, and the streamed\nserver component.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b54bcaa72654695c0938e6b13fc5d063c3a0973c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/git/trees/b54bcaa72654695c0938e6b13fc5d063c3a0973c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/git/commits/42ef6efdd0a563995613b211d4e4df50ed991323","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166856158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/events{/privacy}"