"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166856158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SajithYahya0","id":166856158,"login":"SajithYahya0","node_id":"U_kgDOCfIF3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/commits/6c85242ed45eae2c90e2cd0cd39e0cf5b21d79f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:54:51Z","email":"166856158+SajithYahya0@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sajith Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:54:51Z","email":"166856158+SajithYahya0@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sajith Yahya"},"message":"Docs: repoint stale references, drop unenforceable line anchors\n\nThe runsheet pinned a (Lnn) anchor beside every file path and nothing\nenforced them, so each header edit rotted a few silently. Two rotted this\nphase from my own edits — main.tsx L44 for createRoot, which is now L90,\nand PolicySummaryCard L79 for the use() call, now L87 — and a dozen more\nhad drifted by 60-170 lines over earlier phases. All 83 are removed; the\ncells now carry path + export, which is what the newer rows and the whole\nof coverage-matrix.md already do. The four non-line-number spans that\nshare the class ((3 tests), (table)) are untouched, so the .ln rule is\nstill live.\n\nTwo file cells named modules that do not exist and never will:\n\n- useOnlineStatus.ts. There is no such hook. subscribe and getSnapshot\n  are module-level functions in ConnectivityBanner.tsx and the hook is\n  called inline, which the say cell now states — module scope is what\n  keeps those identities stable, and that is load-bearing rather than\n  incidental.\n- usePrevious.ts. The previous-value pattern is two refs written during\n  render inside StickyPremiumSummary, so the row now names\n  currentPremiumRef / previousPremiumRef.\n\nBoth rows'' data-s search attributes carried the dead names too, and are\nupdated with them.\n\ncoverage-matrix.md W4-D2-01 cited src/shared/theme/theme.d.ts two\nclauses before explaining, correctly, that the file is called\nmui-augment.d.ts and why theme.d.ts would be swallowed by TypeScript''s\nwildcard matcher. Path corrected; the prose was already right.\n\nEvery src/ and docs/ path referenced under docs/ now resolves, except two\nleft deliberately: tokenStore.ts in qa-drills 10.3 and AuthContext.tsx in\nphase-prompts.md, both prose about code that is gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9dc5e42e9b48e7ff2e1ab39b913e6b693ac6267e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/git/trees/9dc5e42e9b48e7ff2e1ab39b913e6b693ac6267e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/git/commits/6c85242ed45eae2c90e2cd0cd39e0cf5b21d79f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166856158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SajithYahya0","id":166856158,"login":"SajithYahya0","node_id":"U_kgDOCfIF3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SajithYahya0/aegis/commit/6c85242ed45eae2c90e2cd0cd39e0cf5b21d79f8","node_id":"C_kwDOUDDMq9oAKDZjODUyNDJlZDQ1ZWFlMmM5MGUyY2QwY2QzOWUwY2Y1YjIxZDc5Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SajithYahya0/aegis/commit/bf1c3fb70e61d8a8b996accb7e0f9b8cc38e9605","sha":"bf1c3fb70e61d8a8b996accb7e0f9b8cc38e9605","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/commits/bf1c3fb70e61d8a8b996accb7e0f9b8cc38e9605"}],"sha":"6c85242ed45eae2c90e2cd0cd39e0cf5b21d79f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/commits/6c85242ed45eae2c90e2cd0cd39e0cf5b21d79f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166856158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SajithYahya0","id":166856158,"login":"SajithYahya0","node_id":"U_kgDOCfIF3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/commits/bf1c3fb70e61d8a8b996accb7e0f9b8cc38e9605/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:44:37Z","email":"166856158+SajithYahya0@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sajith Yahya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T19:44:37Z","email":"166856158+SajithYahya0@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sajith Yahya"},"message":"Week 4 Phase 4: Redux Toolkit auth slice, thunks, memoised selector; retire AuthContext\n\nThe session moves from Context + useState to a Redux Toolkit slice.\nQuoteContext deliberately stays on Context + useReducer as the comparison\ncase (W4-D4-05), and the two providers now sit eight lines apart in\nmain.tsx so the contrast is checkable rather than asserted.\n\n- store/index.ts: makeStore(extra) factory plus the app singleton, typed\n  RootState / AppDispatch / AppStore, and useAppSelector / useAppDispatch\n  built with withTypes rather than a cast.\n- store/authSlice.ts: switchRole and logout written as mutation (Immer''s\n  draft is what produces the new object react-redux compares); loginThunk\n  and refreshThunk through the axios client, with all six lifecycle\n  actions handled in extraReducers via the builder callback.\n- store/selectors.ts: selectRole, selectIsUnderwriter, and one\n  createSelector deriving exposure totals per customer. selectRole and\n  selectIsUnderwriter are deliberately not memoised.\n- store/useAuth.ts: useAuth() keeps its name over useAppSelector, so\n  RequireRole, AppShell and UnderwritingPage changed one import line each.\n\nThe token read moves to store.getState().auth.token, which lets\nhttp/tokenStore.ts be deleted — an interceptor cannot call useContext,\nwhich is why that second home for the token existed, and getState() is a\nplain call from anywhere. installInterceptors now takes the store and is\ncalled from store/index.ts: installing it from http/index.ts is a genuine\ncycle, and it failed at runtime with \"installInterceptors is not a\nfunction\" before being moved.\n\nUnderwritingPage gets a real body (MUI Cards + Table) because the\nmemoised selector needed a consumer; a selector nothing subscribes to is\na cache that is never hit.\n\nW3-D5-03 goes to [ ]. PolicySummaryCard''s conditional use(AuthContext)\nread was the app''s only Context read inside a branch, and it has no\nreactive replacement: use(ReactReduxContext) compiles but the store\nreference never changes, so the note would go stale on the next role\nswitch. Recorded as an honest gap rather than rehomed. W2-D2-04/05/07 and\nW3-D1-04 are rehomed onto QuoteContext and ThemeModeProvider, which were\nalready in the tree; W3-D1-04 is upgraded from [~] because that memo''s\nbail-out branch is reachable.\n\nMatrix: 106 rows, 93 [x], 7 [~], 6 [ ]. qa-drills 4.2, 4.3 and 10.3\nrewritten against the shipped code.\n\nnpx tsc --noEmit clean; npx vitest run 8 files, 36 tests passing;\nnpm run build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"244bd9e64523212494229b155cbcb8e26a9f9660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/git/trees/244bd9e64523212494229b155cbcb8e26a9f9660"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SajithYahya0/aegis/git/commits/bf1c3fb70e61d8a8b996accb7e0f9b8cc38e9605","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166856158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SajithYahya0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://gi