); drop the known gap\n- docs-api-drift is a real gate; drop the known-defect notes (rules + CLAUDE.md)\n- /readyz is declared in apis/openapi.yaml (all 8 routes)\n- adrs.md: add 0034","tree":{"sha":"324b7f1f54a7575ad8f75c6177304e340e527cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/trees/324b7f1f54a7575ad8f75c6177304e340e527cc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/commits/43b2c539508c6bcbbe6a702b24ff48ceb7f72977","verification":{"payload":"tree 324b7f1f54a7575ad8f75c6177304e340e527cc1\nparent 066819d7611ce7009381bb87375bb4789c9e357a\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791285684 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791285684 -0300\n\ndocs(claude): refresh agent rules after ADR-0034 and the docs-api-drift fix (#155)\n\n- OrderLineReleased/OrderReleased are raised now (ADR-0034); drop the known gap\n- docs-api-drift is a real gate; drop the known-defect notes (rules + CLAUDE.md)\n- /readyz is declared in apis/openapi.yaml (all 8 routes)\n- adrs.md: add 0034","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNm0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALb8QAKfR8JnNS/ShmDa2b9rPo2N8\njMOTwnP6LEZ8N8Wc2RLkfRHbVvwqMBkWPoQzhdNiXnQH4C4ywqWzQ/7Gxnf1AN5+\nSzT1j5SaJlk4I/sFD1n966UiNzMWgJJLG+gpPxixtHGERmrzlNanfcJAZpZYKkTB\npubZQzxG0oqCH5bXW+RF41HXsYG0w4SnWB3XSmHwRrWJQMcc6MzE+3rgBWaZdCwk\nTEdwz+FuMGAHG5Nm1CJ3/Mlz1cfOe+17cTVCiIZAFRk5GSbGc40VbeJZDGg7Dp7O\n4sXIu6qK2HCigyBCT3bwRex6jxEkOuNxIx9+8DtFNIt97whPCn3fhDXCdq3WlLj8\nN8RPY+1/X+ILonp+svUiLzEDfeMdqHspVDE1M34sAbHYPsl9hQ7Y9qpkRNEkBV4t\nafQgjWjEkqjy5TTJngxfj8DTbGpvnz1bUFHr7HXp7DkqT0GyhalqJ5DssDan7Qze\n547k28PXRZLs1ffkkG+eJ2YtfG7DSywAQ7GiOVuK/qXhHW/c3GV6sfc71EQFHbV5\nlYDeGRc25fegnHWvx2ZMN65P7lOzih/mGCDXiABdcLJwohZC4D3rx5S3xzsxp515\n5nzRG3Wobq1jwgzVjeQNs2wrvVGYm6y+kBDgkz6JOsBRl2s4D1+IQpINilvTUegU\nxoTZ1HxcoTz0HqCjjyAT\n=Sici\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T11:21:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/order-management/commit/43b2c539508c6bcbbe6a702b24ff48ceb7f72977","node_id":"C_kwDOUDRODNoAKDQzYjJjNTM5NTA4YzZiY2JiZTZhNzAyYjI0ZmY0OGNlYjdmNzI5Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/order-management/commit/066819d7611ce7009381bb87375bb4789c9e357a","sha":"066819d7611ce7009381bb87375bb4789c9e357a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/066819d7611ce7009381bb87375bb4789c9e357a"}],"sha":"43b2c539508c6bcbbe6a702b24ff48ceb7f72977","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/43b2c539508c6bcbbe6a702b24ff48ceb7f72977"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/066819d7611ce7009381bb87375bb4789c9e357a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:59:48Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:59:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#154)\n\n* docs(api): document GET /readyz in apis/openapi.yaml\n\nGET /readyz is registered in server.go (ADR 0025 graceful-shutdown readiness\ngate) but was absent from the OpenAPI contract. Add the operation (200 ready /\n503 not_ready) and regenerate the Docusaurus API reference (clean-api-docs +\ngen-api-docs).\n\n* ci: make the docs-api-drift job actually gate\n\nThe job runs with working-directory: docs but diffed\ndocs/docs/api-reference/rest, which resolves to docs/docs/docs/... (nonexistent),\nso `git diff --exit-code` could never fail. Use the docs/-relative pathspec\ndocs/api-reference/rest, and use `git status --porcelain` so a new generated\npage (untracked file) for a newly documented operation also fails the job.\n\nVerified locally: with the readyz spec change regenerated but uncommitted the\nold step printed NO-DRIFT while the new step exits 1 (DRIFT-DETECTED); after\ncommitting the regenerated output the new step passes.\n\n* docs(api): fix stale OpenAPI descriptions (pathId, promiseDate, Released)\n\n- OrderLine.pathId and the POST /orders description said the path is ALWAYS\n  the default `pick`; since ADR 0021 the service chooses it (eligibility\n  filter, shortest known cycle time, lower id on a tie) and only falls back\n  to `pick` when no catalogue/active path exists.\n- Order.promiseDate described only the lead-time policy; it is a capability\n  promise (ADR 0014, per-shipment-group ADR 0017, requiredShipBy ADR 0020)\n  with lead time as the fallback.\n- OrderLineStatus said Released means \"wes-work-planning accepted the work\";\n  since ADR 0005 it is a pure domain transition announced on Kafka.\n\nText only; regenerated the Docusaurus API reference (clean-api-docs +\ngen-api-docs). The web/ type comment for pathId is aligned too.\n\n* docs: drop \"readyz not in OpenAPI\" caveats now that the spec documents it\n\nFollow-up to the GET /readyz OpenAPI addition: remove the known-gap notes in\nthe DDD pack (ddd-artifacts, use-cases) and the README route table.\n\n* fix(events): raise OrderLineReleased and OrderReleased at the release transition\n\nBoth events were declared (domain, AsyncAPI, analytics projector) but no use\ncase published them, so the Order Funnel''s linesReleased/ordersReleased were\nalways 0.\n\nallocateAndRelease now calls publishReleaseFacts after the aggregate Save and\nthe OrderAllocated/OrderPartiallyAllocated publish, in the same UnitOfWork scope\n(so the transactional outbox commits them with the aggregate): one\nOrderLineReleased per line released in that pass (frozen work-unit id, line''s\nown path) and OrderReleased when the pass leaves every line Released. Nothing is\nraised for BR3-blocked, held, or lost-reservation passes. Analytics topic only;\nCloudEvents type derived from the event-name constants. Additive contract\nchange recorded in ADR 0034 (+ index, sidebar, README).\n\nTests: usecases/release_events_test.go (unit) and the Testcontainers outbox\nintegration test TestOutbox_ReceiveOrder_ReleaseFactsCommitWithTheAggregate.\nExisting event-sequence assertions updated. Docs: domain-events,\naggregate-design-canvas, class-diagram, eventstorming (hotspot -> event),\nsequence-diagrams (diagram 2), order-funnel-report note.\n\n* fix(http): resolve the unreachable ship-complete-blocked problem type\n\nThe ship-complete-blocked (409) problem type was mapped in errors.go but no\nHTTP path returned it: when BR3 blocks a release the release leg treats it as\n\"nothing to release\" and the call answers 201/200 with a Backordered order.\n\nDecision from the ADRs: that success is the contract. ADR 0003 says no line\nproceeds to release \"until RetryAllocation clears it\" (a hold, not an error;\nonly non-409 failures fail the call), ADR 0005 lists\nship-complete-still-backordered-releases-nothing as an explicit success case,\nand ADR 0020 has callers read a hold''s outcome from the order, not a 4xx. So the\ncode is right and the dead mapping is removed (statusFor + problemCatalog);\nErrShipCompleteBlocked stays a domain error. No REST contract change: the spec\nnever listed the type.\n\nTests (internal/adapters/inbound/http/br3_block_test.go) pin the contract at\nevery endpoint that reaches the release leg: POST /orders -> 201,\nretry-allocation still short -> 200, release of a held order that lost its\nreservation -> 200, each Backordered, nothing Released, never problem+json.\n\nDocs: api-reference overview (problem catalogue + BR3 note), use-cases,\naggregate-design-canvas, eventstorming (hotspot -> policy), bounded-context-canvas\n(open question closed).","tree":{"sha":"021bc0a9d5da49909d8ff8d45f15b1c21128bd1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/trees/021bc0a9d5da49909d8ff8d45f15b1c21128bd1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/commits/066819d7611ce7009381bb87375bb4789c9e357a","verification":{"payload":"tree 021bc0a9d5da49909d8ff8d45f15b1c21128bd1b\nparent 000bc8fd88465b7538a292f4db48d31c7c11f077\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791284388 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791284388 -0300\n\nfix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#154)\n\n* docs(api): document GET /readyz in apis/openapi.yaml\n\nGET /readyz is registered in server.go (ADR 0025 graceful-shutdown readiness\ngate) but was absent from the OpenAPI contract. Add the operation (200 ready /\n503 not_ready) and regenerate the Docusaurus API reference (clean-api-docs +\ngen-api-docs).\n\n* ci: make the docs-api-drift job actually gate\n\nThe job runs with working-directory: docs but diffed\ndocs/docs/api-reference/rest, which resolves to docs/docs/docs/... (nonexistent),\nso `git diff --exit-code` could never fail. Use the docs/-relative pathspec\ndocs/api-reference/rest, and use `git status --porcelain` so a new generated\npage (untracked file) for a newly documented operation also fails the job.\n\nVerified locally: with the readyz spec change regenerated but uncommitted the\nold step printed NO-DRIFT while the new step exits 1 (DRIFT-DETECTED); after\ncommitting the regenerated output the new step passes.\n\n* docs(api): fix stale OpenAPI descriptions (pathId, promiseDate, Released)\n\n- OrderLine.pathId and the POST /orders description said the path is ALWAYS\n  the default `pick`; since ADR 0021 the service chooses it (eligibility\n  filter, shortest known cycle time, lower id on a tie) and only falls back\n  to `pick` when no catalogue/active path exists.\n- Order.promiseDate described only the lead-time policy; it is a capability\n  promise (ADR 0014, per-shipment-group ADR 0017, requiredShipBy ADR 0020)\n  with lead time as the fallback.\n- OrderLineStatus said Released means \"wes-work-planning accepted the work\";\n  since ADR 0005 it is a pure domain transition announced on Kafka.\n\nText only; regenerated the Docusaurus API reference (clean-api-docs +\ngen-api-docs). The web/ type comment for pathId is aligned too.\n\n* docs: drop \"readyz not in OpenAPI\" caveats now that the spec documents it\n\nFollow-up to the GET /readyz OpenAPI addition: remove the known-gap notes in\nthe DDD pack (ddd-artifacts, use-cases) and the README route table.\n\n* fix(events): raise OrderLineReleased and OrderReleased at the release transition\n\nBoth events were declared (domain, AsyncAPI, analytics projector) but no use\ncase published them, so the Order Funnel''s linesReleased/ordersReleased were\nalways 0.\n\nallocateAndRelease now calls publishReleaseFacts after the aggregate Save and\nthe OrderAllocated/OrderPartiallyAllocated publish, in the same UnitOfWork scope\n(so the transactional outbox commits them with the aggregate): one\nOrderLineReleased per line released in that pass (frozen work-unit id, line''s\nown path) and OrderReleased when the pass leaves every line Released. Nothing is\nraised for BR3-blocked, held, or lost-reservation passes. Analytics topic only;\nCloudEvents type derived from the event-name constants. Additive contract\nchange recorded in ADR 0034 (+ index, sidebar, README).\n\nTests: usecases/release_events_test.go (unit) and the Testcontainers outbox\nintegration test TestOutbox_ReceiveOrder_ReleaseFactsCommitWithTheAggregate.\nExisting event-sequence assertions updated. Docs: domain-events,\naggregate-design-canvas, class-diagram, eventstorming (hotspot -> event),\nsequence-diagrams (diagram 2), order-funnel-report note.\n\n* fix(http): resolve the unreachable ship-complete-blocked problem type\n\nThe ship-complete-blocked (409) problem type was mapped in errors.go but no\nHTTP path returned it: when BR3 blocks a release the release leg treats it as\n\"nothing to release\" and the call answers 201/200 with a Backordered order.\n\nDecision from the ADRs: that success is the contract. ADR 0003 says no line\nproceeds to release \"until RetryAllocation clears it\" (a hold, not an error;\nonly non-409 failures fail the call), ADR 0005 lists\nship-complete-still-backordered-releases-nothing as an explicit success case,\nand ADR 0020 has callers read a hold''s outcome from the order, not a 4xx. So the\ncode is right and the dead mapping is removed (statusFor + problemCatalog);\nErrShipCompleteBlocked stays a domain error. No REST contract change: the spec\nnever listed the type.\n\nTests (internal/adapters/inbound/http/br3_block_test.go) pin the contract at\nevery endpoint that reaches the release leg: POST /orders -> 201,\nretry-allocation still short -> 200, release of a held order that lost its\nreservation -> 200, each Backordered, nothing Released, never problem+json.\n\nDocs: api-reference overview (problem catalogue + BR3 note), use-cases,\naggregate-design-canvas, eventstorming (hotspot -> policy), bounded-context-canvas\n(open question closed).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNSlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApJoQAFhwAsOgE7yNfRmGzoQDeP/m\nQf9S5Ol8kvDept9SM9ewaqI26ZpOCCqnBzZLXmAwK+PpIx3C2jTaVReSPhaTv/QV\nqmFyHk3Z+UXeoYQnu6WGA5eQd0wVZyK3stcYtmLx4AXyPkZ3HQQzBkIZ+vgib7k6\nDPksRea4zyosDHFTLmthzBU2iiTnwYEPn1vyYXp0Sd9rJT3ImLECDFXewPtrpOV4\ned5jo7Gd+QX73D276fRPRhE/PrfWbMfk0LVJj/XHRnIuzmRs+kBVRMEhJ61i3/QM\nuFN1jVobhrw/jfePDC5i4yJQSBYP9Lrb3X93nL3B9fjZOVJRdJ6fVDSJpg600SYB\nMAHZr2G322Z7yxmUnOvQ3n8CC8WRemDT2+Nu3H6sy4Fw+xOeXv+0eJeqx6fHVDJ2\nkBjsxQlmDnfyu6LMycqkWEHnAD+7Ra9B4I4DASEv2/DXyFfp4krtdMZPz9iSqeRg\nzTlwd9xKIGGXdEHEteqTCt5yFXIhOOI6MElQQ9qha5NhUKyTE4x+PK9UTF1uF9oG\nW/oOuc0y3H0DxLaEze041qG90G69dRp2irxh5Rvy1vfAovIIAkceVP4d+oHhYnhI\nwfpdKALbmb5g8WMqcQboERCsQVvbY2TuRWM8GRacQThVEnydTA41M2Nm+CWMld7H\nfv58+2CVWUD02H71z+mO\n=I1JE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T10:59:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/we