b.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/f6c2d2b887a988f4690b9770cb940c3102284f4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:49:04Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:49:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#115)\n\nProduction-blocking fleet-wide bug found during Phase 4 (k6/HPA\nload-test validation) cleanup: golang-migrate''s postgres driver takes\na session-scoped `pg_advisory_lock` to serialize concurrent migration\nruns at boot, but DATABASE_URL (warehouse-infra PR #43, PgBouncer\nrollout) points this service at PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode,\nwhich does not preserve session state across statements. Two or more\norder-management replicas starting concurrently (an HPA scale-out, or\nan ordinary rolling deploy with replicas>1) crash-loop with `pq:\nunnamed prepared statement does not exist` / `pq: canceling statement\ndue to statement timeout` for ~1-2 minutes until one wins the\nadvisory-lock race. Reproduced live.\n\ncmd/order/main.go and cmd/mcp/main.go (both run migrations at startup)\nnow read a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var for the migration step\nonly, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset:\n\n    migrationsDatabaseURL := getenv(\"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\", databaseURL)\n\nThe pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses\ndatabaseURL unchanged — every request this service serves keeps going\nthrough PgBouncer exactly as before. The fallback keeps local dev, CI\nintegration tests, and any environment that doesn''t provision the\nsplit working byte-identically to before this change.\n\nwarehouse-infra''s companion PR provisions MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL (a\ndirect, non-pooled DSN) as a new secret key alongside the existing\nDATABASE_URL key for all 9 OLTP services.\n\nAdds:\n- TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback: proves the getenv fallback in\n  both directions (falls back to DATABASE_URL when unset; uses\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, not DATABASE_URL, when set).\n- TestBuildRepoAdapters_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations:\n  proves buildRepoAdapters itself threads migrationsDatabaseURL into\n  the migration step (not databaseURL), using a schemeless\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL to get a distinctive parse error that a\n  dial/\"connection refused\" error against databaseURL could never\n  produce.\n- ADR-0029: documents the pg_advisory_lock / transaction-pooling\n  incompatibility, cross-references PgBouncer PR #43, and records the\n  live verification.\n- charts/order-management: a new `database.migrationsExistingSecretKey`\n  value (default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders a\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var, sourced from the same existingSecret,\n  in both the api and mcp Deployments (`optional: true` on the\n  secretKeyRef so a secret that predates this key still starts the\n  pod). Without this the Go code''s env var read would never see\n  anything but an empty string in-cluster, since Kubernetes only injects\n  env vars a Deployment''s pod spec explicitly asks for.\n\nhelm lint and `helm template ... | grep MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL` both\nverified locally before pushing.\n\nmake check, make check-all (coverage 97.9%, gate 90%; 25/25 BDD\nscenarios; arch-test) and make integration all pass.","tree":{"sha":"3cbff837db2a87153840065803a8b6169966a54d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/trees/3cbff837db2a87153840065803a8b6169966a54d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/commits/f6c2d2b887a988f4690b9770cb940c3102284f4d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3cbff837db2a87153840065803a8b6169966a54d\nparent 056be534573e7790bf68e297af6cab21663c1fe1\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790599744 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790599744 -0300\n\nfix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#115)\n\nProduction-blocking fleet-wide bug found during Phase 4 (k6/HPA\nload-test validation) cleanup: golang-migrate''s postgres driver takes\na session-scoped `pg_advisory_lock` to serialize concurrent migration\nruns at boot, but DATABASE_URL (warehouse-infra PR #43, PgBouncer\nrollout) points this service at PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode,\nwhich does not preserve session state across statements. Two or more\norder-management replicas starting concurrently (an HPA scale-out, or\nan ordinary rolling deploy with replicas>1) crash-loop with `pq:\nunnamed prepared statement does not exist` / `pq: canceling statement\ndue to statement timeout` for ~1-2 minutes until one wins the\nadvisory-lock race. Reproduced live.\n\ncmd/order/main.go and cmd/mcp/main.go (both run migrations at startup)\nnow read a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var for the migration step\nonly, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset:\n\n    migrationsDatabaseURL := getenv(\"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\", databaseURL)\n\nThe pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses\ndatabaseURL unchanged — every request this service serves keeps going\nthrough PgBouncer exactly as before. The fallback keeps local dev, CI\nintegration tests, and any environment that doesn''t provision the\nsplit working byte-identically to before this change.\n\nwarehouse-infra''s companion PR provisions MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL (a\ndirect, non-pooled DSN) as a new secret key alongside the existing\nDATABASE_URL key for all 9 OLTP services.\n\nAdds:\n- TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback: proves the getenv fallback in\n  both directions (falls back to DATABASE_URL when unset; uses\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, not DATABASE_URL, when set).\n- TestBuildRepoAdapters_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations:\n  proves buildRepoAdapters itself threads migrationsDatabaseURL into\n  the migration step (not databaseURL), using a schemeless\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL to get a distinctive parse error that a\n  dial/\"connection refused\" error against databaseURL could never\n  produce.\n- ADR-0029: documents the pg_advisory_lock / transaction-pooling\n  incompatibility, cross-references PgBouncer PR #43, and records the\n  live verification.\n- charts/order-management: a new `database.migrationsExistingSecretKey`\n  value (default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders a\n  MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var, sourced from the same existingSecret,\n  in both the api and mcp Deployments (`optional: true` on the\n  secretKeyRef so a secret that predates this key still starts the\n  pod). Without this the Go code''s env var read would never see\n  anything but an empty string in-cluster, since Kubernetes only injects\n  env vars a Deployment''s pod spec explicitly asks for.\n\nhelm lint and `helm template ... | grep MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL` both\nverified locally before pushing.\n\nmake check, make check-all (coverage 97.9%, gate 90%; 25/25 BDD\nscenarios; arch-test) and make integration all pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumJACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWv0QAJ3E5tapd+MzVmYef0EIgWyu\nEr8tOBIg8kiWlvzjyCtmoGyj+lFcE/8/lUJwiB4guPIdvlR1YNXxRmTrVI+HDwc4\nr5N0Xrz4m2tO1XVMv3j15MsCHtbrrNlXvM0Pi7o5eh7B3PfvOlnqqQOJsoo8/aoQ\naNgF0ZkZRGTbtzJzv6uWPtzGq9JdMS4reDCAQTupvWydrP6nHftxJMQlnuOnODh2\nJq6Hw6hT2rZHZnRC4kCniz7EUz9Q9k9tUJudeElgQLJLa7wrD+g/9F5jbD4X8LHf\n1U5r2VtwCLwHFoymYVSdZinxSAbG872IAt/Gd1zVmDGk2dvYbQmMriDE8UQghCv3\nqX8dt8IKo5CW3R8fUh8WXXTsqJTr+74FTwdTCMmZzKH1JMgYg92ZQDib9/erWxhh\nRDHgAc4i4rsZ4zawaRsVIzcfa64S7v2gZMF6hmwOfGqEIJ63VE36U3ZHNIkrwRxH\nzKBCifZIjzFNhJKnd8UO08MCNexlaE9OmKO3zTdC3etids5daelWyeh4zbbqd0Hp\nJC7/nRGKbqN85q933rQEm6sQ1C9Cl9vI9S7VAMFJG2G6zEl41Xwk9jHP0GRxw8/c\ncAqlEVHAAY8BDJLRbeM4n3dOfE63jmz0k4Bz6i0tm7BQJWVMwXnpYvJ73OhvQNIH\nC/SFds92mBwjZ6kIJGFo\n=fRtW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T12:49:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/order-management/commit/f6c2d2b887a988f4690b9770cb940c3102284f4d","node_id":"C_kwDOUDRODNoAKGY2YzJkMmI4ODdhOTg4ZjQ2OTBiOTc3MGNiOTQwYzMxMDIyODRmNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/order-management/commit/056be534573e7790bf68e297af6cab21663c1fe1","sha":"056be534573e7790bf68e297af6cab21663c1fe1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/056be534573e7790bf68e297af6cab21663c1fe1"}],"sha":"f6c2d2b887a988f4690b9770cb940c3102284f4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/f6c2d2b887a988f4690b9770cb940c3102284f4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/056be534573e7790bf68e297af6cab21663c1fe1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:19:04Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:19:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(inventory-storage): send Idempotency-Key on POST /reservations (ADR 0028) (#114)\n\ninventory-storage PR #98 required a caller-supplied Idempotency-Key\nheader on POST /reservations, but order-management''s outbound\nClient.Reserve was never updated to send one. Every real allocation\nattempt against a live cluster failed with 400\nidempotency-key-required, leaving every order line stuck Pending\nforever and tripping the inventory-storage circuit breaker\npermanently open -- reproduced with zero fault injection.\n\n- ports.ReservationRequest gains LineNo/Attempt (Attempt reuses the\n  Order aggregate''s existing optimistic-concurrency Version() from\n  ADR 0024 -- no new counter needed: stable within one allocation\n  pass, strictly greater on any later, independent pass.\n- Client.Reserve derives a deterministic\n  res-<orderId>-line-<lineNo>-att-<version> key and sends it as\n  Idempotency-Key on every POST /reservations call -- stable across a\n  retry of the same attempt, different for a genuinely new one,\n  matching inventory-storage''s documented replay contract (its own\n  idempotency.go, mirrored verbatim from this repo''s ADR 0023).\n- RevokeReservation is confirmed NOT idempotency-gated on the\n  inventory-storage side (DELETE /reservations/{id} is registered\n  plain in its server.go route table) -- documented in place, no\n  header added there.\n- Fleet-wide grep confirms order-management is the only caller of\n  POST /reservations, and no repo besides inventory-storage itself\n  calls POST /stock/receive (the other idempotency-gated route);\n  warehouse-ops-agent is read-only/GET-only per its own ADR.\n\nNew regression tests: header-presence assertion on the existing\nReserve request-shape test, plus\nTestReserveIdempotencyKeyIsStableAcrossRetryButDiffersAcrossLineOrAttempt\nproving the key is identical across a retry of the same attempt and\ndifferent across line/order/attempt.\n\nmake check, make check-all (97.9% coverage, gate 90%; arch-test; 25\nBDD scenarios) all green.\nEOF\n)","tree":{"sha":"f563aff9dc6c7b6f60c55b440deb8fb8039829e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/trees/f563aff9dc6c7b6f60c55b440deb8fb8039829e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/commits/056be534573e7790bf68e297af6cab21663c1fe1","verification":{"payload":"tree f563aff9dc6c7b6f60c55b440deb8fb8039829e3\nparent f1cfcf8d8dea7f1b7bc7750fc3b53389abe0433c\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790594344 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790594344 -0300\n\nfix(inventory-storage): send Idempotency-Key on POST /reservations (ADR 0028) (#114)\n\ninventory-storage PR #98 required a caller-supplied Idempotency-Key\nheader on POST /reservations, but order-management''s outbound\nClient.Reserve was never updated to send one. Every real allocation\nattempt against a live cluster failed with 400\nidempotency-key-required, leaving every order line stuck Pending\nforever and tripping the inventory-storage circuit breaker\npermanently open -- reproduced with zero fault injection.\n\n- ports.ReservationRequest gains LineNo/Attempt (Attempt reuses the\n  Order aggregate''s existing optimistic-concurrency Version() from\n  ADR 0024 -- no new counter needed: stable within one allocation\n  pass, strictly greater on any later, independent pass.\n- Client.Reserve derives a deterministic\n  res-<orderId>-line-<lineNo>-att-<version> key and sends it as\n  Idempotency-Key on every POST /reservations call -- stable across a\n  retry of the same attempt, different for a genuinely new one,\n  matching inventory-storage''s documented replay contract (its own\n  idempotency.go, mirrored verbatim from this repo''s ADR 0023).\n- RevokeReservation is confirmed NOT idempotency-gated on the\n  inventory-storage side (DELETE /reservations/{id} is registered\n  plain in its server.go route table) -- documented in place, no\n  header added there.\n- Fleet-wide grep confirms order-management is the only caller of\n  POST /reservations, and no repo besides inventory-storage itself\n  calls POST /stock/receive (the other idempotency-gated route);\n  warehouse-ops-agent is read-only/GET-only per its own ADR.\n\nNew regression tests: header-presence assertion on the existing\nReserve request-shape test, plus\nTestReserveIdempotencyKeyIsStableAcrossRetryButDiffersAcrossLineOrAttempt\nproving the key is identical across a retry of the same attempt and\ndifferent across line/order/attempt.\n\nmake check, make check-all (97.9% coverage, gate 90%; arch-test; 25\nBDD scenarios) all green.\nEOF\n)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquk0oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWWEQAGEjhRI+SNGo+zJ9ig21K+Wt\nzlY8UsMVMjoKbMUxdsIEH36EEu3cAa6KaQRMDAU3XHXHsxgnWgOXy0oPu3eQuOPB\nYRXEg5N8Mwn7l0koNdIfXZ3e4ffGg6ZqzCEtsDl+w5lgxk6lTew5UHP++mSJmnNf\ncN6GvrIuxjro8qGUQmUqHw6CtxSBhBmJdArRR1l9S8/NJRFjB0jH26U0tjXtX0hm\n1kCkLQa9PRaC8OlFQ4+h35EvCAq5R8KewBJ2tAzR+DrKc6tTapKAK1sFEC4C5KIz\nXon9J6DQMnaaX3pe0V84Qy0aGQzufWD8ij5i9dm6tot+7i0BvDIeQk4n0QLgYrI6\naShdIyRxcO/3VsQatpmrU2iel6wJ3SRHB71y/bUtUKsOnlI3jNCZsDaNlWiju3Bg\nVTFrPSXQOCQx+OrMkz6g4D3b2CLzWh3t4ZFQFYnPLNZgs