github.com/IQVO/order-management/commit/d65072f0914076703d11e333e5865bead84c4389","sha":"d65072f0914076703d11e333e5865bead84c4389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/d65072f0914076703d11e333e5865bead84c4389"}],"sha":"86ba34c1b39a37788d11cf28457fa742b6727627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/86ba34c1b39a37788d11cf28457fa742b6727627"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/commits/d65072f0914076703d11e333e5865bead84c4389/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:41:41Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:41:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resilience): per-dependency circuit breakers, read-only retry, Kafka DLQ, graceful shutdown (ADR 0025) (#107)\n\nPhase 2 of the fleet production-readiness plan, built on the already-merged\nPhase 0 (boot-retry) and Phase 1 (outbox, idempotency-key middleware,\noptimistic concurrency).\n\n- internal/resilience: shared gobreaker tuning (ReadyToTrip, timeouts) and\n  resilience.CallTimeout (derives each outbound call''s deadline from the\n  caller''s remaining context budget, capped at 30s).\n- inventorystorage.BreakerClient: wraps Reserve/RevokeReservation behind\n  one circuit breaker; OPEN state falls back to the existing fail-loud\n  PermissiveClient behaviour (reserving stock must never silently\n  \"succeed\"). No retry (Reserve is already idempotency-key-guarded;\n  RevokeReservation''s blind-retry safety is not yet proven).\n- productclassification.BreakerClient: wraps the read-only GET behind its\n  own, independent breaker; OPEN state falls back to the existing\n  fail-open PermissiveLookup behaviour. Adds jittered retry\n  (cenkalti/backoff/v4, up to 3 attempts) around a newly-split raw\n  fetch() call, so a 404 (a real answer) never consumes retry budget.\n- telemetry.CircuitBreakerMetrics: circuit_breaker_state{dependency=...}\n  OTel/Prometheus gauge on the existing global Meter.\n- RepromiseConsumer: in-process retry (3 attempts, jittered backoff) then\n  dead-letters an exhausted/poisoned message to <topic>.dlq with\n  x-dlq-source-topic/x-dlq-error/x-dlq-failed-at headers, committing the\n  offset so one bad message can never block its partition.\n  ErrConcurrentModification keeps its own pre-existing\n  leave-uncommitted-for-redelivery path, unaffected by this retry loop.\n- Graceful shutdown: readiness flips to not-ready FIRST (new GET\n  /readyz, distinct from the liveness-only /healthz), then HTTP drain,\n  then the outbox relay/RepromiseConsumer are stopped and awaited, then\n  the pg pool closes last. charts/order-management: readinessProbe now\n  targets /readyz; added terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30.\n- go.mod/go.sum: sony/gobreaker/v2 and cenkalti/backoff/v4 promoted to\n  direct dependencies.\n- docs/docs/adr/0025: full design record.\n\nVerification (worktree order-management-resilience):\n- go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration): clean\n- gofmt -l .: clean\n- make check (fmt-check, vet, build, lint, test -race): clean, 0 lint\n  issues (fixed one bodyclose nolint gap in breaker_test.go)\n- make arch-test: all hexagonal/analytics/ports fitness tests pass\n- make coverage: 97.9% (gate: 90%)\n- go test -tags=integration for every Kafka-touching package\n  (outbound/kafka, kafkacatalog, kafkacptschedule, kafkapathcapacity,\n  inbound/kafka), each against a real Testcontainers Kafka broker: all\n  pass, including the new\n  TestRepromiseConsumer_PoisonMessage_GoesToDeadLetterTopicWithoutBlockingPartition\n  (poison message reaches .dlq after 3 attempts with full payload/error\n  context; a well-formed message published right after it is processed\n  without delay)\n- apis/openapi.yaml unchanged by this branch -- no docs-api-drift\n  regeneration needed","tree":{"sha":"f7e431518735dfba5ce72b2acf89f72a980783ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/trees/f7e431518735dfba5ce72b2acf89f72a980783ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/order-management/git/commits/d65072f0914076703d11e333e5865bead84c4389","verification":{"payload":"tree f7e431518735dfba5ce72b2acf89f72a980783ea\nparent dc5757496bbf002421d7315d70315823e540b1df\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790538101 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790538101 -0300\n\nfeat(resilience): per-dependency circuit breakers, read-only retry, Kafka DLQ, graceful shutdown (ADR 0025) (#107)\n\nPhase 2 of the fleet production-readiness plan, built on the already-merged\nPhase 0 (boot-retry) and Phase 1 (outbox, idempotency-key middleware,\noptimistic concurrency).\n\n- internal/resilience: shared gobreaker tuning (ReadyToTrip, timeouts) and\n  resilience.CallTimeout (derives each outbound call''s deadline from the\n  caller''s remaining context budget, capped at 30s).\n- inventorystorage.BreakerClient: wraps Reserve/RevokeReservation behind\n  one circuit breaker; OPEN state falls back to the existing fail-loud\n  PermissiveClient behaviour (reserving stock must never silently\n  \"succeed\"). No retry (Reserve is already idempotency-key-guarded;\n  RevokeReservation''s blind-retry safety is not yet proven).\n- productclassification.BreakerClient: wraps the read-only GET behind its\n  own, independent breaker; OPEN state falls back to the existing\n  fail-open PermissiveLookup behaviour. Adds jittered retry\n  (cenkalti/backoff/v4, up to 3 attempts) around a newly-split raw\n  fetch() call, so a 404 (a real answer) never consumes retry budget.\n- telemetry.CircuitBreakerMetrics: circuit_breaker_state{dependency=...}\n  OTel/Prometheus gauge on the existing global Meter.\n- RepromiseConsumer: in-process retry (3 attempts, jittered backoff) then\n  dead-letters an exhausted/poisoned message to <topic>.dlq with\n  x-dlq-source-topic/x-dlq-error/x-dlq-failed-at headers, committing the\n  offset so one bad message can never block its partition.\n  ErrConcurrentModification keeps its own pre-existing\n  leave-uncommitted-for-redelivery path, unaffected by this retry loop.\n- Graceful shutdown: readiness flips to not-ready FIRST (new GET\n  /readyz, distinct from the liveness-only /healthz), then HTTP drain,\n  then the outbox relay/RepromiseConsumer are stopped and awaited, then\n  the pg pool closes last. charts/order-management: readinessProbe now\n  targets /readyz; added terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30.\n- go.mod/go.sum: sony/gobreaker/v2 and cenkalti/backoff/v4 promoted to\n  direct dependencies.\n- docs/docs/adr/0025: full design record.\n\nVerification (worktree order-management-resilience):\n- go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration): clean\n- gofmt -l .: clean\n- make check (fmt-check, vet, build, lint, test -race): clean, 0 lint\n  issues (fixed one bodyclose nolint gap in breaker_test.go)\n- make arch-test: all hexagonal/analytics/ports fitness tests pass\n- make coverage: 97.9% (gate: 90%)\n- go test -tags=integration for every Kafka-touching package\n  (outbound/kafka, kafkacatalog, kafkacptschedule, kafkapathcapacity,\n  inbound/kafka), each against a real Testcontainers Kafka broker: all\n  pass, including the new\n  TestRepromiseConsumer_PoisonMessage_GoesToDeadLetterTopicWithoutBlockingPartition\n  (poison message reaches .dlq after 3 attempts with full payload/error\n  context; a well-formed message published right after it is processed\n  without delay)\n- apis/openapi.yaml unchanged by this branch -- no docs-api-drift\n  regeneration needed","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquXF1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjUsQAJxs7EuYF4Ihm3jWZHf6ETAw\n+TzMAWGz3Z4U92IdxCaUCDhmmjH8/3rKzIauxia0RryVFTl/kWghHNYSfFbz4kZT\nmLZAZejnrQzv9aUJluhIZ/i2mUKzcs90tRyWzssxOQD22uPg1P6zqpWKjhmb1ZzO\nB6o8uLW3PKYmDcz9ELGoo6bCFzbQ1DaC9KEB/zzSm8hYcn+OIsAEUiUJ04430zwz\nqcZ+KUadqCJlC0+wTv2a3f4ftaZCvL2qlFJd2xpaxv6vmcxyflINYAXpMXY+7dZu\n8+39X5lWlRRUjToMCo/cn/qxHUxlPd1ir6b53iGVa986RQiW97+3ftqhFT9IxMmL\nk4C9UZFoyaewgppCTRoczGhjhFCk/4l0cfd1pCA/AnO6k5HxW0Rmq8sHCn+zHV8V\nsYKLYGUDKjgLeN+AEVBK8Xbx0SW80WrARDdugokGzmMNeOvT9d1Le2l/49/0zxZa\n3xv5AGGP674u8h+Gj9qyVzr8ttsfXXyZFLJdk25oDAF3Dv6xDYvzXGW0PThOQPfI\nsE80Y3fuvuqLm/WOlWDiJUwOmP2i3CZCjoue7x11W7CJql2EefklqJ6r2T+aQyN1\nWHeTWwwPx9wnu3NBFilMGTuYKRZxPouxoxHpiWTUylGjx1rz9X6lDs4Od0TSStI9\naXHUJ/Ju0nihWmB3X+6n\n=JxgG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T19:41:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/