t.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/ca03a9cae6d3017a0d294042b07998eb087bb562/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:48:56Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:48:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(postgres): add direct MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL secret key for all 9 OLTP services (#44)\n\nProduction-blocking bug found during Phase 4 load-test validation: every\nOLTP service''s golang-migrate postgres driver takes a session-scoped\n`SELECT pg_advisory_lock($1)` to serialize concurrent migration runs at\nboot, but DATABASE_URL (PR #43, PgBouncer rollout) points every OLTP\nservice at PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode, which does not support\nsession-scoped state. Two or more replicas of the same service starting\nconcurrently (an HPA scale-out, or an ordinary rolling deploy with\nreplicas>1) crash-loop with `pq: unnamed prepared statement does not\nexist` / `pq: canceling statement due to statement timeout` until one\nwins the advisory-lock race.\n\nAdds a second Secret key, MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, to all 9 OLTP\nservices'' existing `<service>-db` Secret (the 8 in local.services plus\nnetwork-fulfillment) — a direct, non-pooled Postgres connection string\n(same dbname/user/password as DATABASE_URL, host:port only) for use\nONLY by each service''s migration-runner step. DATABASE_URL itself is\ncompletely unchanged (still PgBouncer, still transaction pool_mode) —\nthis is purely additive and does not alter runtime traffic behavior at\nall. Mirrors the same \"migrations need a direct/session connection, app\ntraffic goes through the pooler\" split this repo already uses for\nanalytics_database_urls.\n\nApplied to the live kind-warehouse cluster and verified via\n`kubectl get secret <svc>-db -o jsonpath=''{.data}''` for all 9 services:\neach now carries both DATABASE_URL (unchanged, still pgbouncer:6432) and\nMIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL (new, postgres-postgresql:5432).\n\n`make check` passes (tf-fmt-check, tf-validate, helm-lint, shellcheck,\nchart-selector-check).\n\nReference implementation: order-management''s own PR wires\nMIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL into cmd/order/main.go''s migration-runner call\nsite and documents the fix in an ADR. The other 8 OLTP services'' Go-code\nfan-out to actually consume this key is a separate follow-up task —\nthis PR only provisions the secret key fleet-wide.","tree":{"sha":"7d0460ab81e31c2ce6b8a1a4bfbdfd5a7e710243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/7d0460ab81e31c2ce6b8a1a4bfbdfd5a7e710243"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/ca03a9cae6d3017a0d294042b07998eb087bb562","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d0460ab81e31c2ce6b8a1a4bfbdfd5a7e710243\nparent 6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790599736 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790599736 -0300\n\nfix(postgres): add direct MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL secret key for all 9 OLTP services (#44)\n\nProduction-blocking bug found during Phase 4 load-test validation: every\nOLTP service''s golang-migrate postgres driver takes a session-scoped\n`SELECT pg_advisory_lock($1)` to serialize concurrent migration runs at\nboot, but DATABASE_URL (PR #43, PgBouncer rollout) points every OLTP\nservice at PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode, which does not support\nsession-scoped state. Two or more replicas of the same service starting\nconcurrently (an HPA scale-out, or an ordinary rolling deploy with\nreplicas>1) crash-loop with `pq: unnamed prepared statement does not\nexist` / `pq: canceling statement due to statement timeout` until one\nwins the advisory-lock race.\n\nAdds a second Secret key, MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, to all 9 OLTP\nservices'' existing `<service>-db` Secret (the 8 in local.services plus\nnetwork-fulfillment) — a direct, non-pooled Postgres connection string\n(same dbname/user/password as DATABASE_URL, host:port only) for use\nONLY by each service''s migration-runner step. DATABASE_URL itself is\ncompletely unchanged (still PgBouncer, still transaction pool_mode) —\nthis is purely additive and does not alter runtime traffic behavior at\nall. Mirrors the same \"migrations need a direct/session connection, app\ntraffic goes through the pooler\" split this repo already uses for\nanalytics_database_urls.\n\nApplied to the live kind-warehouse cluster and verified via\n`kubectl get secret <svc>-db -o jsonpath=''{.data}''` for all 9 services:\neach now carries both DATABASE_URL (unchanged, still pgbouncer:6432) and\nMIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL (new, postgres-postgresql:5432).\n\n`make check` passes (tf-fmt-check, tf-validate, helm-lint, shellcheck,\nchart-selector-check).\n\nReference implementation: order-management''s own PR wires\nMIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL into cmd/order/main.go''s migration-runner call\nsite and documents the fix in an ADR. The other 8 OLTP services'' Go-code\nfan-out to actually consume this key is a separate follow-up task —\nthis PR only provisions the secret key fleet-wide.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumI4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASDUQAGtRS6CqLoboG41UwmRgtBvI\nY8MmljcpteE/d9JTJcEmk+v7KVwxkbuH5qIUZemcWi/cjZtFSbJFD63VkwKZ96Zk\n/nsoPPqyoIxhl/ClBlPGHVAWvXHsr5ZHFQgHxkJDNyb3IrF9IrXoAM6sTgDxjlyR\ndLnz2Ok5RH36cYvle0+SvBXFeME5rwfOgrIOGMuNlQ4f5QV4wCNmGejfUL6Equ49\nfWcmbEQUjCK3aJ+arRzMqHHnO0/i2iqp4e5Qntv+A4hmgzm/VpQIORzRjvv/mraR\nCLQWlEFNRt3lpA8cp+oN4FuiBW01oxN+m0Mxzfk/bJT5rm3DYbYJQBBOP+s+Um8P\nrCpSxygVnB1XsW1zbl36ZnAR56EACCp2e9sva7E9iKpgH7cVnc2UeOeQPpJIgOfg\nLApdIb6TAu9mWk81gr+aqT7Df5LnDJlLgDmns5zOeFbwnpC2udCcz1g1kdio4vJZ\noZOp3MTZlG+6TotOGTokoN4NBp0YDkX3A4An/HKQ8qUMT8Jr7WCUoSlzG1T3GltW\n+IJTLMSxXtLY1r0R9NuJiMhdw4fil+6tp+aPa78WA3kHAoa6pa+YJTrwSvAosDyt\n2IssnIawERhrTt6Kuf99mf3zsuScD9txfGetujz2qQWV2yQtkAI58OKlINyR2ILQ\ngpfbcILl7v2FXogK8lrx\n=fy1a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T12:48:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/ca03a9cae6d3017a0d294042b07998eb087bb562","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKGNhMDNhOWNhZTZkMzAxN2EwZDI5NDA0MmIwNzk5OGViMDg3YmI1NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9","sha":"6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9"}],"sha":"ca03a9cae6d3017a0d294042b07998eb087bb562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/ca03a9cae6d3017a0d294042b07998eb087bb562"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:09:47Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:09:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"infra(services): pull backend images from GHCR/Docker Hub, no local build (#36)\n\nRemove the local docker build + kind load supply chain\n(null_resource.build_and_load / scripts/build-and-load.sh /\nservice_source_hash content-addressed tags) for every backend service\nin local.services, plus warehouse-ops-agent and network-fulfillment.\n\nEvery backend repo''s own docker-publish CI job already pushes a\n:latest tag on merge to main (order-management, warehouse-ops-agent\nand network-fulfillment to GHCR; the other six services to Docker\nHub) -- so no CI change was needed anywhere. Terraform now sets\nimage.tag = \"latest\" with pullPolicy: Always, which is required for\n:latest to actually track the newest published image rather than\ncaching whatever the kubelet first resolved it to.\n\nFrontend MFE remotes and warehouse-console are explicitly OUT of\nscope here and keep their existing local build (content-addressed\nlocal-<hash> tag via build-and-load-frontend.sh) -- that stays a\nseparate follow-up.\n\nAlso removes the now-dead var.image_tag variable and updates\nCLAUDE.md/README.md to describe the new supply chain instead of the\nretired one.","tree":{"sha":"070f3602717fee58fdb8264701e48ffe5af7b970","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/070f3602717fee58fdb8264701e48ffe5af7b970"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9","verification":{"payload":"tree 070f3602717fee58fdb8264701e48ffe5af7b970\nparent 34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790590187 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790590187 -0300\n\ninfra(services): pull backend images from GHCR/Docker Hub, no local build (#36)\n\nRemove the local docker build + kind load supply chain\n(null_resource.build_and_load / scripts/build-and-load.sh /\nservice_source_hash content-addressed tags) for every backend service\nin local.services, plus warehouse-ops-agent and network-fulfillment.\n\nEvery backend repo''s own docker-publish CI job already pushes a\n:latest tag on merge to main (order-management, warehouse-ops-agent\nand network-fulfillment to GHCR; the other six services to Docker\nHub) -- so no CI change was needed anywhere. Terraform now sets\nimage.tag = \"latest\" with pullPolicy: Always, which is required for\n:latest to actually track the newest published image rather than\ncaching whatever the kubelet first resolved it to.\n\nFrontend MFE remotes and warehouse-console are explicitly OUT of\nscope here and keep their existing local build (content-addressed\nlocal-<hash> tag via build-and-load-frontend.sh) -- that stays a\nseparate follow-up.\n\nAlso removes the now-dead var.image_tag variable and updates\nCLAUDE.md/README.md to describe the new supply chain instead of the\nretired one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqujzrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0HIQALDJcUoTDnZYx/eRlPxV7Nv2\nS52Hmi0APA101yqJ849XTrOaB3V67ZGog3uAIZDCMA4U4Ad+MZZJuUcSfk5xzRIV\n6m+I0wl1pd87luee03e1wT8Y7cRFlLn5oJVx1/zLyiXxmgPJyWWY2vmID+aUGOzz\nRU0Ry/Y3cuweICI/s5VIALSH9GqP9L8u0e5OfkmicvoqxXh2Vur2GHy1/HSrSoJT\ny9d6wT8yJ4jWhmR/HhsgPn821F38c5IniHOMR33tlO0nIJ2rJ4VHE2QG84o60p8M\nyXkG4pBkF1oBpBCr5bRpg/eHIfpHrr5jqQRtsMo+wNfX9ljlkNiGywTUiYBenjIU\nKGUgzqadoiiPLorDAFeifRyn1drRdAIavQs72Tl1Rjc9VebDrnnXc7kW/eXLEW0q\nhPSCN0+q8DSCCNYRKjU1ARHEB9eGBbJB2hCm/wTnwl/PoE3of50JtgLAjyqb+Qyw\n5ztiuQJ0PFICfDGWMzFTovid971pfYWP7kysUnlYeI0+3oy2oSN+KhHt2cb47c7p\nxy5OJ6IN3Sa1hFEaW11b0O01feIE4vRmGj3e8IxBlWkWyvB9nJtMHyW+DZoz5vlM\n4pKWCkVasMmoRTG+RWAtyfopkoTu64KBHbHAK52fBSEd/h98R3UHM0eq39anSq6X\nV1LVH0j/5PNVXSI9MUMG\n=Tixs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T10:09:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDZjYTU4NmVmYjQyMGNkNWU0NjcxMzQxYjQ2Y2UzMTEzYTQ1MWNhYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8","sha":"34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8"}],"sha":"6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6ca586efb420cd5e4671341b46ce3113a451caa9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:00:42Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:00:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(terraform): add PgBouncer transaction pooling in front of shared Postgres (#43)\n\nPhase 3 scalability follow-up to order-management''s ADR-0026 (PR #110),\nwhich found order-management alone could reach ~80/100 of the shared\nPostgres server''s max_connections at its own HPA ceiling. Rolling the\nsame pgxpool.MaxConns tuning to the other 9 services would blow that\nshared 100-connection ceiling. The plan''s own Section 3.4 named the\nfallback for this: add PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- terraform/pgbouncer.tf: hand-rolled Deployment/Service/Secret for\n  bitnamilegacy/pgbouncer (no Bitnami OCI chart exists for pgbouncer --\n  verified 401 Unauthorized on oci://registry-1.docker.io/bitnamicharts/\n  pgbouncer -- so this follows frontends.tf''s existing chart-less\n  Deployment pattern, same convention already used for the Nginx web\n  gateway). Readiness/liveness/startup probes query PgBouncer''s own\n  admin console (SHOW POOLS), not a bare port-open check, matching the\n  fleet''s Phase-0 dial-reset-avoidance convention.\n- terraform/templates/pgbouncer.ini.tftpl,\n  pgbouncer-userlist.txt.tftpl: one [databases] entry per OLTP database\n  (the 8 in local.services plus network-fulfillment), pool_size=12 each,\n  pool_mode=transaction. ignore_startup_parameters=extra_float_digits\n  added after order-management''s migration step failed against PgBouncer\n  with \"unsupported startup parameter\" (lib/pq, used transitively by\n  golang-migrate, sends this; pgx/pgxpool itself does not).\n- terraform/locals.tf, network-fulfillment.tf: every OLTP DATABASE_URL\n  now points at pgbouncer.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local:6432 instead of\n  Postgres directly. Same dbname/user/password, only host:port changed --\n  transparent to every service''s pgxpool. Analytics DSNs are unchanged\n  and stay direct against Postgres (low-QPS, single long-lived consumer\n  per service; see the design doc for the full reasoning).\n- terraform/variables.tf: pgbouncer_image_tag variable, pinned to\n  bitnamilegacy/pgbouncer:1.24.1-debian-12-r10 (verified pullable).\n- docs/scalability/pgbouncer-connection-pooling.md: full design record,\n  including the fleet-wide session-level-feature audit (grepped all 10\n  service repos'' origin/develop for pg_advisory/LISTEN/NOTIFY -- zero\n  real hits, every outbox relay is polling-based, so transaction pooling\n  introduces no blocking incompatibility).\n\nPostgres''s own max_connections is left unmodified at 100, per the design\nintent: the fix lives entirely in PgBouncer''s pooling, not in raising the\nserver''s own ceiling.\n\nVerified end-to-end against order-management (already pgxpool-tuned):\nbooted clean through PgBouncer after the ignore_startup_parameters fix,\nreal POST /orders (write) and GET /orders/{id} (read) succeeded via its\nown HTTP API, PgBouncer''s SHOW STATS showed the corresponding pool\nactivity. PgBouncer pod-restart resilience tested directly (kubectl\ndelete pod): new pod came up on its own, order-management reconnected\nand completed another write with zero manual intervention. All remaining\n8 services rolled out against their re-pointed DATABASE_URL secrets and\nreport Running/Ready with SHOW POOLS confirming all 9 OLTP databases live\nin transaction mode.\n\nmake check passes (tf-fmt-check, tf-validate, helm-lint x10, shellcheck,\nchart-selector-check).","tree":{"sha":"19cf32095d0ca11023f8d2d67ce442d14ee0b632","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/19cf32095d0ca11023f8d2d67ce442d14ee0b632"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 19cf32095d0ca11023f8d2d67ce442d14ee0b632\nparent b742d08466f3210008c84bcc12ae1f304ffec304\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790564442 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790564442 -0300\n\nfeat(terraform): add PgBouncer transaction pooling in front of shared Postgres (#43)\n\nPhase 3 scalability follow-up to order-management''s ADR-0026 (PR #110),\nwhich found order-management alone could reach ~80/100 of the shared\nPostgres server''s max_connections at its own HPA ceiling. Rolling the\nsame pgxpool.MaxConns tuning to the other 9 services would blow that\nshared 100-connection ceiling. The plan''s own Section 3.4 named the\nfallback for this: add PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- terraform/pgbouncer.tf: hand-rolled Deployment/Service/Secret for\n  bitnamilegacy/pgbouncer (no Bitnami OCI chart exists for pgbouncer --\n  verified 401 Unauthorized on oci://registry-1.docker.io/bitnamicharts/\n  pgbouncer -- so this follows frontends.tf''s existing chart-less\n  Deployment pattern, same convention already used for the Nginx web\n  gateway). Readiness/liveness/startup probes query PgBouncer''s own\n  admin console (SHOW POOLS), not a bare port-open check, matching the\n  fleet''s Phase-0 dial-reset-avoidance convention.\n- terraform/templates/pgbouncer.ini.tftpl,\n  pgbouncer-userlist.txt.tftpl: one [databases] entry per OLTP database\n  (the 8 in local.services plus network-fulfillment), pool_size=12 each,\n  pool_mode=transaction. ignore_startup_parameters=extra_float_digits\n  added after order-management''s migration step failed against PgBouncer\n  with \"unsupported startup parameter\" (lib/pq, used transitively by\n  golang-migrate, sends this; pgx/pgxpool itself does not).\n- terraform/locals.tf, network-fulfillment.tf: every OLTP DATABASE_URL\n  now points at pgbouncer.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local:6432 instead of\n  Postgres directly. Same dbname/user/password, only host:port changed --\n  transparent to every service''s pgxpool. Analytics DSNs are unchanged\n  and stay direct against Postgres (low-QPS, single long-lived consumer\n  per service; see the design doc for the full reasoning).\n- terraform/variables.tf: pgbouncer_image_tag variable, pinned to\n  bitnamilegacy/pgbouncer:1.24.1-debian-12-r10 (verified pullable).\n- docs/scalability/pgbouncer-connection-pooling.md: full design record,\n  including the fleet-wide session-level-feature audit (grepped all 10\n  service repos'' origin/develop for pg_advisory/LISTEN/NOTIFY -- zero\n  real hits, every outbox relay is polling-based, so transaction pooling\n  introduces no blocking incompatibility).\n\nPostgres''s own max_connections is left unmodified at 100, per the design\nintent: the fix lives entirely in PgBouncer''s pooling, not in raising the\nserver''s own ceiling.\n\nVerified end-to-end against order-management (already pgxpool-tuned):\nbooted clean through PgBouncer after the ignore_startup_parameters fix,\nreal POST /orders (write) and GET /orders/{id} (read) succeeded via its\nown HTTP API, PgBouncer''s SHOW STATS showed the corresponding pool\nactivity. PgBouncer pod-restart resilience tested directly (kubectl\ndelete pod): new pod came up on its own, order-management reconnected\nand completed another write with zero manual intervention. All remaining\n8 services rolled out against their re-pointed DATABASE_URL secrets and\nreport Running/Ready with SHOW POOLS confirming all 9 OLTP databases live\nin transaction mode.\n\nmake check passes (tf-fmt-check, tf-validate, helm-lint x10, shellcheck,\nchart-selector-check).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqudhaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApC8QAJ2H3NFeEDmHUyi9LGyI9dE8\naJMrIcf+A6HkpbHouzQCHjFO3zaDOSHLcmTXhScqVuaDR1MSHIluuFma3FB72xMC\n0ITXNb3Tc+Dmk7K3Obe2RIS3Qz+qVR5rB1a59FJD9D2bITsGvzL77jwOPtQTLh6u\nshXKBZiBS60FEYYbr77jlYJUDNWDUhE+S/FQYgDcQ8QwOttgGKJk0WIu2nUvB7NH\nQ+pp5P6TWdAewW1xYInPITrMVpEbB7CkJ8zIqyiQVUbw1EPYZv+WKUvkpzT5101K\n5KGpfKL2ljLQ8IeFi2c1B1t/qG1K9w6Sxm5NJOPUTMKfXX3LCwIB9rZwqFt75Yln\n6hTHeYohdxK1QdSEVJ1ToJLnV5FwQcOP021fZrQJcKpJ/jvE4G6B2Ckngc+RGTkM\n/BWEcOXZhS6ei7psy6xXsSNd6vkynExnK2k6p4WZ0sBat+F4hpR0sJ8n4k2W0mGn\nJpS2ncF1Vkc41Elmrg6KL/OmPJBnodG9yjTCp/iDVaujydxix/ax/YpnF8klKqwd\nQPTmZzLPNjxRwyfer7ZWlB93l3HeBhHCalLJ2U6KWgiX/9D0g8ERZi4jb4sgRr00\n2lBoixKmVpw2bnGSBcocKEtlhiNsVcaYn4bpfRp/qWWCH0vl5zuE9B5tOSbnlDjr\nYkWDx48rb2EneeKv4Cjy\n=n7E/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:00:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDM0YTliZTBiNGM4ZWEyMTI4NWJlNDcwMTUzYjA1MjAyODM4YmE1ZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/b742d08466f3210008c84bcc12ae1f304ffec304","sha":"b742d08466f3210008c84bcc12ae1f304ffec304","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/b742d08466f3210008c84bcc12ae1f304ffec304"}],"sha":"34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/34a9be0b4c8ea21285be470153b05202838ba5e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/b742d08466f3210008c84bcc12ae1f304ffec304/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T00:47:22Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T00:47:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"infra(kafka): bump business topics from 1 to 8 partitions (#42)\n\nEvery active business Kafka topic (16 events/analytics topics across the\n10 bounded contexts, plus network-fulfillment.analytics) was provisioned\nwith 1 partition, capping horizontal consumer scaling at exactly one\nactive consumer per group regardless of replica count (WMS\nproduction-readiness plan section 3.2). __consumer_offsets (internal,\nalready 50 partitions) is untouched.\n\n- Bumped all 17 topics live via `kafka-topics.sh --alter --partitions 8`\n  against the broker directly (kafka-controller-0), not through\n  `terraform apply`: this repo has no kafka_topic/Mongey Terraform\n  resource, so the only Terraform-visible knob (the broker''s\n  num.partitions default) has zero effect on already-existing topics.\n  Partition count can only be increased in Kafka, never decreased, and\n  this alter path is exactly Kafka''s supported growth mechanism, not a\n  workaround — verified additive and safe (TopicId unchanged before and\n  after for all 17 topics, replication.factor unchanged at 1).\n- Set `overrideConfiguration.\"num.partitions\" = \"8\"` in\n  terraform/kafka.tf so a FUTURE auto-created topic (every service''s\n  writer sets AllowAutoTopicCreation: true) does not silently start at\n  Kafka''s own default of 1, and so `terraform plan` does not drift\n  against or fight the live cluster state.\n- Applied the Helm value scoped (`terraform apply\n  -target=helm_release.kafka[0]`) and re-verified: topics still show\n  8 partitions post-apply, `terraform plan` shows zero remaining\n  Kafka/topic diff, `make check` passes clean.\n- Verified live: every affected pod''s logs clean for ~90s post-alter (no\n  errors, no rebalance-storm, no group-coordinator errors); restart-count\n  diff across the fleet showed zero restarts from the live `--alter`\n  calls themselves. The subsequent Helm-value apply DID restart the\n  Kafka broker pod, which re-triggered the fleet''s already-documented,\n  pre-existing boot-time dial-reset bug (plan section 2.1) on a few\n  dependents (order-management, labor-performance, its projector) — each\n  recovered via its own retry/backoff within seconds; not a regression\n  from this change, and not new information (already tracked as an open\n  bug in the production-readiness plan).\n- Re-verified the fleet''s production consumer-group-id convention still\n  holds from actual consumer code (not assumed): every production\n  consumer uses ONE stable group name per logical service\n  (AnalyticsConsumerGroup constants, KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP env defaults\n  like \"labor-performance\"/\"fulfillment-execution\",\n  RepromiseConsumerGroup = \"order-management-repromise\"). Only the\n  read-only catalogue/facility-cache consumers\n  (kafkacatalog/facilitycache/kafkacptschedule/kafkapathcapacity — used\n  for local in-memory cache warm-up, not ordered business-event\n  consumption) intentionally use uniqueConsumerGroup() per-process, which\n  is correct for their use case and does not apply to production business\n  consumers.\n\nAlso audited every outbound Kafka producer in the fleet for\npartition-key-less (round-robin) publishing on an order-sensitive topic —\na latent bug the 1-partition topology was accidentally masking, which\nthis bump newly exposes. Findings documented in\ndocs/kafka-partition-scaleup.md: order-management''s integration\npublisher, inventory-storage''s integration publisher, and\nworkforce-management''s publisher all publish with no Key at all on their\nrespective .events topics. Every other producer in the fleet already\nkeys by the correct aggregate id. Not fixed here (cross-repo, out of\nscope for this infra-only change per task instructions) — flagged\nprecisely (file, line, topic) for follow-up per-repo fixes.","tree":{"sha":"56722f0dfd32b6563008abe5b1b1d2448e5b4bb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/56722f0dfd32b6563008abe5b1b1d2448e5b4bb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/b742d08466f3210008c84bcc12ae1f304ffec304","verification":{"payload":"tree 56722f0dfd32b6563008abe5b1b1d2448e5b4bb1\nparent 5be251c5a14711b290522d8b5cbb1ba6d98ed090\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790556442 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790556442 -0300\n\ninfra(kafka): bump business topics from 1 to 8 partitions (#42)\n\nEvery active business Kafka topic (16 events/analytics topics across the\n10 bounded contexts, plus network-fulfillment.analytics) was provisioned\nwith 1 partition, capping horizontal consumer scaling at exactly one\nactive consumer per group regardless of replica count (WMS\nproduction-readiness plan section 3.2). __consumer_offsets (internal,\nalready 50 partitions) is untouched.\n\n- Bumped all 17 topics live via `kafka-topics.sh --alter --partitions 8`\n  against the broker directly (kafka-controller-0), not through\n  `terraform apply`: this repo has no kafka_topic/Mongey Terraform\n  resource, so the only Terraform-visible knob (the broker''s\n  num.partitions default) has zero effect on already-existing topics.\n  Partition count can only be increased in Kafka, never decreased, and\n  this alter path is exactly Kafka''s supported growth mechanism, not a\n  workaround — verified additive and safe (TopicId unchanged before and\n  after for all 17 topics, replication.factor unchanged at 1).\n- Set `overrideConfiguration.\"num.partitions\" = \"8\"` in\n  terraform/kafka.tf so a FUTURE auto-created topic (every service''s\n  writer sets AllowAutoTopicCreation: true) does not silently start at\n  Kafka''s own default of 1, and so `terraform plan` does not drift\n  against or fight the live cluster state.\n- Applied the Helm value scoped (`terraform apply\n  -target=helm_release.kafka[0]`) and re-verified: topics still show\n  8 partitions post-apply, `terraform plan` shows zero remaining\n  Kafka/topic diff, `make check` passes clean.\n- Verified live: every affected pod''s logs clean for ~90s post-alter (no\n  errors, no rebalance-storm, no group-coordinator errors); restart-count\n  diff across the fleet showed zero restarts from the live `--alter`\n  calls themselves. The subsequent Helm-value apply DID restart the\n  Kafka broker pod, which re-triggered the fleet''s already-documented,\n  pre-existing boot-time dial-reset bug (plan section 2.1) on a few\n  dependents (order-management, labor-performance, its projector) — each\n  recovered via its own retry/backoff within seconds; not a regression\n  from this change, and not new information (already tracked as an open\n  bug in the production-readiness plan).\n- Re-verified the fleet''s production consumer-group-id convention still\n  holds from actual consumer code (not assumed): every production\n  consumer uses ONE stable group name per logical service\n  (AnalyticsConsumerGroup constants, KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP env defaults\n  like \"labor-performance\"/\"fulfillment-execution\",\n  RepromiseConsumerGroup = \"order-management-repromise\"). Only the\n  read-only catalogue/facility-cache consumers\n  (kafkacatalog/facilitycache/kafkacptschedule/kafkapathcapacity — used\n  for local in-memory cache warm-up, not ordered business-event\n  consumption) intentionally use uniqueConsumerGroup() per-process, which\n  is correct for their use case and does not apply to production business\n  consumers.\n\nAlso audited every outbound Kafka producer in the fleet for\npartition-key-less (round-robin) publishing on an order-sensitive topic —\na latent bug the 1-partition topology was accidentally masking, which\nthis bump newly exposes. Findings documented in\ndocs/kafka-partition-scaleup.md: order-management''s integration\npublisher, inventory-storage''s integration publisher, and\nworkforce-management''s publisher all publish with no Key at all on their\nrespective .events topics. Every other producer in the fleet already\nkeys by the correct aggregate id. Not fixed here (cross-repo, out of\nscope for this infra-only change per task instructions) — flagged\nprecisely (file, line, topic) for follow-up per-repo fixes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqubkaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8zIQAEgeI67q/hpGjL2czLL1ABg8\n9uO3OZxNjD+e+udTHTzRM78hj2jVQj1EAtWPq074rJthg/sFw3mleE3FvxUw2O4v\n36Cajhjx6hg112q06LUM66pz3uGUj1Eq9