,"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/fc90a86b0abb21cd33ebc4590b068a8a98114e15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:28:25Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:28:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: network-fulfillment infra parity (mcp/analytics/frontend) + reports-routing gap closure for all 9 contexts (#40)\n\n* feat(network-fulfillment): mcp, analytics, and frontend infra parity\n\nMirrors the shared local.services-driven wiring services.tf/frontends.tf/\nmcp.tf already do for the other 8 contexts, hand-rolled in\nnetwork-fulfillment.tf''s own locals merge since network-fulfillment is\ndeliberately not in local.services (see that file''s header).\n\n- mcp.tf: add \"network-fulfillment\" to mcp_services (safe: the\n  mcp_endpoint for-comprehension only needs the name string, never\n  indexes into local.services).\n- network-fulfillment.tf: add mcp.enabled (reusing the shared\n  var.deploy_mcp_servers), frontend.enabled (reusing\n  local.frontend_remotes/local.frontend_source_hash), and a hand-rolled\n  analytics database (own random_password, db/user locals,\n  kubernetes_secret, DSN local) mirroring the OLTP database block\n  exactly -- NOT joined to local.analytics_services, which would KeyError\n  via analytics_db_info''s local.services[name] lookup.\n- postgres.tf: merge network-fulfillment''s analytics db into the\n  init-databases template feed, the same \"merged in rather than a second\n  loop\" pattern the OLTP services map two blocks above already uses for\n  this same context.\n- frontends.tf: add network-fulfillment to local.frontend_remotes\n  (netfulfil_mfe, confirmed from PR#16''s web/vite.config.ts).\n\nReal values (not assumed) confirmed by reading PR#16/#18''s actual branch\ncontent before writing this:\n  - netfulfil-reports HTTP_ADDR default :8092, router registers\n    GET /reports/acknowledgement (reports_handler.go).\n  - chart''s analytics.database has a single existingSecret/url pair (NOT\n    facility-layout''s projectorUrl/reportsUrl split) -- both\n    netfulfil-projector and netfulfil-reports read one\n    ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL key.\n  - analytics.reports.service.port: 80 (values.yaml).\n  - mcp.service.port: 8090, matching every sibling.\n  - web/ directory tree at network-fulfillment/web/... exactly like every\n    sibling remote.\n\nInherits the same ''***'' password-interpolation characteristic\nlocal.network_fulfillment_database_url (OLTP) already has, deliberately,\nto avoid introducing a new inconsistency -- see this change''s PR\ndescription for the separate, pre-existing masking-bug finding this does\nNOT fix.\n\n* feat(routing): close the reports-routing gap for all 9 contexts\n\nwarehouse-console#43''s own author flagged an unresolved gap: every\nanalytics-enabled bounded context already ships a reports\nDeployment+Service in its chart, but no Kong Ingress or Gateway API\nHTTPRoute anywhere in this repo routes to it -- confirmed by reading\nservices.tf''s existing ingress/gatewayApi blocks, which route ONLY to the\nmain OLTP Service.\n\nAdds a SECOND Terraform-rendered Ingress/HTTPRoute per analytics-enabled\ncontext at `${var.api_path_prefix}/<context>/reports`, pointing at that\ncontext''s own `<context>-reports` Service (chart''s\nanalytics.reports.service.port, confirmed 80 across all 8 charts''\nvalues.yaml). Mechanism picked PER CONTEXT via the same\ncontains(local.gateway_api_pilot_services, name) membership check the\nmain-API route already uses, not a blanket assumption.\n\nStrips ${var.api_path_prefix}/<context>/reports down to /reports (one\nsegment longer than the main route''s strip to /), matching every\nsibling''s reports_handler.go NewReportsRouter, which registers\nGET /reports/<report-name>, verified across all 8 repos.\n\nRendered directly in Terraform (kubernetes_ingress_v1 for the Ingress\ncase; a null_resource + kubectl apply for the HTTPRoute case, mirroring\ngateway-api.tf''s own null_resource.gateway_api_crds/gateway_class/gateway\npattern and its documented reason: kubernetes_manifest needs the CRD''s\nschema at plan time, which does not exist yet on a from-scratch apply\nthat installs the CRDs and a resource using them in the same run) rather\nthan a new chart template in each of the 8 repos -- matches this repo''s\nown stated \"warehouse-infra contributes only the environment\"\nphilosophy (services.tf''s header) and avoids an 8-repo fan-out for a\nrouting decision.\n\nnetwork-fulfillment''s own reports route is wired directly in\nnetwork-fulfillment.tf (separate commit), matching whichever mechanism\nits existing OLTP route already uses in that same file.","tree":{"sha":"33d1291a0476c5e255b99ab5c9205182cd8b5cb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/33d1291a0476c5e255b99ab5c9205182cd8b5cb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/fc90a86b0abb21cd33ebc4590b068a8a98114e15","verification":{"payload":"tree 33d1291a0476c5e255b99ab5c9205182cd8b5cb2\nparent 1e9bf3e408ab4eaf2d8d6aac282582d0a1445bc3\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790