ts.service.port: 80 (values.yaml).\n  - mcp.service.port: 8090, matching every sibling.\n  - web/ directory tree at network-fulfillment/web/... exactly like every\n    sibling remote.\n\nInherits the same ''***'' password-interpolation characteristic\nlocal.network_fulfillment_database_url (OLTP) already has, deliberately,\nto avoid introducing a new inconsistency -- see this change''s PR\ndescription for the separate, pre-existing masking-bug finding this does\nNOT fix.\n\n* feat(routing): close the reports-routing gap for all 9 contexts\n\nwarehouse-console#43''s own author flagged an unresolved gap: every\nanalytics-enabled bounded context already ships a reports\nDeployment+Service in its chart, but no Kong Ingress or Gateway API\nHTTPRoute anywhere in this repo routes to it -- confirmed by reading\nservices.tf''s existing ingress/gatewayApi blocks, which route ONLY to the\nmain OLTP Service.\n\nAdds a SECOND Terraform-rendered Ingress/HTTPRoute per analytics-enabled\ncontext at `${var.api_path_prefix}/<context>/reports`, pointing at that\ncontext''s own `<context>-reports` Service (chart''s\nanalytics.reports.service.port, confirmed 80 across all 8 charts''\nvalues.yaml). Mechanism picked PER CONTEXT via the same\ncontains(local.gateway_api_pilot_services, name) membership check the\nmain-API route already uses, not a blanket assumption.\n\nStrips ${var.api_path_prefix}/<context>/reports down to /reports (one\nsegment longer than the main route''s strip to /), matching every\nsibling''s reports_handler.go NewReportsRouter, which registers\nGET /reports/<report-name>, verified across all 8 repos.\n\nRendered directly in Terraform (kubernetes_ingress_v1 for the Ingress\ncase; a null_resource + kubectl apply for the HTTPRoute case, mirroring\ngateway-api.tf''s own null_resource.gateway_api_crds/gateway_class/gateway\npattern and its documented reason: kubernetes_manifest needs the CRD''s\nschema at plan time, which does not exist yet on a from-scratch apply\nthat installs the CRDs and a resource using them in the same run) rather\nthan a new chart template in each of the 8 repos -- matches this repo''s\nown stated \"warehouse-infra contributes only the environment\"\nphilosophy (services.tf''s header) and avoids an 8-repo fan-out for a\nrouting decision.\n\nnetwork-fulfillment''s own reports route is wired directly in\nnetwork-fulfillment.tf (separate commit), matching whichever mechanism\nits existing OLTP route already uses in that same file.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquEcJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATqkQAIt5cAeNCPfj7O7mEe29vCd5\nOEZlW1qJ1zRmuoWRc9l0Z/6gTuroeheI5t76Id6AC8l+byAWHTmm/79xMwmgoy+Q\nxsSK/aAGGfYONMgymJuiAuxDwmTyCdmIM2+eo7DWdVnxrLsa4dIQdeYOq87A5hRN\nlRIy4MaZc7mW5MhNaI5SH2VZdYXX5zHNPBjO3s6B6+ydddNEqj8Qvxjfzf35upd9\n3S+jRV1eDvEm2mCJEPXIq6eG8BbbLxeYYzjtM6yTnl1ePZiWK6ogb7FRpDEjr6XH\nZcXpGsssIt1MK4gGVmo5D/UD3v8OPy6wtwvzGC4OxucIRNmUVIBS/bTOwLVe/2dJ\n+z1QuzYUZ9Mtsl6GQQsbyo2BJqSGzGzCP4X+qmlKfmHvacwqZCo4CuXVvFmqJzTY\nCuUv6K6GQUNeJgndE70ju5y4UCGW913jm/92XBiMc2ENz6LcXKAiayiYqWH/4Yy4\n+bPn8L/+hborDZvJW6PUZyg/h33ORDe8SffcRG0a9Iw+IFDsfqCt2qdjA/5VdShH\nm4c2Tpeq5x28YFVTUIQAlo342GtkcBz8a3MDJZVTRtoMCMOQK3OmwWzFnZF77id3\nVGtawqdk9tkTKIVunDKFF6lsMyjLQdbI32Y4rPUTWCOjk2OfvAMtREOWittKPhhL\nbuzkUpT7Tshg2gvgthra\n=ZRvk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:28:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/fc90a86b0abb21cd33ebc4590b068a8a98114e15","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKGZjOTBhODZiMGFiYjIxY2QzM2ViYzQ1OTBiMDY4YThhOTgxMTRlMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/1e9bf3e408ab4eaf2d8d6aac282582d0a1445bc3","sha":"1e9bf3e408ab4eaf2d8d6aac282582d0a1445bc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/1e9bf3e408ab4eaf2d8d6aac282582d0a1445bc3"}],"sha":"fc90a86b0abb21cd33ebc4590b068a8a98114e15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/fc90a86b0abb21cd33ebc4590b068a8a98114e15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/1e9bf3e408ab4eaf2d8d6aac282582d0a1445bc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:04:14Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:04:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"infra: wire ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret for warehouse-ops-agent (LLM_MODE=shadow) (#39)\n\nWires warehouse-ops-agent''s ADR-0004 model-backed Reasoner for real cluster\nuse, per the user''s 2026-09-26 decision: LLM_MODE=shadow (runs the LLM\nreasoner alongside the deterministic policy, never acts on the model''s\noutput alone).\n\n- terraform/variables.tf: new `anthropic_api_key` variable (string,\n  sensitive = true, default = \"\" — never a real value). Supplied\n  out-of-band only (TF_VAR_anthropic_api_key or a gitignored\n  terraform.tfvars).\n- terraform/ops-agent.tf:\n  - kubernetes_secret.ops_agent_anthropic creates the\n    \"warehouse-ops-agent-anthropic\" Secret from var.anthropic_api_key,\n    mirroring postgres.tf''s kubernetes_secret.service_db /\n    network-fulfillment.tf''s kubernetes_secret.network_fulfillment_db\n    generated-Secret pattern (never a plaintext value inside the ArgoCD\n    Application CR''s helm.valuesObject).\n  - ops_agent_helm_values now sets credentials.existingSecret to that\n    Secret''s name and llm.mode = \"shadow\" (the chart already supports\n    both — verified against warehouse-ops-agent''s charts/warehouse-ops-agent\n    values.yaml/secret.yaml/deployment.yaml on origin/develop).\n  - a `check` block warns at plan/apply time if LLM_MODE is not \"off\" and\n    the key is empty, without failing validate/plan/apply. Confirmed\n    ADR-0004''s actual cluster-side enforcement is in\n    cmd/agent/reasoner.go: a non-off LLM_MODE with an empty\n    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is already a hard startup error there\n    (CrashLoopBackOff), so this check is purely earlier visibility, not a\n    new gate.\n- terraform/argocd-apps.tf: ops_agent_application now depends_on the new\n  Secret.\n- terraform/terraform.tfvars.example + README.md: documents how to supply\n  the real key locally without committing it.\n\nVerified: `make check` (terraform fmt/validate, helm-lint, shellcheck,\nchart-selector-check) passes with var.anthropic_api_key left at its empty\ndefault. A targeted `terraform plan` against the real cluster state shows\nthe Secret being created and the check-block warning firing as designed\n(non-fatal). No `terraform apply` was run.\n\nThe user must supply the real ANTHROPIC_API_KEY value themselves before\napplying — see README.md''s new \"Secrets you must supply yourself\" section.","tree":{"sha":"b8b909440a11546a9bfced7086c7a20f69d85774","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/b8b909440a11546a9bfced7086c7a20f69d85774"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/1e9bf3e408ab4eaf2d8d6aac282582d0a1445bc3","verification":{"payload":"tree b8b909440a11546a9bfced7086c7a20f69d85774\nparent 4e96305ce60d2dcd470eb2d6cdf19062edbc1f98\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790435054 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790435054 -0300\n\ninfra: wire ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret for warehouse-ops-agent (LLM_MODE=shadow) (#39)\n\nWires warehouse-ops-agent''s ADR-0004 model-backed Reasoner for real cluster\nuse, per the user''s 2026-09-26 decision: LLM_MODE=shadow (runs the LLM\nreasoner alongside the deterministic policy, never acts on the model''s\noutput alone).\n\n- terraform/variables.tf: new `anthropic_api_key` variable (string,\n  sensitive = true, default = \"\" — never a real value). Supplied\n  out-of-band only (TF_VAR_anthropic_api_key or a gitignored\n  terraform.tfvars).\n- terraform/ops-agent.tf:\n  - kubernetes_secret.ops_agent_anthropic creates the\n    \"warehouse-ops-agent-anthropic\" Secret from var.anthropic_api_key,\n    mirroring postgres.tf''s kubernetes_secret.service_db /\n    network-fulfillment.tf''s kubernetes_secret.network_fulfillment_db\n    generated-Secret pattern (never a plaintext value inside the ArgoCD\n    Application CR''s helm.valuesObject).\n  - ops_agent_helm_values now sets credentials.existingSecret to that\n    Secret''s name and llm.mode = \"shadow\" (the chart already supports\n    both — verified against warehouse-ops-agent''s charts/warehouse-ops-agent\n    values.yaml/secret.yaml/deployment.yaml on origin/develop).\n  - a `check` block warns at plan/apply time if LLM_MODE is not \"off\" and\n    the key is empty, without failing validate/plan/apply. Confirmed\n    ADR-0004''s actual cluster-side enforcement is in\n    cmd/agent/reasoner.go: a non-off LLM_MODE with an empty\n    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is already a hard startup error there\n    (CrashLoopBackOff), so this check is purely earlier visibility, not a\n    new gate.\n- terraform/argocd-apps.tf: ops_agent_application now depends_on the new\n  Secret.\n- terraform/terraform.tfvars.example + README.md: documents how to supply\n  the real key locally without committing it.\n\nVerified: `make check` (terraform fmt/validate, helm-lint, shellcheck,\nchart-selector-check) passes with var.anthropic_api_key left at its empty\ndefault. A targeted `terraform plan` against the real cluster state shows\nthe Secret being created and the check-block warning firing as designed\n(non-fatal). No `terraform apply` was run.\n\nThe user must supply the real ANTHROPIC_API_KEY value themselves before\napplying — see README.md''s new \"Secrets you must supply yourself\" section.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt97uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc0QQADIzVdekec8uRaMkxbj5sH16\nlQ3BK1w7G0z65Rk5a2UsbgE9WzXE19hLisWM+8gdOsIPL9pNmW32xz2T+UnGGAKx\n43QCjAZZ6j9HQDL/hXVSJtykCoHzWu1K5SxIX1yBhf285ZhHH6zi3fU3+uKR1CwD\nY7pVFNnUXWHGjgZSdGxiQIhmRc0Qage49NTGseOI5DL1aCwD1FhftZoiXnHmLNig\nrwfx1VV4fdbOY+8RR20iWae0anemsdt7qDRv5QDYwh6DbASLpERED/V8ElKBmZ3j\n0Mlr5OeA6kSRAlSQAovw7KDHC3YCGdutru8dZyrnjWPGXkAvsoDcIgvsU25CvjB5\