"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/4e96305ce60d2dcd470eb2d6cdf19062edbc1f98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:00:05Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:00:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: enable Postgres/Kafka persistence by default, deploy metrics-server (#38)\n\nTurns Postgres and Kafka persistence ON by default (user decision,\n2026-09-26: data durability across pod/node restarts is now preferred\nover the old reproducible-from-any-state disposability) and adds a\nmetrics-server deployment so the HPA templates already shipped in every\nservice chart actually work.\n\n- terraform/variables.tf: postgres_persistence_enabled and\n  kafka_persistence_enabled now default to true; descriptions updated\n  with the new reasoning and the initdb-never-reruns tradeoff this flip\n  reintroduces for any future new logical database.\n- terraform/postgres.tf, terraform/kafka.tf: added an explicit small PVC\n  size (3Gi, vs. the charts'' own 8Gi default) sized for a laptop kind\n  cluster, with a comment explaining why.\n- terraform/metrics-server.tf (new): helm_release.metrics_server,\n  gated behind new var.deploy_metrics_server (default true), installing\n  kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server into kube-system with\n  --kubelet-insecure-tls set (kind''s kubelet serving certs aren''t\n  CA-signed, so metrics-server can''t scrape without it -- verified by\n  rendering the chart and confirming the flag lands in the container''s\n  args alongside the chart''s own defaultArgs).\n- terraform/outputs.tf: added metrics_server_enabled output, following\n  the existing \"platform components\" output pattern.\n- README.md: updated the persistence prose (no longer describes the old\n  false/emptyDir default), added a metrics-server section describing\n  what it fixes and how to verify it.\n\nValidated locally: `make check` (terraform fmt -check, terraform\nvalidate, helm lint on all 10 charts, chart-selector-check, shellcheck)\npasses. Also independently rendered the metrics-server chart with these\nexact values via `helm template` to confirm --kubelet-insecure-tls is\nappended to (not replacing) the chart''s defaultArgs.\n\nNOT RUN: terraform apply. This PR is Terraform-only; the change has not\nbeen applied to the live ''warehouse'' kind cluster. That is a separate,\nhigh-blast-radius step (touches every running pod: Postgres and Kafka\nrelease recreation, plus a new cluster-scoped resource) to be run\ndeliberately after review, not part of this PR.","tree":{"sha":"9770f3d7994a0bb87db1667ed9f884788829cdc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/9770f3d7994a0bb87db1667ed9f884788829cdc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/4e96305ce60d2dcd470eb2d6cdf19062edbc1f98","verification":{"payload":"tree 9770f3d7994a0bb87db1667ed9f884788829cdc9\nparent 1955636881010c1067d7d61aee3fff38efb26414\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790434805 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790434805 -0300\n\nfeat: enable Postgres/Kafka persistence by default, deploy metrics-server (#38)\n\nTurns Postgres and Kafka persistence ON by default (user decision,\n2026-09-26: data durability across pod/node restarts is now preferred\nover the old reproducible-from-any-state disposability) and adds a\nmetrics-server deployment so the HPA templates already shipped in every\nservice chart actually work.\n\n- terraform/variables.tf: postgres_persistence_enabled and\n  kafka_persistence_enabled now default to true; descriptions updated\n  with the new reasoning and the initdb-never-reruns tradeoff this flip\n  reintroduces for any future new logical database.\n- terraform/postgres.tf, terraform/kafka.tf: added an explicit small PVC\n  size (3Gi, vs. the charts'' own 8Gi default) sized for a laptop kind\n  cluster, with a comment explaining why.\n- terraform/metrics-server.tf (new): helm_release.metrics_server,\n  gated behind new var.deploy_metrics_server (default true), installing\n  kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server into kube-system with\n  --kubelet-insecure-tls set (kind''s kubelet serving certs aren''t\n  CA-signed, so metrics-server can''t scrape without it -- verified by\n  rendering the chart and confirming the flag lands in the container''s\n  args alongside the chart''s own defaultArgs).\n- terraform/outputs.tf: added metrics_server_enabled output, following\n  the existing \"platform components\" output pattern.\n- README.md: updated the persistence prose (no longer describes the old\n  false/emptyDir default), added a metrics-server section describing\n  what it fixes and how to verify it.\n\nValidated locally: `make check` (terraform fmt -check, terraform\nvalidate, helm lint on all 10 charts, chart-selector-check, shellcheck)\npasses. Also independently rendered the metrics-server chart with these\nexact values via `helm template` to confirm --kubelet-insecure-tls is\nappended to (not replacing) the chart''s defaultArgs.\n\nNOT RUN: terraform apply. This PR is Terraform-only; the change has not\nbeen applied to the live ''warehouse'' kind cluster. That is a separate,\nhigh-blast-radius step (touches every running pod: Postgres and Kafka\nrelease recreation, plus a new cluster-scoped resource) to be run\ndeliberately after review, not part of this PR.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt931CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARHgQAFRMZBVRW5r9Au61tfBIQE1e\nwhEMKO6hFMxYqAgB+uinXjNkLG5grHNyrAPsyFuY5YAxX8RtTB96gZ0H2L5UTlCY\n1OwhJ3SCp67EqNIOvOL7nFvFmw2tu9RB8wNMsI01v3VIOju3T+6Df9+vSf469OeF\npVvgo0v0HCwIz9cd816YP9f5ObOwAeJIVPv3thcdkdBHdWf7DoJIcTzDJOdtV44s\nSQ+GDd+wsjYwulDvzMuzxnYmmEYVC+JDVo0TPABgDTZToD0d9zzlJg2mJ9A6FVIH\nDwJnjItLJkEcd62AShUe41mjVCDMB1lkZbSLp2euLyskYsrL0BGrfC1mKFFM3zWZ\nDS/rl09LIyq4czXSbo8YJsQDY9ZAggRazVTufbvYK4SY7N7haghqJO1R/BheBi5d\nHalewJAdiNsSUbZEiFF2x+fZhPFU7axkZNcnvfaKHvaDoHPY8CwtuFJC2F38qdeC\nDVMKwwS1Ty0I7lm/0Hvm4qhWRoAcIsQ2y7M568B6nPwpGOxuEl7HlGT1il3DbmOl\nVDRcoAcfgedFnOysS0y0KF2yIJuu5aEfJfSeGYL7UsQ3u0McqPwijIZ3E0m6daDo\nLI99trlDyGa0Zi6RrPVD2jZ9eo6IuYTEhx4luSm7Dgh6/7dvp1ABagIhGHvhSenS\nypXM+OFkBNVGAaKc/une\n=aFiI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T15:00:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://ap