b.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/ea23994e6efd86093a568de92f74155bfcd563af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T02:29:34Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T02:29:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(network-fulfillment): wire the inbound leg in the local cluster (#35)\n\nnetwork-fulfillment#6 added the poller and the curated ACL files; this\nconfigures them for the kind cluster.\n\n- pollInterval 1m: the ONLY thing that brings demand into this context\n  (inbound is a poll and nothing else, ADR 0001 section 5), kept far below\n  the 24h acknowledgement window because a stopped poller spends a deadline\n  the network set.\n\n- productTranslation: two mappings using SKUs this cluster already knows.\n  NOT optional decoration -- with an empty dictionary every order is\n  rejected as untranslatable, and the symptom is invisible because refusing\n  unknown products is also correct behaviour. Found by running the poller\n  for real, not by reading the code.\n\n- stubDemand: one order, so the inbound leg is OBSERVABLE here. Without it\n  the poller runs correctly forever against a network with nothing to give\n  it, which is indistinguishable from a broken poller. Relative deadline\n  (\"+36h\") because a fixed instant goes stale and makes every order\n  instantly infeasible.\n\nVerified live after network-fulfillment#7 (which fixed the CrashLoopBackOff\nthis deployment exposed):\n- pod 2/2 Running, 0 restarts\n- poller: polls=2 received=1 failed=0, watermark advancing\n- the ACL translated ASIN-LOCAL-1 -> sku-1\n- a real NetworkOrder is persisted and readable through Kong at\n  /api/network-fulfillment/network-orders/po-local-1\n- it SURVIVES a rollout restart with receivedAt and acknowledgeBy\n  unchanged, which is the whole point of the Postgres work in #5\n- 11 ArgoCD apps Synced/Healthy, 0 non-Running pods fleet-wide\n\nThe order reads REJECTED, and that is correct rather than a failure:\norder-management answered not-feasible for a deadline it cannot meet with\nno inventory seeded, so this context refused inside the window instead of\ncommitting to a shipment it could not make. That verdict crossing both\ncontexts is the integration working.\n\nterraform validate clean, fmt clean.","tree":{"sha":"aa36913c84e8545d5d1c1576984c209be48284e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/aa36913c84e8545d5d1c1576984c209be48284e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/ea23994e6efd86093a568de92f74155bfcd563af","verification":{"payload":"tree aa36913c84e8545d5d1c1576984c209be48284e1\nparent 33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790216974 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790216974 -0300\n\nfeat(network-fulfillment): wire the inbound leg in the local cluster (#35)\n\nnetwork-fulfillment#6 added the poller and the curated ACL files; this\nconfigures them for the kind cluster.\n\n- pollInterval 1m: the ONLY thing that brings demand into this context\n  (inbound is a poll and nothing else, ADR 0001 section 5), kept far below\n  the 24h acknowledgement window because a stopped poller spends a deadline\n  the network set.\n\n- productTranslation: two mappings using SKUs this cluster already knows.\n  NOT optional decoration -- with an empty dictionary every order is\n  rejected as untranslatable, and the symptom is invisible because refusing\n  unknown products is also correct behaviour. Found by running the poller\n  for real, not by reading the code.\n\n- stubDemand: one order, so the inbound leg is OBSERVABLE here. Without it\n  the poller runs correctly forever against a network with nothing to give\n  it, which is indistinguishable from a broken poller. Relative deadline\n  (\"+36h\") because a fixed instant goes stale and makes every order\n  instantly infeasible.\n\nVerified live after network-fulfillment#7 (which fixed the CrashLoopBackOff\nthis deployment exposed):\n- pod 2/2 Running, 0 restarts\n- poller: polls=2 received=1 failed=0, watermark advancing\n- the ACL translated ASIN-LOCAL-1 -> sku-1\n- a real NetworkOrder is persisted and readable through Kong at\n  /api/network-fulfillment/network-orders/po-local-1\n- it SURVIVES a rollout restart with receivedAt and acknowledgeBy\n  unchanged, which is the whole point of the Postgres work in #5\n- 11 ArgoCD apps Synced/Healthy, 0 non-Running pods fleet-wide\n\nThe order reads REJECTED, and that is correct rather than a failure:\norder-management answered not-feasible for a deadline it cannot meet with\nno inventory seeded, so this context refused inside the window instead of\ncommitting to a shipment it could not make. That verdict crossing both\ncontexts is the integration working.\n\nterraform validate clean, fmt clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtIsOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADEgQACZXcwUkU4r+G+x5UUF0wlPV\n3SV+AObkhdW5XHcuuazbNNqYWLNWaVFmKw5ofoXxk5xeEZbFhy91/iRN2XRpGAfO\nPjnXKE/2wo/8HJwe1qf58pO17PqkYKn3qiF/kchbTrFLG15+OJK7A4QDbnLqIXJp\nZjYUaR8se983JgO3Uzcca7f0tkoJsWJwgasKUDTCWK/NbxYL7JRZDHFc0kzHajo5\nzcHu7Gf/8v8CXgAR6FgrN9cWnO1uDnz03NZanS9iJtAClJGuRrecEMUpP3a2qsKR\n6sXTVxB1KV7xX3/j3RMD2spCaOGcu5tqmILSel1vm2uYB70SGL97OC1v2kHdKQJ5\nb9/kXFKPuTbnvjR2hA2Evuw+HqRiKfr94Ri78preG5o3rkkBq/qc3qf4Gt7g62Ok\nr9FC5xOQEqCh25GYbZW3ZokWBCI7hgbbZy0keNMASweQBu0BSShVEA9GXlJOyQqq\nR71DeyRJBaXR3x6IwKQtXlvTcSWla36RtVj2ATNzV5YJEXWRcmIkeB5/ravBFoeL\nHsZw/paB/MLvwBJZRdphdnOOKkNQw2NRTjwEzSVTegA31XuhtBxI63g6+FHYixCS\nmosyMFaDM/bXDVGEDeUYHX7z6cEsMd12tK5NZXzTikQiVq2Sn4dbmqy6qCO8t6jO\nXjx8VZZTZsHugWRQYT/n\n=Py8R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T02:29:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/ea23994e6efd86093a568de92f74155bfcd563af","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKGVhMjM5OTRlNmVmZDg2MDkzYTU2OGRlOTJmNzQxNTViZmNkNTYzYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250","sha":"33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250"}],"sha":"ea23994e6efd86093a568de92f74155bfcd563af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/ea23994e6efd86093a568de92f74155bfcd563af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T01:25:19Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T01:25:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(network-fulfillment): OLTP database for the acknowledgement deadlines (#34)\n\nnetwork-fulfillment persisted nothing: its NetworkOrder aggregate held the\n24h acknowledgement deadlines its sweep enforces in an in-memory map, and\npods here restart once at rollout by design. Its Postgres adapter landed in\nnetwork-fulfillment#5; this wires the database it needs.\n\nStill NOT added to local.services, deliberately. Membership there also\nimplies the analytics projector/reports apparatus, the Kafka wiring and a\nper-service chart shape none of which exist in this context, and moving it\nin would recreate the resources network-fulfillment.tf already owns. So the\ndatabase is wired explicitly, mirroring postgres.tf''s pattern (generated\npassword never committed, Secret consumed via the chart''s\ndatabase.existingSecret) rather than inheriting it.\n\nThe role/database is ALSO merged into init-databases.sql.tftpl''s `services`\nmap, so a fresh cluster provisions it on first boot like any other. On an\nalready-initialized Postgres that render never executes (Bitnami runs\ninitdb scripts exactly once, against an empty data directory) -- the file\nheader says so and names the recovery, and the generated password is\nexposed as a sensitive output for exactly that purpose.\n\nVerified against the live kind cluster, not just planned:\n- role + database created by hand (this cluster''s Postgres predates the\n  template change, so the documented initdb-runs-once pitfall applied)\n- pod 2/2 Running, 0 restarts, logging `\"order repository wired\",\n  \"backend\":\"postgres\"` -- not the in-memory fallback\n- startup migration created network_orders, network_order_lines and both\n  partial indexes the sweep and the confirmation leg depend on\n- /api/network-fulfillment/healthz still 200 through Kong\n- ArgoCD Synced/Healthy; all 45 pods Running\n- fail-closed PROVEN in-cluster: a throwaway release with a wrong password\n  CrashLoopBackOffs with `password authentication failed`, rather than\n  degrading to the in-memory map. Namespace removed; real deployment\n  untouched throughout.\n\nThe full plan also wants helm_release.postgresql updated in place (the\ninitdb ConfigMap changed). That is inert for an initialized cluster but\nwould touch the Postgres shared by all 11 services, so it is left for a\ndeliberate apply rather than folded in here -- the targeted apply used\ncovers only this context''s own resources.\n\nterraform validate clean, fmt clean.","tree":{"sha":"2c014738b2f58e6696a946946a2014296712569b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/2c014738b2f58e6696a946946a2014296712569b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c014738b2f58e6696a946946a2014296712569b\nparent 3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790213119 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790213119 -0300\n\nfeat(network-fulfillment): OLTP database for the acknowledgement deadlines (#34)\n\nnetwork-fulfillment persisted nothing: its NetworkOrder aggregate held the\n24h acknowledgement deadlines its sweep enforces in an in-memory map, and\npods here restart once at rollout by design. Its Postgres adapter landed in\nnetwork-fulfillment#5; this wires the database it needs.\n\nStill NOT added to local.services, deliberately. Membership there also\nimplies the analytics projector/reports apparatus, the Kafka wiring and a\nper-service chart shape none of which exist in this context, and moving it\nin would recreate the resources network-fulfillment.tf already owns. So the\ndatabase is wired explicitly, mirroring postgres.tf''s pattern (generated\npassword never committed, Secret consumed via the chart''s\ndatabase.existingSecret) rather than inheriting it.\n\nThe role/database is ALSO merged into init-databases.sql.tftpl''s `services`\nmap, so a fresh cluster provisions it on first boot like any other. On an\nalready-initialized Postgres that render never executes (Bitnami runs\ninitdb scripts exactly once, against an empty data directory) -- the file\nheader says so and names the recovery, and the generated password is\nexposed as a sensitive output for exactly that purpose.\n\nVerified against the live kind cluster, not just planned:\n- role + database created by hand (this cluster''s Postgres predates the\n  template change, so the documented initdb-runs-once pitfall applied)\n- pod 2/2 Running, 0 restarts, logging `\"order repository wired\",\n  \"backend\":\"postgres\"` -- not the in-memory fallback\n- startup migration created network_orders, network_order_lines and both\n  partial indexes the sweep and the confirmation leg depend on\n- /api/network-fulfillment/healthz still 200 through Kong\n- ArgoCD Synced/Healthy; all 45 pods Running\n- fail-closed PROVEN in-cluster: a throwaway release with a wrong password\n  CrashLoopBackOffs with `password authentication failed`, rather than\n  degrading to the in-memory map. Namespace removed; real deployment\n  untouched throughout.\n\nThe full plan also wants helm_release.postgresql updated in place (the\ninitdb ConfigMap changed). That is inert for an initialized cluster but\nwould touch the Postgres shared by all 11 services, so it is left for a\ndeliberate apply rather than folded in here -- the targeted apply used\ncovers only this context''s own resources.\n\nterraform validate clean, fmt clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtHv/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiOMQAJ2AerbY4VYRjLDamiJwpVU9\nZhF76JBYmyGguA7/RO7RhcJWuiLH3jOv0DhPm73AhPk+UdT6zPb9eJNvNEJrA2lb\n/mwaaSRK1FPP7mxmFDApP91Mq3mj3JPFnoABe+8R6uH3V2mjZPXdh4GZVYlm0Svs\nerEQtzAoqlBgTL0GdfhAwLkcM6wwqXziaUZ6nfK5j0/aPNmnViHx2Uq6UwgzqXea\nG7en+qsVoF/rKsQXtuaM91Niv7xX5udjJlMUA1vCjWZUOWWibcYkeveUPWejYPof\naY4HaZXk0EN/J/tjIZusHaSiM1bfVoSb4y9FAiQyx8UsILi4yX+o7ucgqxUkDyqN\n6k/knITJm/wuJdeRe7NSSUG9eji1eC8eVinOJ/sgoLmYkf/ZRAKZiWshVPRYU93I\n76ipYOBseBqDl9+hUusWUxObF10JFc1hCA5xCZ3cgJlAdDCIfnYaPJXhCVA/AJnQ\nt+1j1gNnSqu27xgz0hvH4M2zb5L2ebVI6zJ06vD229EhlC+KqlkWxb3hCLTXC5n1\nKWTaQac+S4mX6ITejJuetPeyltcIPPyEwyCHH4q86McCDFKlLVHTZIsMPLylAkOz\nAXuAOZlrQdN1zoHsL24i2IOSF3DStr3w9sgqedADIxL12odivTGBXM9YRHIQ1xvh\n4O7+dFx77NdMsFYBgNhP\n=hR1N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T01:25:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDMzZGQ1MjU3MjU1MGNiNmMzM2IyOTYzMDhjYjlkZDA2YTU1ZWYyNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd","sha":"3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd"}],"sha":"33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/33dd52572550cb6c33b296308cb9dd06a55ef250"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T02:38:45Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T02:38:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: register network-fulfillment, stub-mode only (#33)\n\n* feat: register network-fulfillment, stub-mode only\n\nThe fleet''s tenth context could not deploy: local.services assumes a\ndatabase per service and network-fulfillment has none, so there was\nnowhere to put it and no chart_path to point at until its chart landed\n(network-fulfillment#4).\n\nRegistered the way warehouse-ops-agent is -- its own file, its own\nArgoCD Application, outside local.services -- because it shares the same\nshape: no database, no Kafka, so the per-service Postgres/secret/\nanalytics apparatus in services.tf would have nothing to act on.\n\nTHE IMPORTANT PART IS WHAT THIS DOES NOT SET. networkMode stays at the\nchart''s stub default, deliberately and permanently for the local kind\ncluster: no external calls, no credentials, no Secret. This cluster\ntherefore CANNOT acknowledge a real retailer''s order, and terraform\napply never needs an SP-API credential to exist anywhere. A real-network\nenvironment sets networkMode and credentials.existingSecret in ITS\noverlay, not here.\n\nsweepInterval is 5m against a 24h acknowledgement window on purpose: the\nsweep must run many times inside the window it enforces, or an expired\nhold sits on real inventory reservations until the next pass rather than\nat its deadline.\n\nterraform validate passes, fmt clean.\n\n* ci: check out network-fulfillment for the terraform jobs\n\nterraform validate failed on the registration commit: network-fulfillment.tf\nhashes that repo''s Dockerfile/go.mod/go.sum to derive an image tag, and CI\nchecks out each sibling repo explicitly rather than the whole fleet. The new\ncontext was not in that list, so filesha256 had nothing to read.\n\nIt passed locally only because every sibling repo exists on the dev machine\n-- exactly the kind of gap a local-only check cannot see.\n\nAdded to all three jobs that check out siblings, mirroring the\nwarehouse-ops-agent entry directly above each one.","tree":{"sha":"04618b4bd06362ce966acdfe38e1f00777a00fd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/04618b4bd06362ce966acdfe38e1f00777a00fd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd","verification":{"payload":"tree 04618b4bd06362ce966acdfe38e1f00777a00fd0\nparent 07dc5745358386ec84402986bd896aeb674e4e67\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790131125 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790131125 -0300\n\nfeat: register network-fulfillment, stub-mode only (#33)\n\n* feat: register network-fulfillment, stub-mode only\n\nThe fleet''s tenth context could not deploy: local.services assumes a\ndatabase per service and network-fulfillment has none, so there was\nnowhere to put it and no chart_path to point at until its chart landed\n(network-fulfillment#4).\n\nRegistered the way warehouse-ops-agent is -- its own file, its own\nArgoCD Application, outside local.services -- because it shares the same\nshape: no database, no Kafka, so the per-service Postgres/secret/\nanalytics apparatus in services.tf would have nothing to act on.\n\nTHE IMPORTANT PART IS WHAT THIS DOES NOT SET. networkMode stays at the\nchart''s stub default, deliberately and permanently for the local kind\ncluster: no external calls, no credentials, no Secret. This cluster\ntherefore CANNOT acknowledge a real retailer''s order, and terraform\napply never needs an SP-API credential to exist anywhere. A real-network\nenvironment sets networkMode and credentials.existingSecret in ITS\noverlay, not here.\n\nsweepInterval is 5m against a 24h acknowledgement window on purpose: the\nsweep must run many times inside the window it enforces, or an expired\nhold sits on real inventory reservations until the next pass rather than\nat its deadline.\n\nterraform validate passes, fmt clean.\n\n* ci: check out network-fulfillment for the terraform jobs\n\nterraform validate failed on the registration commit: network-fulfillment.tf\nhashes that repo''s Dockerfile/go.mod/go.sum to derive an image tag, and CI\nchecks out each sibling repo explicitly rather than the whole fleet. The new\ncontext was not in that list, so filesha256 had nothing to read.\n\nIt passed locally only because every sibling repo exists on the dev machine\n-- exactly the kind of gap a local-only check cannot see.\n\nAdded to all three jobs that check out siblings, mirroring the\nwarehouse-ops-agent entry directly above each one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqszu1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqq4QAJiLdwQvlERJeybQyMYuz33I\n0jke/gal4hodpZD2YqXeBO9WqyDuo4+sor17AMwoH5YiRkn27HXRl5itJe61rndr\nU8i3SjyaSeTom+8C85E9j/cBhmej4/deFInHuqtJ5MeZ+ckFD8TVej9d3FyF1Oqv\nuR4AhKL41cmOxoJSGDcH6gINGfY9mEP3ijqwy0EiC0t7mhgbZvA2j4hqbR9Z5RFf\ntEc9Zk/IQYOsbMrJhnCCOaIVUfH38ejBO6uOGV9r1aYRbaIpMvBsbrnKdwH7NX7z\n1AiOUH3Rq4g6vI2tud6iKcxCmmY5Ecq5gP7Qmsy6cIWnHqbjxJtwpYmde+Nlw6Og\n2GR9UcOy/O12KE70OC7wRVdswj4qcgqN6ka7IpZxNDBFpdhnDJDCGjKNRFtw4qe8\nZLfHv7JaPCw36FzLgjDK2WdSoH3HsaNcvbMH2rmN5NlHSrNRgatTgFtVUxCi/Pl4\nB9srWLwjzVLqn/0MNPtdjZD7BfThiNTAAy4BBINtf1D7G3t0bCbrvBkpKicJWkW8\nr4+kdRaNfKyIkY74Ob1bvLFMN3CbhRYASREq2i87/CNPqT+QasTQaARH01OBuf8j\nHamcj86Cm+Ivx2paCgkmmmm04V/I04qPVnNiOcR/5vgDEy+0H33em5HAtF/i1X3q\nZlSI4A7lv/2QQG8Su4gU\n=YYro\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T02:38:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDNiNTAzNzNlYzM4MzA0MGI4MDBlNzRmMzA4MTJkMDQ1N2MzZTlmZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/07dc5745358386ec84402986bd896aeb674e4e67","sha":"07dc5745358386ec84402986bd896aeb674e4e67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/07dc5745358386ec84402986bd896aeb674e4e67"}],"sha":"3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/3b50373ec383040b800e74f30812d0457c3e9ffd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/07dc5745358386ec84402986bd896aeb674e4e67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:24:16Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:24:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(agents): add AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md — cluster deploy model, pitfalls, non-negotiables (#32)\n\nThis repo had zero agent guide at all, unlike every other repo in the\nfleet. Documents: local.services as the single source of truth for what\nTerraform deploys, the chart-template/rebuild/image-tag pitfalls that\nhave each cost real time (terraform apply not picking up chart changes,\nstale local sibling checkouts, image tag local + IfNotPresent never\nrolling), the initdb-never-reruns trap for analytics_services/\nmcp_services additions, the ternary key-set unification rule, the\ncomputed-extraEnv-overrides-helm-values gotcha, the MODE-defaults-to-\npermissive trap, the selector-collision fix and its CI conformance\ncheck, the destroy-leaves-phantom-state recovery, and the git rm vs\nrm -rf rule.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 4\nTask 4.4.","tree":{"sha":"d8dfac06afe6cce1c6eff9f0d5491e28902a3b26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/d8dfac06afe6cce1c6eff9f0d5491e28902a3b26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/07dc5745358386ec84402986bd896aeb674e4e67","verification":{"payload":"tree d8dfac06afe6cce1c6eff9f0d5491e28902a3b26\nparent d1f1fbb5b640d55128ca712fb45088752383ca11\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789385056 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789385056 -0300\n\ndocs(agents): add AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md — cluster deploy model, pitfalls, non-negotiables (#32)\n\nThis repo had zero agent guide at all, unlike every other repo in the\nfleet. Documents: local.services as the single source of truth for what\nTerraform deploys, the chart-template/rebuild/image-tag pitfalls that\nhave each cost real time (terraform apply not picking up chart changes,\nstale local sibling checkouts, image tag local + IfNotPresent never\nrolling), the initdb-never-reruns trap for analytics_services/\nmcp_services additions, the ternary key-set unification rule, the\ncomputed-extraEnv-overrides-helm-values gotcha, the MODE-defaults-to-\npermissive trap, the selector-collision fix and its CI conformance\ncheck, the destroy-leaves-phantom-state recovery, and the git rm vs\nrm -rf rule.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 4\nTask 4.4.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp9lgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATMMQAEVPMmtKeVZzErww6CPJm1hy\nLbrbJLAxfx/lXMQOn29rA3hmtzIsmpEIPkxEu6ijNaGDjXQOQV9/8yWrY6Yw937q\nHQbly0qNNsmPKCHOBdpGAGCUY3e5oYQxs6Hp5svRZZjSM9h4CdCQL6u4iP0cLmz3\nPin36OTGRZpDb11fHeZPJ2424iAjK0YQo2lFyKmR3N/zP32D//awa4gUXjattj5E\nIDWogn3t9wuy0LzIxBfkgRweK5ajwK+XCEuT1KRXB4Sc1UYlK+A