.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/07dc5745358386ec84402986bd896aeb674e4e67"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/d1f1fbb5b640d55128ca712fb45088752383ca11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:41:43Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:41:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): add GitHub Actions workflow — terraform, helm-lint, shellcheck, chart-selector-check (#31)\n\n* feat(ci): add GitHub Actions workflow — terraform, helm-lint, shellcheck, chart-selector-check\n\nThis repo had zero CI of any kind. Adds .github/workflows/ci.yml with four\njobs, each wired to the Phase 1 Makefile targets so local and CI feedback\nmatch exactly:\n\n- terraform: fmt -check + validate (hashicorp/setup-terraform)\n- shellcheck: scripts/*.sh at warning severity (ubuntu-latest ships\n  shellcheck preinstalled -- no third-party action needed)\n- helm-lint: lints all 10 charts this repo deploys, checking out all nine\n  sibling repos (+ warehouse-console) at develop next to this one so\n  relative chart paths resolve exactly as they do in local dev\n- chart-selector-check: NEW sensor (scripts/check-chart-selectors.py) --\n  renders every chart with every optional component enabled and asserts\n  each Service selects exactly one Deployment\n\n## Why chart-selector-check\n\nThis fleet already lived the bug class it guards against: every chart''s\nselectorLabels helper originally emitted only\napp.kubernetes.io/{name,instance}, identical across a service''s\nOLTP/MCP/projector/reports/frontend pods, so the OLTP Service silently\nselected all of them (verified live via endpointslices; a\nGET /order-management/healthz through Kong was answered by the reports\npod, not the OLTP pod). Every chart has since had a component label added\nto fix it, but nothing enforced the convention going forward -- a new\ncomponent template that forgets the label reintroduces the exact same\nsilent multi-select, and `helm lint` has no opinion on selector\ncardinality.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 2\nTasks 2.3 and 2.3b.\n\n## Verified locally\n\n- Simulated the CI job topology exactly: symlinked all 10 sibling repos\n  next to a copy of this worktree, ran `make helm-lint` and `make\n  chart-selector-check` from inside it -- both green, all 10 charts OK.\n- Proved the new sensor actually fires: temporarily removed\n  order-management''s OLTP Service''s `app.kubernetes.io/component: api`\n  selector line, re-ran the script, got \"Service ...order-management\n  selects 5 Deployment(s)\" -- the exact bug shape this fleet already hit\n  live -- then reverted before committing (order-management''s working\n  tree is untouched, confirmed via `git status`/`git diff --stat` showing\n  no change to that file).\n- `make check` (tf-fmt-check, tf-validate, helm-lint, shellcheck,\n  chart-selector-check) passes end to end from the real checkout.\n\n* fix(ci): terraform job needs all 11 sibling repos checked out, not just 10\n\nterraform validate''s services.tf/frontends.tf reference every sibling\nrepo''s go.sum (services.tf) AND warehouse-console/warehouse-ui-kit''s\nsource files (frontends.tf) via filesha256() -- the terraform job was\nmissing checkouts entirely on the first push and failed outright; this\nfix adds all 10 service+console checkouts to the terraform job (it only\nhad the bare warehouse-infra checkout) plus the additional\nwarehouse-ui-kit checkout terraform validate needs that helm-lint/\nchart-selector-check do not (they only render chart templates, never\ntouch frontends.tf''s source-hash locals).\n\nVerified in a local sibling-symlink simulation of the exact CI checkout\ntopology: make tf-fmt-check and make tf-validate both pass cleanly.","tree":{"sha":"0e76feea5bedb8d35ae10b1e1b45faa91be035d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/0e76feea5bedb8d35ae10b1e1b45faa91be035d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/d1f1fbb5b640d55128ca712fb45088752383ca11","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e76feea5bedb8d35ae10b1e1b45faa91be035d4\nparent 771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789350103 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789350103 -0300\n\nfeat(ci): add GitHub Actions workflow — terraform, helm-lint, shellcheck, chart-selector-check (#31)\n\n* feat(ci): add GitHub Actions workflow — terraform, helm-lint, shellcheck, chart-selector-check\n\nThis repo had zero CI of any kind. Adds .github/workflows/ci.yml with four\njobs, each wired to the Phase 1 Makefile targets so local and CI feedback\nmatch exactly:\n\n- terraform: fmt -check + validate (hashicorp/setup-terraform)\n- shellcheck: scripts/*.sh at warning severity (ubuntu-latest ships\n  shellcheck preinstalled -- no third-party action needed)\n- helm-lint: lints all 10 charts this repo deploys, checking out all nine\n  sibling repos (+ warehouse-console) at develop next to this one so\n  relative chart paths resolve exactly as they do in local dev\n- chart-selector-check: NEW sensor (scripts/check-chart-selectors.py) --\n  renders every chart with every optional component enabled and asserts\n  each Service selects exactly one Deployment\n\n## Why chart-selector-check\n\nThis fleet already lived the bug class it guards against: every chart''s\nselectorLabels helper originally emitted only\napp.kubernetes.io/{name,instance}, identical across a service''s\nOLTP/MCP/projector/reports/frontend pods, so the OLTP Service silently\nselected all of them (verified live via endpointslices; a\nGET /order-management/healthz through Kong was answered by the reports\npod, not the OLTP pod). Every chart has since had a component label added\nto fix it, but nothing enforced the convention going forward -- a new\ncomponent template that forgets the label reintroduces the exact same\nsilent multi-select, and `helm lint` has no opinion on selector\ncardinality.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 2\nTasks 2.3 and 2.3b.\n\n## Verified locally\n\n- Simulated the CI job topology exactly: symlinked all 10 sibling repos\n  next to a copy of this worktree, ran `make helm-lint` and `make\n  chart-selector-check` from inside it -- both green, all 10 charts OK.\n- Proved the new sensor actually fires: temporarily removed\n  order-management''s OLTP Service''s `app.kubernetes.io/component: api`\n  selector line, re-ran the script, got \"Service ...order-management\n  selects 5 Deployment(s)\" -- the exact bug shape this fleet already hit\n  live -- then reverted before committing (order-management''s working\n  tree is untouched, confirmed via `git status`/`git diff --stat` showing\n  no change to that file).\n- `make check` (tf-fmt-check, tf-validate, helm-lint, shellcheck,\n  chart-selector-check) passes end to end from the real checkout.\n\n* fix(ci): terraform job needs all 11 sibling repos checked out, not just 10\n\nterraform validate''s services.tf/frontends.tf reference every sibling\nrepo''s go.sum (services.tf) AND warehouse-console/warehouse-ui-kit''s\nsource files (frontends.tf) via filesha256() -- the terraform job was\nmissing checkouts entirely on the first push and failed outright; this\nfix adds all 10 service+console checkouts to the terraform job (it only\nhad the bare warehouse-infra checkout) plus the additional\nwarehouse-ui-kit checkout terraform validate needs that helm-lint/\nchart-selector-check do not (they only render chart templates, never\ntouch frontends.tf''s source-hash locals).\n\nVerified in a local sibling-symlink simulation of the exact CI checkout\ntopology: make tf-fmt-check and make tf-validate both pass cleanly.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp1DXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL+kQAFxNnYcctMIe6hoXcehXUxpe\noBoBeUsRaccEwCViVunLIeuzSdi+hY6uG6Ec4RCnD/Ryf+3wd9lXt5gpReBe/88l\nv/hUeJ9QCddH8cG6PtgoXXw7hcmKC+RgIKXYEGEn+oFBDlUmtnZMlR7ZkGX/I3Iz\njG5t9mihF/XCFvTgmWKn2Z4uH38+AZoR80PHJbiLEMbcF2wE1TcrBo6/K37t8NKI\nZWe4flzUYOA+CH2YJ8eJEMCojTwzMgwu5bx4YgCgFk/EGPcxvONe/fq6m81RqtL8\nnm5XCRFWZXViS56CrlCrAiHrtxhJch42LhPUQG5+O0WBzcBI2y1GiTBIiJSjznoy\n5Ja63XxeShVbN7E+CScDh7GVScI+HXH9D+1wUIx97pqfs9mjQAAFPTjI3m/afrg7\nYy1rM+ZuYVgzTVhi0NZ0V0PP8q9Ouuaf8MulIfD3QvSYPlyBsd3eoxuu68gCAZ3j\nhzQBRPIoX8c62BRJklZ9If1KE1wqHbQnm5PezfpOBb+ujc2cHk2nx53RAWV6S75r\n7K8DQV58EkJY2k6IXCXqPsKIj43NQ4fAYxc4aiaiyJY8KdRrc+fdrtGv28mCZqap\niEqmdtlkXgv1e0JVAQIgU3uwU+reNWCBtyXnMruVlDr3WnPdw5f07SlMsMdwb3CP\npjp7UWfvP9riwUijNY6T\n=h6Ez\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T01:41:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/d1f1fbb5b640d55128ca712fb45088752383ca11","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKGQxZjFmYmI1YjY0MGQ1NTEyOGNhNzEyZmI0NTA4ODc1MjM4M2NhMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52","sha":"771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52"}],"sha":"d1f1fbb5b640d55128ca712fb45088752383ca11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/d1f1fbb5b640d55128ca712fb45088752383ca11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:08:31Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T01:08:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(build): add Makefile — terraform fmt/validate, helm-lint, shellcheck (#30)\n\nThis repo had zero CI/local sensors of any kind: no .github/workflows,\nno Makefile, no `make check`. terraform fmt/validate, helm lint on the ten\ncharts this repo deploys, and shellcheck on scripts/*.sh were only ever\nrun by hand, ad hoc.\n\nAdds a Makefile with tf-fmt-check, tf-validate, helm-lint (iterating the\nsame chart_path list terraform/locals.tf + ops-agent.tf + frontends.tf\nactually deploy, with workforce-management''s required dummy database.url),\nand shellcheck --severity=warning, rolled into a `check`/`check-all` bundle\nmatching the vocabulary every other repo in the fleet now uses.\n\nAlso fixes the one real shellcheck warning.severity finding:\nscripts/smoke-test.sh''s unchecked `cd` (SC2164) now exits on failure\ninstead of silently continuing in the wrong directory.\n\nThis is not wired into GitHub Actions yet (this repo has no CI workflow at\nall) -- that is tracked as a separate follow-up in the harness-engineering\ncoverage expansion plan. `make check` is the gate for now; run it before\nevery commit/PR that touches terraform/, charts referenced by this repo,\nor scripts/.\n\nVerified locally: terraform fmt clean, terraform validate succeeds\n(init -backend=false against the real sibling repo checkouts), all 10\ncharts lint clean, shellcheck clean at warning severity.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 1\nTask 1.5.","tree":{"sha":"be7a499c46a60764fc7c3fd63db502dea23007f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/be7a499c46a60764fc7c3fd63db502dea23007f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52","verification":{"payload":"tree be7a499c46a60764fc7c3fd63db502dea23007f1\nparent 1a70189eeaeab00be9e4acb9400d03e262c1ba63\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789348111 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789348111 -0300\n\nfeat(build): add Makefile — terraform fmt/validate, helm-lint, shellcheck (#30)\n\nThis repo had zero CI/local sensors of any kind: no .github/workflows,\nno Makefile, no `make check`. terraform fmt/validate, helm lint on the ten\ncharts this repo deploys, and shellcheck on scripts/*.sh were only ever\nrun by hand, ad hoc.\n\nAdds a Makefile with tf-fmt-check, tf-validate, helm-lint (iterating the\nsame chart_path list terraform/locals.tf + ops-agent.tf + frontends.tf\nactually deploy, with workforce-management''s required dummy database.url),\nand shellcheck --severity=warning, rolled into a `check`/`check-all` bundle\nmatching the vocabulary every other repo in the fleet now uses.\n\nAlso fixes the one real shellcheck warning.severity finding:\nscripts/smoke-test.sh''s unchecked `cd` (SC2164) now exits on failure\ninstead of silently continuing in the wrong directory.\n\nThis is not wired into GitHub Actions yet (this repo has no CI workflow at\nall) -- that is tracked as a separate follow-up in the harness-engineering\ncoverage expansion plan. `make check` is the gate for now; run it before\nevery commit/PR that touches terraform/, charts referenced by this repo,\nor scripts/.\n\nVerified locally: terraform fmt clean, terraform validate succeeds\n(init -backend=false against the real sibling repo checkouts), all 10\ncharts lint clean, shellcheck clean at warning severity.\n\nPart of the harness-engineering coverage expansion plan\n(.hermes/plans/2026-09-13_234500-harness-coverage-expansion.md), Phase 1\nTask 1.5.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp0kPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANFcQAGtxE9b2Hg3mmf7a56gI83KH\npQedD1rzUJ8s7al7BJur5gVdSpTuoFeDRvgItQjTZjS34nkj7QWWfSRVZti23mU3\n7D3K5KuWU4zfz/vlrAzByRLkC1qYhhdwh8ukJeInvK0Lym2lHTKRVBGhIiOf9IX4\niJ6vFT/2/xhR8RMPFCsN3Tj/yuHt1uMDOuoJOoegsYgrqkzknfd3qYJv28QHkX6R\nn+YcKLHiE7Mzq/CmVhtMvzr2Uax4UJa0Sef4SmFE5lipyigk4as1Lf+i0u6LQ4tv\nwuBDpQb2ysi6/dQtUFXaT3fwgnXUpFKbqE/fuZmvfGsoCbKftFVG2xcXj3jCQ0iX\nbDQrCjidoodvt3VbasJOwRpzTdbMlYIzt3BuLDFw9b1KUx1T4SF5pkIeAcXbnPCB\n6gm4d6N54aQtn0TuY7Jh+rLmD/AukW5tSFJagXYgDW8UE5iY6hZPY21KlGmlr6KS\njxE+rJVAx55xuyVAJY1UO5oZwWiOrFKFz+KjolFZA3BB4pCF8Rce3YXxgC2U/xr+\ne5J2U/vIoVdJ9sd1ncvTUQ5TT/BX2SS4M6ihKjnHZLaKReV1EqD4xtf75iaRW5pI\nuO67nkaYibzrdVNnDVAIlGH/kqCyPqGpsYcvBgrFiiXvLBEf+aUbZ3XQq84hN5re\nhev1eU+riIdixsqusWO2\n=50qJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T01:08:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDc3MWMwYzE3MmJiN2YwOTE0NmJkNTgxNTk2MmUyNWQ5MjYzZGNhNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/1a70189eeaeab00be9e4acb9400d03e262c1ba63","sha":"1a70189eeaeab00be9e4acb9400d03e262c1ba63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/1a70189eeaeab00be9e4acb9400d03e262c1ba63"}],"sha":"771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/771c0c172bb7f09146bd5815962e25d9263dca52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/1a70189eeaeab00be9e4acb9400d03e262c1ba63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T22:45:39Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T22:45:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(observability): fleet-wide + per-context log dashboards (Loki) (#29)\n\nAdds the logs pillar to the dashboard-as-code work in PR #28 (Kong\nmetrics + per-context Grafana dashboards), completing the\nmetrics/traces/logs triad -- traces already had Jaeger''s own UI, and this\nwas the last pillar with no Grafana surface at all despite logging.tf''s\nLoki+Alloy pipeline having existed since before that PR.\n\n## What\n\n- `terraform/dashboards/logs-overview.json` (new): fleet-wide cross-context\n  error/warning triage in one raw log stream, plus log-volume-per-context\n  and error+warning-volume-per-context timeseries. Built from an explicit\n  EXCLUSION list of platform/infra `app` labels (Kong, Istio, ArgoCD,\n  Kafka, Postgres, the observability stack itself, console/ops-agent) so a\n  newly deployed bounded context appears here automatically -- no script\n  edit needed, unlike the per-context dashboards which need an inclusion\n  entry.\n- Each of the 8 per-context dashboards (`terraform/dashboards/contexts/*.json`)\n  gains a fifth row: a live raw-log-stream panel (that context''s pods only,\n  istio-proxy/istio-init sidecar noise excluded), a log-volume-by-level\n  timeseries, and an errors/warnings-only stream.\n- `scripts/gen-context-dashboards.py`: `loki_target()`/`logs_panel()`\n  helpers, a `loki_app` field per CONTEXTS entry (the exact `app` label\n  Alloy assigns, uniform across a context''s OLTP/frontend/mcp/projector/\n  reports pods -- unlike the Prometheus side''s `service_regex`, which\n  needs per-context regex variants), and `build_logs_overview()`.\n\n## Why\n\nlogging.tf''s Loki+Alloy pipeline has existed since before the dashboard\nwork in #28, but the ONLY way to read a log was `kubectl logs <pod>` --\nno cross-service search, no correlation with the metrics/traffic panels\nalready on each context''s dashboard. Every service already writes\nstructured JSON with the active trace_id in the body (see logging.tf''s\nderived-fields comment on the Grafana Loki datasource), so this makes\nthat log data actually reachable from the same dashboards operators\nalready look at for metrics.\n\n## Design notes\n\n- **`app` label, not `service_name`.** Loki''s label comes straight from\n  the `app.kubernetes.io/name` pod label (logging.tf''s Alloy pipeline),\n  which is IDENTICAL across a context''s OLTP/frontend/mcp/projector/\n  reports pods -- a plain equality match, not the regex the Prometheus\n  side needs for its differently-named `service_name` values\n  (order-management-projector vs. wes-projector vs. fulfillment-projector).\n- **Loki requires a positive matcher.** A selector built purely from `!~`\n  exclusions (`app!~\"...\", container!~\"...\"`) is rejected outright with\n  \"queries require at least one regexp or equality matcher that does not\n  have an empty-compatible value\" -- verified against the live instance,\n  not assumed from docs. The fleet-wide dashboard''s exclusion-list\n  selector adds `app=~\".+\"` to satisfy this without narrowing the match.\n- **istio-proxy/istio-init excluded everywhere.** Every pod in this fleet\n  runs a native Istio sidecar (kubernetes-deployment.md''s documented\n  gotcha); its own Envoy access logs would otherwise dominate a raw panel\n  meant to show application output.\n\n## Verification (live against the `warehouse` kind cluster)\n\n- `terraform validate` / `terraform fmt -check` clean.\n- `terraform plan -target=helm_release.grafana` -> 1 to change; applied\n  twice (once with the initial Loki-selector bug, once after the fix).\n- `GET /api/search?query=warehouse` lists all 11 dashboards (go-runtime,\n  kong-gateway-overview, logs-overview, 8 per-context).\n- Queried Grafana''s own Loki-datasource proxy directly with the EXACT\n  expressions the generated panels use:\n  - order-management''s \"Live log stream\" selector returned 2 real streams\n    (OLTP + reports pods).\n  - the fleet-wide \"Total log lines per second, by context\" query returned\n    a real per-app matrix (facility-layout, etc. -- confirmed non-empty\n    values across a hover window).\n  - the ERROR|WARN-filtered queries (both fleet-wide and per-context)\n    execute with `status: success` and correctly return zero results\n    (the fleet is healthy right now; the earlier -- unfixed -- version of\n    this same query family failed with a Loki parse error, which is the\n    bug this verification step exists to catch).","tree":{"sha":"be45e87608783b8868a256c93bdd882225ba0a6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/be45e87608783b8868a256c93bdd882225ba0a6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/1a70189eeaeab00be9e4acb9400d03e262c1ba63","verification":{"payload":"tree be45e87608783b8868a256c93bdd882225ba0a6a\nparent 2e85142614c645be76896b31962b6abdc71a2324\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789339539 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789339539 -0300\n\nfeat(observability): fleet-wide + per-context log dashboards (Loki) (#29)\n\nAdds the logs pillar to the dashboard-as-code work in PR #28 (Kong\nmetrics + per-context Grafana dashboards), completing the\nmetrics/traces/logs triad -- traces already had Jaeger''s own UI, and this\nwas the last pillar with no Grafana surface at all despite logging.tf''s\nLoki+Alloy pipeline having existed since before that PR.\n\n## What\n\n- `terraform/dashboards/logs-overview.json` (new): fleet-wide cross-context\n  error/warning triage in one raw log stream, plus log-volume-per-context\n  and error+warning-volume-per-context timeseries. Built from an explicit\n  EXCLUSION list of platform/infra `app` labels (Kong, Istio, ArgoCD,\n  Kafka, Postgres, the observability stack itself, console/ops-agent) so a\n  newly deployed bounded context appears here automatically -- no script\n  edit needed, unlike the per-context dashboards which need an inclusion\n  entry.\n- Each of the 8 per-context dashboards (`terraform/dashboards/contexts/*.json`)\n  gains a fifth row: a live raw-log-stream panel (that context''s pods only,\n  istio-proxy/istio-init sidecar noise excluded), a log-volume-by-level\n  timeseries, and an errors/warnings-only stream.\n- `scripts/gen-context-dashboards.py`: `loki_target()`/`logs_panel()`\n  helpers, a `loki_app` field per CONTEXTS entry (the exact `app` label\n  Alloy assigns, uniform across a context''s OLTP/frontend/mcp/projector/\n  reports pods -- unlike the Prometheus side''s `service_regex`, which\n  needs per-context regex variants), and `build_logs_overview()`.\n\n## Why\n\nlogging.tf''s Loki+Alloy pipeline has existed since before the dashboard\nwork in #28, but the ONLY way to read a log was `kubectl logs <pod>` --\nno cross-service search, no correlation with the metrics/traffic panels\nalready on each context''s dashboard. Every service already writes\nstructured JSON with the active trace_id in the body (see logging.tf''s\nderived-fields comment on the Grafana Loki datasource), so this makes\nthat log data actually reachable from the same dashboards operators\nalready look at for metrics.\n\n## Design notes\n\n- **`app` label, not `service_name`.** Loki''s label comes straight from\n  the `app.kubernetes.io/name` pod label (logging.tf''s Alloy pipeline),\n  which is IDENTICAL across a context''s OLTP/frontend/mcp/projector/\n  reports pods -- a plain equality match, not the regex the Prometheus\n  side needs for its differently-named `service_name` values\n  (order-management-projector vs. wes-projector vs. fulfillment-projector).\n- **Loki requires a positive matcher.** A selector built purely from `!~`\n  exclusions (`app!~\"...\", container!~\"...\"`) is rejected outright with\n  \"queries require at least one regexp or equality matcher that does not\n  have an empty-compatible value\" -- verified against the live instance,\n  not assumed from docs. The fleet-wide dashboard''s exclusion-list\n  selector adds `app=~\".+\"` to satisfy this without narrowing the match.\n- **istio-proxy/istio-init excluded everywhere.** Every pod in this fleet\n  runs a native Istio sidecar (kubernetes-deployment.md''s documented\n  gotcha); its own Envoy access logs would otherwise dominate a raw panel\n  meant to show application output.\n\n## Verification (live against the `warehouse` kind cluster)\n\n- `terraform validate` / `terraform fmt -check` clean.\n- `terraform plan -target=helm_release.grafana` -> 1 to change; applied\n  twice (once with the initial Loki-selector bug, once after the fix).\n- `GET /api/search?query=warehouse` lists all 11 dashboards (go-runtime,\n  kong-gateway-overview, logs-overview, 8 per-context).\n- Queried Grafana''s own Loki-datasource proxy directly with the EXACT\n  expressions the generated panels use:\n  - order-management''s \"Live log stream\" selector returned 2 real streams\n    (OLTP + reports pods).\n  - the fleet-wide \"Total log lines per second, by context\" query returned\n    a real per-app matrix (facility-layout, etc. -- confirmed non-empty\n    values across a hover window).\n  - the ERROR|WARN-filtered queries (both fleet-wide and per-context)\n    execute with `status: success` and correctly return zero results\n    (the fleet is healthy right now; the earlier -- unfixed -- version of\n    this same query family failed with a Loki parse error, which is the\n    bug this verification step exists to catch).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpyeTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHQ0QADkzsKQpAPwzvt46GIzq6w1E\nC2hJShoW2n9tM+HaCGaWxjKfVmutpXjnIfn33XtrbC3KHXXLE3vegktm5bZVGuPy\nkUK7gHzGj7vdpFuQJtBOm4EDAWDKgYGvvo/8VrJVEzfiZA++kzHKQadMZaoCQ07m\n1FD6kkoywOJyj1nSc+QZRBDSIdj7sP2B65jKd8VrChE5Ycovp6qBJK09fzplIGHJ\nA8/sU727N4QwHZunbNEDyagl8fLi+lIoLVF5gj1y24BMfgd9lJHV/+nB0jmKKn6H\ncXWbMF8GmtKyw0Wmg4aWhKdFToDaqiQO5tXjoh+ND