e9e4acb9400d03e262c1ba63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/2e85142614c645be76896b31962b6abdc71a2324/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:29:48Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:29:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(observability): Kong Prometheus plugin + Grafana dashboards as code (#28)\n\nAdds an API-gateway-aware observability layer on top of the existing\nOTel/Prometheus/Grafana stack, entirely as infrastructure-as-code:\n\n## Kong Prometheus plugin (terraform/kong-prometheus.tf)\n\nEnables Kong''s own `prometheus` KongClusterPlugin (global, mirroring the\nexisting `warehouse-cors` KongClusterPlugin''s cluster-wide-vs-per-route\nrationale in kong-cors.tf) and annotates the Kong pod\n(`prometheus.io/scrape=true`, port 8100, the chart''s existing `status`\nlistener) so Prometheus''s stock `kubernetes-pods` scrape job picks it up\nwith zero new Prometheus-side config. This surfaces Kong''s own north-south\nview: request rate/errors/latency BEFORE a request even reaches an\nupstream that never got instrumented (crashed pod, 5xx from Envoy, etc.),\nwhich no per-service otelchi histogram can ever report because the\nrequest never arrived there.\n\nVerified live: `kong_datastore_reachable`, `kong_http_requests_total`,\n`kong_request_latency_ms_bucket`, `kong_upstream_latency_ms_bucket`,\n`kong_bandwidth_bytes` all present and incrementing in this cluster''s\nPrometheus after real traffic through every one of the 8 bounded\ncontexts'' Kong routes.\n\n## Grafana dashboards, generated (scripts/gen-context-dashboards.py)\n\n- `terraform/dashboards/kong-gateway-overview.json`: fleet-wide API\n  Gateway view -- health, per-context request rate/errors, upstream vs.\n  Kong-added latency, bandwidth.\n- `terraform/dashboards/contexts/<name>.json`, one per bounded context\n  (order-management, inventory-storage, wes-work-planning,\n  fulfillment-execution, workforce-management, facility-layout,\n  labor-performance, process-path-management): that context''s slice of\n  the Kong view, its own HTTP RED (otelchi, per ADR-0009 \"standard\n  metrics convention\"), its Tier-2 business counter(s), and Go runtime.\n\nGenerated, not hand-written, because all eight contexts share the exact\nsame four-row panel shape and only the service-name regex / Kong route /\nbusiness-metric queries differ -- see the script''s own header for the\nfull rationale and the metric-name provenance (verified against each\nservice''s internal/adapters/outbound/telemetry package on origin/develop,\ncross-checked live against this cluster''s Prometheus label_values).\nRe-run the script after editing CONTEXTS or the panel builders; never\nhand-edit the generated JSON.\n\n## Wiring (terraform/observability.tf)\n\n`helm_release.grafana`''s `dashboards.warehouse` map now merges the\nexisting go-runtime dashboard with the new kong-gateway-overview\ndashboard and a `fileset()`-driven loop over `dashboards/contexts/*.json`\n-- adding a new context''s dashboard later is drop-a-generated-file, no\nTerraform edit required.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `terraform validate` / `terraform fmt -check` clean.\n- `terraform plan -target=helm_release.kong -target=null_resource.kong_prometheus_plugin`\n  -> 1 to add, 1 to change; applied cleanly.\n- `terraform plan -target=helm_release.grafana` -> 1 to change; applied\n  cleanly.\n- Live cluster verification: Kong pod rolled with the new annotations,\n  `kubectl get kongclusterplugin` shows `warehouse-prometheus` PROGRAMMED\n  alongside the pre-existing `warehouse-cors`; Prometheus''s\n  `kubernetes-pods` job picked up the Kong pod with zero config changes\n  on the Prometheus side; sent real traffic through all 8 contexts''\n  `/api/<context>/healthz` Kong routes and confirmed `kong_http_requests_total`\n  counters incrementing per context and `rate(...)` non-zero.\n- Grafana: `GET /api/search?query=warehouse` lists all 10 dashboards\n  (go-runtime, kong-gateway-overview, 8 per-context) provisioned in the\n  `warehouse` folder; queried the Prometheus datasource proxy directly\n  for panel expressions from the Kong overview dashboard and confirmed\n  non-empty, non-zero results against live traffic.\n- Found and fixed (separate PR, claudioed/order-management#50) a real\n  gap surfaced by this work: order-management''s OLTP Deployment never\n  wired OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT/OTEL_SERVICE_NAME despite ADR-0009\n  adding telemetry.Setup to cmd/order, so its dashboard here will render\n  data as soon as that fix rolls and this cluster rebuilds the image.","tree":{"sha":"df76ee6a6168cb193da70582c47a774f5e6f0343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/df76ee6a6168cb193da70582c47a774f5e6f0343"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/2e85142614c645be76896b31962b6abdc71a2324","verification":{"payload":"tree df76ee6a6168cb193da70582c47a774f5e6f0343\nparent a7bd812401ae9aa1e4e41fcf9c47fac4784c920e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789313388 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789313388 -0300\n\nfeat(observability): Kong Prometheus plugin + Grafana dashboards as code (#28)\n\nAdds an API-gateway-aware observability layer on top of the existing\nOTel/Prometheus/Grafana stack, entirely as infrastructure-as-code:\n\n## Kong Prometheus plugin (terraform/kong-prometheus.tf)\n\nEnables Kong''s own `prometheus` KongClusterPlugin (global, mirroring the\nexisting `warehouse-cors` KongClusterPlugin''s cluster-wide-vs-per-route\nrationale in kong-cors.tf) and annotates the Kong pod\n(`prometheus.io/scrape=true`, port 8100, the chart''s existing `status`\nlistener) so Prometheus''s stock `kubernetes-pods` scrape job picks it up\nwith zero new Prometheus-side config. This surfaces Kong''s own north-south\nview: request rate/errors/latency BEFORE a request even reaches an\nupstream that never got instrumented (crashed pod, 5xx from Envoy, etc.),\nwhich no per-service otelchi histogram can ever report because the\nrequest never arrived there.\n\nVerified live: `kong_datastore_reachable`, `kong_http_requests_total`,\n`kong_request_latency_ms_bucket`, `kong_upstream_latency_ms_bucket`,\n`kong_bandwidth_bytes` all present and incrementing in this cluster''s\nPrometheus after real traffic through every one of the 8 bounded\ncontexts'' Kong routes.\n\n## Grafana dashboards, generated (scripts/gen-context-dashboards.py)\n\n- `terraform/dashboards/kong-gateway-overview.json`: fleet-wide API\n  Gateway view -- health, per-context request rate/errors, upstream vs.\n  Kong-added latency, bandwidth.\n- `terraform/dashboards/contexts/<name>.json`, one per bounded context\n  (order-management, inventory-storage, wes-work-planning,\n  fulfillment-execution, workforce-management, facility-layout,\n  labor-performance, process-path-management): that context''s slice of\n  the Kong view, its own HTTP RED (otelchi, per ADR-0009 \"standard\n  metrics convention\"), its Tier-2 business counter(s), and Go runtime.\n\nGenerated, not hand-written, because all eight contexts share the exact\nsame four-row panel shape and only the service-name regex / Kong route /\nbusiness-metric queries differ -- see the script''s own header for the\nfull rationale and the metric-name provenance (verified against each\nservice''s internal/adapters/outbound/telemetry package on origin/develop,\ncross-checked live against this cluster''s Prometheus label_values).\nRe-run the script after editing CONTEXTS or the panel builders; never\nhand-edit the generated JSON.\n\n## Wiring (terraform/observability.tf)\n\n`helm_release.grafana`''s `dashboards.warehouse` map now merges the\nexisting go-runtime dashboard with the new kong-gateway-overview\ndashboard and a `fileset()`-driven loop over `dashboards/contexts/*.json`\n-- adding a new context''s dashboard later is drop-a-generated-file, no\nTerraform edit required.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `terraform validate` / `terraform fmt -check` clean.\n- `terraform plan -target=helm_release.kong -target=null_resource.kong_prometheus_plugin`\n  -> 1 to add, 1 to change; applied cleanly.\n- `terraform plan -target=helm_release.grafana` -> 1 to change; applied\n  cleanly.\n- Live cluster verification: Kong pod rolled with the new annotations,\n  `kubectl get kongclusterplugin` shows `warehouse-prometheus` PROGRAMMED\n  alongside the pre-existing `warehouse-cors`; Prometheus''s\n  `kubernetes-pods` job picked up the Kong pod with zero config changes\n  on the Prometheus side; sent real traffic through all 8 contexts''\n  `/api/<context>/healthz` Kong routes and confirmed `kong_http_requests_total`\n  counters incrementing per context and `rate(...)` non-zero.\n- Grafana: `GET /api/search?query=warehouse` lists all 10 dashboards\n  (go-runtime, kong-gateway-overview, 8 per-context) provisioned in the\n  `warehouse` folder; queried the Prometheus datasource proxy directly\n  for panel expressions from the Kong overview dashboard and confirmed\n  non-empty, non-zero results against live traffic.\n- Found and fixed (separate PR, claudioed/order-management#50) a real\n  gap surfaced by this work: order-management''s OLTP Deployment never\n  wired OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT/OTEL_SERVICE_NAME despite ADR-0009\n  adding telemetry.Setup to cmd/order, so its dashboard here will render\n  data as soon as that fix rolls and this cluster rebuilds the image.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpsFsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3HgQAJS1/I7v2LSeucwJKXoA4W0p\n4Vx8d9f0uTJRM+QZvXv5fLf1XPIen7hBOiEsUgwdJDa26FH3Br85BF/rPnARe39H\nwZ6sW8sJLXz2rX+uF7EaJzO0dQUESjix9B9PsONxZhpyZU31chuVMYRlqHS0o6n2\n0ogyx/Lm2zcOEaS7YrEaDw5LFrgR6t5VFNu8v+IBLTDf1PygGQR6Cfdp8W6+hcm/\nwzXOYgq3R5XsbWcRk+RsjqOwD8C/rBKX+9V241dlzYQEr3TnQTN1yvi4pLiwK+Qv\n+lqJPO+ALLG/6fx0LNagc/ruQLGoSvzEZE86oraSBeX97MEwqL7JUqujsvLp4iSv\nPU5gatUJE+c+YqCkNUd3BYbGdwOh+j10DRUxRRUegJl3AWWAgrOABWOBrI/lqCZD\nCP1/t5nCDCzUtsR1j0vZsdt4mc2iUZkHb5DhkSXWxa7uwhO+HhmRDYBDRWCjehOh\nfJ3dhhc9Cnq/MBxH7Vx811eqad9UZosmmgTknwA8pBeuXcHWyl+cSTtGNQQU2MJI\n/YCtCy6JBKNwpw3rolQ7gwtYRKCPFN3GY3GV/yPIxPkdBHx1QeR4twUiiUWqqihU\ndVMPBOG6/NPyDkVu/Mo7pD50w4aInbPzh73yT0EVEvRAEQDG1wWowl7kaNcw4a05\nCHNs3fqTcV7Q3kupmfLG\n=ghru\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T15:29:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/2e85142614c645be76896b31962b6abdc71a2324","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDJlODUxNDI2MTRjNjQ1YmU3Njg5NmIzMTk2MmI2YWJkYzcxYTIzMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/a7bd812401ae9aa1e4e41fcf9c47fac4784c920e","sha":"a7bd812401ae9aa1e4e41fcf9c47fac4784c920e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/a7bd812401ae9aa1e4e41fcf9c47fac4784c920e"}],"sha":"2e85142614c645be76896b31962b6abdc71a2324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/2e85142614c645be76896b31962b6abdc71a2324"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/a7bd812401ae9aa1e4e41fcf9c47fac4784c920e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T14:31:54Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T14:31:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add a ports & hosts reference covering every app, incl. ArgoCD (#27)\n\nNew ''Ports & hosts reference'' section documents:\n- every kind extraPortMappings host port (product edges, observability\n  UIs, Kiali, Kafka EXTERNAL) with listen_address and backing Service\n- every in-cluster-only ClusterIP port (OLTP/MCP/reports/frontend/console/\n  ops-agent/Postgres/Kafka CLIENT/otel-collector/istiod)\n- ArgoCD''s deliberate lack of a host port mapping, its port-forward access\n  command, and its internal Services'' ports\n- the shared-selector port-forward pitfall (pod/ vs deploy/ vs svc/)\n\nVerified against live cluster state (kubectl get svc -A) rather than\nguessed from Terraform alone.","tree":{"sha":"db40b740dd51acb68ebeb3dfaeaf7e65d6049ee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/db40b740dd51acb68ebeb3dfaeaf7e65d6049ee9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/a7bd812401ae9aa1e4e41fcf9c47fac4784c920e","verification":{"payload":"tree db40b740dd51acb68ebeb3dfaeaf7e65d6049ee9\nparent 92cba9e9525e34c929131c9aa92d2a4f9fefd914\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789309914 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789309914 -0300\n\ndocs: add a ports & hosts reference covering every app, incl. ArgoCD (#27)\n\nNew ''Ports & hosts reference'' section documents:\n- every kind extraPortMappings host port (product edges, observability\n  UIs, Kiali, Kafka EXTERNAL) with listen_address and backing Service\n- every in-cluster-only ClusterIP port (OLTP/MCP/reports/frontend/console/\n  ops-agent/Postgres/Kafka CLIENT/otel-collector/istiod)\n- ArgoCD''s deliberate lack of a host port mapping, its port-forward access\n  command, and its internal Services'' ports\n- the shared-selector port-forward pitfall (pod/ vs deploy/ vs svc/)\n\nVerified against live cluster state (kubectl get svc -A) rather than\nguessed from Terraform alone.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqprPaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABxoQAC9ECaQo7vt6lEc2KVGbJyRd\nVXsLKzzIpS3vqrtI//VaN12h4vqi5OcFg6vHqS5Fnck9K/v3b73EY5KURDpctkI6\nJvdxqGuu3hOlyiiPmu4HoMmflxySPD51BU60c5sazoeP6d/B/axviL/7Qh/5P/Ms\nnnrQX4Yu45hktEnutupp6istrrg+juSHiiaXhEY0ow6ad0SuMMRp8xw+9OYsPa7L\nwL4yrFWCOLcl9Tv7bGLibWERrd3WS4re4fsJqLjWjJg11coq8Xeg5WUxwu4hmXZp\ny+nL9t9EriYEd7JrIH7Vkd6Zit1YpL5SaDZIWz/uGkdGsQHgS0fMSJh4KqeCCgrN\ns0vINiOy3GYth7cx8Dbw03hOfJHaLoSDxVb8ZeMxy4iT9n3OpnAzczjtbBbCvKUC\nbrOml59HJSYPFgih8qNhfO9dvqRqLnEw4o7R52YB/SDOXWxYy0VwRn05Fd0BT9Cw\n+y6kB+RxeuNcU5MXmNYaMtmLxT5XU2D/ZT/LNoR96uQhXilE7Tm+zGNN/e4dx6g/\n4YbaNfcf/Ml6H1a9dnk/0PNAsBAbi0dYMnCquUmgPdOIUpKVTE57bh8E1UdvuGem\n3NrTPI4YvV5iPMml0NaE81unFCV7CPflj9t1/nvS0gX3rbwgAO03Smsbz2xMCPoT\nyUfOGyw5ofRMFun8GvGr\n=ntkQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T14:31:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscr