r","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/92cba9e9525e34c929131c9aa92d2a4f9fefd914","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDkyY2JhOWU5NTI1ZTM0YzkyOTEzMWM5YWE5MmQyYTRmOWZlZmQ5MTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/e138aeedd77df22ef75e12fd2692e78e21ec9715","sha":"e138aeedd77df22ef75e12fd2692e78e21ec9715","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/e138aeedd77df22ef75e12fd2692e78e21ec9715"}],"sha":"92cba9e9525e34c929131c9aa92d2a4f9fefd914","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/92cba9e9525e34c929131c9aa92d2a4f9fefd914"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/e138aeedd77df22ef75e12fd2692e78e21ec9715/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T00:25:18Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T00:25:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(infra): adopt ArgoCD for GitOps deployment of all 8 service charts (#25)\n\n* feat(infra): install ArgoCD via Helm, auth disabled per fleet posture\n\n* feat(infra): create per-service DB secrets directly, ahead of ArgoCD cutover\n\n* feat(infra): extract service Helm values to a shared local; use existingSecret; add kubectl provider\n\n* feat(infra): pilot ArgoCD Application for order-management with full values parity\n\nVerified live: Synced/Healthy, all resources reconciled, REST healthz OK,\nself-heal reverted a manual replica-count drift within ~1s.\n\n* feat(infra): fan out ArgoCD Applications to all 8 services\n\nVerified live: all 8 Synced/Healthy, all pods Running, all REST healthz\ngreen through Kong.\n\n* feat(infra): switch to content-derived image tags so ArgoCD detects rebuilds\n\nFixes the fleet-documented ''rebuilt image alone does not roll a running\nDeployment'' pitfall as a side effect -- var.image_tag (fixed ''local'') left\nArgo with nothing to diff on a rebuild. Verified live: all 8 services\nrebuilt, rolled, Synced/Healthy, healthz green.\n\n* feat(infra): ArgoCD is now sole owner of service Helm releases\n\nRemoved helm_release.service from Terraform state (terraform state rm,\nnever a helm uninstall) after confirming all 8 Applications were already\nSynced/Healthy, then deleted the resource block. Rewired frontends.tf''s\nweb-gateway and ops-agent.tf''s depends_on from helm_release.service to\nkubectl_manifest.application.\n\nVerified live: terraform plan reports ''No changes. Your infrastructure\nmatches the configuration.'' -- all 8 pods Running, all 8 Applications\nSynced/Healthy, all healthz 200 through Kong.\n\n* docs: document the ArgoCD GitOps workflow for adding/removing a service","tree":{"sha":"6e1e36ca1c89730253110b95821c3faedb7b7d85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/6e1e36ca1c89730253110b95821c3faedb7b7d85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/e138aeedd77df22ef75e12fd2692e78e21ec9715","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e1e36ca1c89730253110b95821c3faedb7b7d85\nparent 9dcf84f7ac2c9b9955a96a26f1e4c90fe6276e4e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789259118 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789259118 -0300\n\nfeat(infra): adopt ArgoCD for GitOps deployment of all 8 service charts (#25)\n\n* feat(infra): install ArgoCD via Helm, auth disabled per fleet posture\n\n* feat(infra): create per-service DB secrets directly, ahead of ArgoCD cutover\n\n* feat(infra): extract service Helm values to a shared local; use existingSecret; add kubectl provider\n\n* feat(infra): pilot ArgoCD Application for order-management with full values parity\n\nVerified live: Synced/Healthy, all resources reconciled, REST healthz OK,\nself-heal reverted a manual replica-count drift within ~1s.\n\n* feat(infra): fan out ArgoCD Applications to all 8 services\n\nVerified live: all 8 Synced/Healthy, all pods Running, all REST healthz\ngreen through Kong.\n\n* feat(infra): switch to content-derived image tags so ArgoCD detects rebuilds\n\nFixes the fleet-documented ''rebuilt image alone does not roll a running\nDeployment'' pitfall as a side effect -- var.image_tag (fixed ''local'') left\nArgo with nothing to diff on a rebuild. Verified live: all 8 services\nrebuilt, rolled, Synced/Healthy, healthz green.\n\n* feat(infra): ArgoCD is now sole owner of service Helm releases\n\nRemoved helm_release.service from Terraform state (terraform state rm,\nnever a helm uninstall) after confirming all 8 Applications were already\nSynced/Healthy, then deleted the resource block. Rewired frontends.tf''s\nweb-gateway and ops-agent.tf''s depends_on from helm_release.service to\nkubectl_manifest.application.\n\nVerified live: terraform plan reports ''No changes. Your infrastructure\nmatches the configuration.'' -- all 8 pods Running, all 8 Applications\nSynced/Healthy, all healthz 200 through Kong.\n\n* docs: document the 