/commits/ba2fc6ce688383a9195222507f105114a342b275"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/670f3ab8140d5185cb3df0fe3a815b2289b19aeb","sha":"670f3ab8140d5185cb3df0fe3a815b2289b19aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/670f3ab8140d5185cb3df0fe3a815b2289b19aeb"}],"sha":"872432cfbda535632824eedda8c71c18f55c85c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/872432cfbda535632824eedda8c71c18f55c85c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/670f3ab8140d5185cb3df0fe3a815b2289b19aeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T17:41:35Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T17:41:35Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"fix(infra): flip LABOR_PERFORMANCE_MODE to kafka-cache; wire second-wave MCP upstreams\n\nFound live while verifying the labor-utilization/idleness feature\n(labor-performance PR #44, workforce-management PR #66, warehouse-ops-\nagent PR #45): two real infra gaps predating and blocking those PRs''\nnew behaviour from ever reaching a running cluster.\n\n1. terraform/locals.tf: workforce-management''s LABOR_PERFORMANCE_MODE\n   was still \"http\" despite workforce-management ADR-0019 (merged\n   2026-09-11, PR #65) having already shipped the kafka-cache adapter.\n   The cluster was therefore never actually exercising the event-fed\n   cache -- including its new idle-share tracking (ADR 0020) -- no\n   matter how green that PR''s CI was. Flipped to \"kafka-cache\";\n   LABOR_PERFORMANCE_BASE_URL kept as the documented rollback value.\n\n2. terraform/ops-agent.tf: the upstreams map only ever wired the\n   original five MCP endpoints. order-management, labor-performance,\n   and process-path-management got outbound mcpclient adapters in\n   warehouse-ops-agent PR #44, and labor-performance specifically\n   graduated to actually CONSUMED by FlowBalanceAdvisory in PR #45\n   (ADR 0008) -- but with no endpoint wired here, cfg.LaborPerformance\n   .Endpoint was always empty in any real deploy, so the new\n   correlation logic could build the client but never reach a live\n   MCP server. Companion chart-side fix in warehouse-ops-agent PR #46\n   (this repo''s upstreams.* values + deployment.yaml env vars) is a\n   prerequisite this Terraform change depends on -- already merged.\n\nVerified live in the cluster, in order:\n- terraform apply (after pulling the three services'' develop HEADs and\n  the warehouse-ops-agent chart fix), then the mandatory\n  kubectl rollout restart for all 4 affected deployments (rebuilt\n  images alone never roll a Deployment pinned to image.tag=\"local\",\n  IfNotPresent -- documented fleet pitfall).\n- Drove a real associate through fulfillment-execution (claim, complete,\n  ~92s deliberate idle gap, claim, complete) and confirmed\n  GET /associates/{id}/utilization on labor-performance reflects it:\n  idleSeconds=93, taskSeconds=5, utilizationPct~4.7","tree":{"sha":"b07d9bd0860efa9167d6592dcaf769e8ec5cb0ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/b07d9bd0860efa9167d6592dcaf769e8ec5cb0ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/670f3ab8140d5185cb3df0fe3a815b2289b19aeb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/670f3ab8140d5185cb3df0fe3a815b2289b19aeb","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDY3MGYzYWI4MTQwZDUxODVjYjNkZjBmZTNhODE1YjIyODliMTlhZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/ba2fc6ce688383a9195222507f105114a342b275","sha":"ba2fc6ce688383a9195222507f105114a342b275","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/ba2fc6ce688383a9195222507f105114a342b275"}],"sha":"670f3ab8140d5185cb3df0fe3a815b2289b19aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/670f3ab8140d5185cb3df0fe3a815b2289b19aeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/ba2fc6ce688383a9195222507f105114a342b275/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T06:14:52Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T06:14:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(analytics): deploy process-path-management''s analytics data product (#19)\n\nFleet-wide bounded-context wiring plan, Phase 5: analytics data products\n7/8 -> 8/8. process-path-management shipped its own projector + reports\nbinaries, a warehouse.process-path-management.analytics topic, and a\n\"Process Path Catalogue Growth & Change\" report bucketed by day\n(process-path-management#28).\n\nAdds it to analytics_services; every downstream local\n(analytics_db_info, analytics_service_passwords, analytics_database_urls)\nand services.tf''s `contains(local.analytics_services, each.key)` gate\nalready derive from this single set, so no other Terraform file needed a\nchange.\n\nVerified live in the warehouse kind cluster: all 3 new pods\n(mcp/projector/reports) Running, GET /healthz -> 200, GET\n/reports/catalogue-growth/freshness -> {\"lagSeconds\":0} (projector caught\nup), GET /reports/catalogue-growth with a date range -> valid empty\nresult (no historical events replayed onto the brand-new analytics topic\nyet, expected).\n\nNote: this cluster''s Postgres already had data (initdb only runs once\nagainst an empty data directory), so adding a new analytics_services\nentry does not retroactively create its role/database. Ran the\nequivalent CREATE ROLE / CREATE DATABASE / REVOKE / GRANT statements\nmanually against the live postgres-postgresql-0 pod, mirroring\ntemplates/init-databases.sql.tftpl''s analytics_services loop body\nexactly, before the projector could start successfully (first attempt\ncrash-looped with \"password authentication failed\" until this was done).","tree":{"sha":"c13f2da13a1cb6b9ae8e68c7a37dba407e81a67f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/c13f2da13a1cb6b9ae8e68c7a37dba407e81a67f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/ba2fc6ce688383a9195222507f105114a342b275","verification":{"payload":"tree c13f2da13a1cb6b9ae8e68c7a37dba407e81a67f\nparent caee475e645a5df6b641b1b2588fb5b1d552a432\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789107292 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789107292 -0300\n\nfeat(analytics): deploy process-path-management''s analytics data product (#19)\n\nFleet-wide bounded-context wiring plan, Phase 5: analytics data products\n7/8 -> 8/8. process-path-management shipped its own projector + reports\nbinaries, a warehouse.process-path-management.analytics topic, and a\n\"Process Path Catalogue Growth & Change\" report bucketed by day\n(process-path-management#28).\n\nAdds it to analytics_services; every downstream local\n(analytics_db_info, analytics_service_passwords, analytics_database_urls)\nand services.tf''s `contains(local.analytics_services, each.key)` gate\nalready derive from this single set, so no other Terraform file needed a\nchange.\n\nVerified live in the warehouse kind cluster: all 3 new pods\n(mcp/projector/reports) Running, GET /healthz -> 200, GET\n/reports/catalogue-growth/freshness -> {\"lagSeconds\":0} (projector caught\nup), GET /reports/catalogue-growth with a date range -> valid empty\nresult (no historical events replayed onto the brand-new analytics topic\nyet, expected).\n\nNote: this cluster''s Postgres already had data (initdb only runs once\nagainst an empty data directory), so adding a new analytics_services\nentry does not retroactively create its role/database. Ran the\nequivalent CREATE ROLE / CREATE DATABASE / REVOKE / GRANT statements\nmanually against the live postgres-postgresql-0 pod, mirroring\ntemplates/init-databases.sql.tftpl''s analytics_services loop body\nexactly, before the projector could start successfully (first attempt\ncrash-looped with \"password authentication failed\" until this was done).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo5xcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxTwQAElOTcaAgjCFb/Hf7+/NqMCa\nxB7NNbQSEHuGClGuKq1NlD7JfBNAky7ZaV5mKga7MBbNzCaSXD1QIjniSzLS4I3T\nxyHIR2Rnahc3kMhgXPWmdjk7Sy6s0fBjj7PaFV4bVGbHsd/47NfH9P1qZWxrId7O\n472EUOM0hdP5Eg6lsavpTRNJKcNvge9wWgwvDdZyqsYW6dAU0BnVlyV44aM9LdoZ\nXk4ISQywBMVJ/KwVlZJVHyuZp+o+QpJ3mR+DAT0/VQWapFZA4t3AiVVZ5vXKdXn8\n6t8QgX/Rn5lcKZCWMSfAtlu8gp1P2LGOmnOOLgC/fVl1fHZGofa/GfFxuhqNWFX0\noca+tkWeLcfufq4lM4QPLvG2u4CADgLP8JDLy28jHdZTaZearRxVJaQQ8FMMvXlf\nPIBBC5Pl8b0pZUZTLgilrKfdXyQuHG7PWIVMxdOvpKSMEI3dcfZSPCMgH/i2sx9Q\nS+k4TZMgkw5elqzeTNIunoaF8aKeQUNIKYJqdsj3nt8YWj5QS5HSOcTGE8fRlc0H\n4y7pbivJgxT14YwWLGiATbDzfmzRB4qa025YnMfwS0YD4xUUlb1NHPKp2i4t28ji\n8aTmv0X3yZiLHvkHmBV5M/vAV8U8t2T6IpSorKuZliVrDar3Q50hteMPaphnIVL8\ncmn73zZfmEm5OEDlBZOP\n=0pvA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T06:14:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v