pi.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/caee475e645a5df6b641b1b2588fb5b1d552a432/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T03:14:45Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T03:14:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp): deploy MCP servers for order-management, labor-performance, process-path-management (#18)\n\nFleet-wide bounded-context wiring plan, Phase 1: MCP surface 5/9 -> 8/9.\n\norder-management and labor-performance already shipped a cmd/mcp binary\nbut had no chart templates to deploy it. process-path-management had no\nMCP server at all -- both the Go adapter and its chart templates were\nbuilt as part of this same wiring pass (two read-only tools:\nget_process_path, list_process_paths).\n\nAdds all three to mcp_services so services.tf''s existing\n`contains(local.mcp_services, each.key)` gate picks them up with no\nfurther Terraform change needed. mcp_endpoint''s for-comprehension over\nmcp_services also now covers all three automatically.\n\nVerified live in the warehouse kind cluster after apply +\nkubectl rollout restart (image tag \"local\" never rolls a Deployment on\nits own): all three -mcp pods Running, each answered a real MCP\ninitialize handshake over the wire, and process-path-management''s\nlist_process_paths tool returned real catalogue data from Postgres\n(PICK/PACK/REBIN/SLAM/STAGE/WRAP plus historical test entries).\n\nNote: process-path-management''s Dockerfile initially lacked a build/copy\nstep for cmd/mcp (CrashLoopBackOff: exec: /app/mcp: no such file or\ndirectory) -- fixed separately in that repo''s own PR #27 before this\napply succeeded cleanly.","tree":{"sha":"46843208e061b679fefceeb1bcf3d9e0151c6fc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/46843208e061b679fefceeb1bcf3d9e0151c6fc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/caee475e645a5df6b641b1b2588fb5b1d552a432","verification":{"payload":"tree 46843208e061b679fefceeb1bcf3d9e0151c6fc1\nparent 0bfcecb6c07a1b79ffcd10233ffd617f5a107c2e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789096485 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789096485 -0300\n\nfeat(mcp): deploy MCP servers for order-management, labor-performance, process-path-management (#18)\n\nFleet-wide bounded-context wiring plan, Phase 1: MCP surface 5/9 -> 8/9.\n\norder-management and labor-performance already shipped a cmd/mcp binary\nbut had no chart templates to deploy it. process-path-management had no\nMCP server at all -- both the Go adapter and its chart templates were\nbuilt as part of this same wiring pass (two read-only tools:\nget_process_path, list_process_paths).\n\nAdds all three to mcp_services so services.tf''s existing\n`contains(local.mcp_services, each.key)` gate picks them up with no\nfurther Terraform change needed. mcp_endpoint''s for-comprehension over\nmcp_services also now covers all three automatically.\n\nVerified live in the warehouse kind cluster after apply +\nkubectl rollout restart (image tag \"local\" never rolls a Deployment on\nits own): all three -mcp pods Running, each answered a real MCP\ninitialize handshake over the wire, and process-path-management''s\nlist_process_paths tool returned real catalogue data from Postgres\n(PICK/PACK/REBIN/SLAM/STAGE/WRAP plus historical test entries).\n\nNote: process-path-management''s Dockerfile initially lacked a build/copy\nstep for cmd/mcp (CrashLoopBackOff: exec: /app/mcp: no such file or\ndirectory) -- fixed separately in that repo''s own PR #27 before this\napply succeeded cleanly.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo3IlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuF0QAE0EY0F7n3vDxJERi21dt62K\nYBif0Sliwo1GixSYYoGDdppWBef4DqJdZqoX2x94lqjiP/QyvST0xi6d3HIcvqe+\nDJyaII/oHyEUtM8jdvgxrZGio64LLVZzndYla3Gaa3gzJrUAxyBLcV9TUFgBeicx\ny/kxKxuRLQ2JKWJQ4RqREVszM6qG76l7xbhRfYfvrSZXiHJu+JWqKtWnigWDmDLc\nYTHqQ0hRdrIsvyLxg6HPyrNZ13lP8BWDIc6YUD+3a+2ayRyqPCj8j3XyOeIb1FO+\niMHGHhL0kZhEanVyAcjGrFhzhpj5gJdw/tV6FajsDethnvsacU+3VBhSp5Ud0pm4\nTOlRmAYwBb/uTGWplhdqiTtpKnv00MO8FtPQjp7Ua6zIkD4Hooyf0D6ls7OUFz03\nZGJPeeJnpon97BS1bXCEl9POh7DcuLfBsTLjC6cy55YVrvu1Tc6LoEVx1Rqv/9+n\nRnryySYTdgEwda+d6Vl7oRWsEOL40BUPPVhj4yEdmwSg/T5TXgSxBAbjm1dDQB7q\nSnZ55gBdfYYB44cSMtvzXyT22OPorOJ0OMcG4h93gGR0kgvEzx1ePSdMC9jIzWyO\nr/OPUCdSFjd6/rstpX9cVSjK4FjkWyZEq+msU1+7aa+A7QaII3h7EcI6R/RjbELf\nWxHiZhpjDv0qQ1BI3hZ7\n=I7Yp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T03:14:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/caee475e645a5df6b641b1b2588fb5b1d552a432","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKGNhZWU0NzVlNjQ1YTVkZjZiNjQxYjFiMjU4OGZiNWIxZDU1MmE0MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/0bfcecb6c07a1b79ffcd10233ffd617f5a107c2e","sha":"0bfcecb6c07a1b79ffcd10233ffd617f5a107c2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/0bfcecb6c07a1b79ffcd10233ffd617f5a107c2e"}],"sha":"caee475e645a5df6b641b1b2588fb5b1d552a432","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/caee475e645a5df6b641b1b2588fb5b1d552a432"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/0bfcecb6c07a1b79ffcd10233ffd617f5a107c2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T00:42:28Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T00:42:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: wire order-management to the process-path Kafka catalogue (#17)\n\nAdds var.deploy_order_management_path_catalogue_kafka (default true,\nflipped after live verification below) which injects\nPATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE=kafka via order-management''s chart extraEnv.\nIndependent of var.deploy_process_path_kafka_source above: order-\nmanagement is a NEW consumer of process-path-management''s Kafka topic\n(order-management ADR-0013 / PR claudioed/order-management#45), not a\nfile-to-kafka cutover like fulfillment-execution/wes-work-planning/\nworkforce-management, so it gets its own single-service ternary rather\nthan joining their shared flag. KAFKA_BROKERS needs no separate wiring:\norder-management''s helm-values already sets config.eventPublisher=kafka\nunconditionally, so the chart already renders it regardless of this\nflag.\n\nRolled out against the live cluster, not just planned:\n- order-management''s local checkout was stale (11 commits behind\n  origin/develop, on the wrong branch) -- fast-forwarded to develop\n  before any apply, per this fleet''s \"Terraform builds from the local\n  sibling checkout\" pitfall. Same fast-forward applied to every other\n  service repo for hygiene.\n- Rebuilt+redeployed order-management with the flag still false (a\n  same-image, zero-config-change apply) first, confirmed 201 Created\n  intake behavior unchanged and the pod''s own log explicitly said\n  \"process-path catalogue source not configured; ReceiveOrder will skip\n  path validation\" -- proving the new code path defaults to a true no-op.\n- Flipped the flag to true, re-applied (scoped to\n  helm_release.service[\"order-management\"] -- 0 rebuild, 1 chart config\n  change as planned), `kubectl rollout restart` (image tag \"local\" +\n  IfNotPresent never auto-rolls, per this fleet''s known pitfall).\n- The new pod hit this fleet''s known, pre-existing \"every pod restarts\n  once at rollout\" issue harder than usual (6 restarts before settling,\n  vs. the documented single restart) -- confirmed via logs this is the\n  same \"connection reset by peer\" Postgres-dial-timing issue already\n  tracked as OPEN in the fleet skill, NOT caused by the kafkacatalog\n  consumer (its own logs show it started, ran, and reached Ready cleanly\n  every time; the crashes were all pre-database-connection).\n- Verified for real once stable: the pod''s startup log shows\n  \"process-path catalogue source configured\" / source=kafka and the\n  readiness wait completing; POST /orders against the live pod returns\n  201 with pathId=pick (PICK being genuinely ACTIVE in\n  process-path-management''s live catalogue); restart count stayed flat\n  across all probe traffic (no crash from the new validation path).\n- The FULL discriminating probe (accept -> deactivate -> confirm 400 ->\n  reactivate) was NOT run against a real path: order-management''s v1\n  PathSelectionPolicy always resolves every line to \"pick\" (attribute-\n  driven routing is an explicit, documented later phase), so the only\n  candidate for that probe is PICK itself -- and process-path-\n  management''s domain rule makes deactivation PERMANENT (a deactivated\n  path id can never be redefined), and PICK is live-depended-on by\n  wes-work-planning, fulfillment-execution, AND workforce-management\n  right now. Deliberately not risking that for a probe. A disposable\n  throwaway path (OMPROBE) was defined and cleanly deleted instead, to\n  confirm PPM''s define/list/delete cycle itself works end-to-end, but it\n  could not exercise order-management''s OWN rejection path for the\n  reason above. Revisit once order-management''s PathSelectionPolicy can\n  resolve to more than one path.","tree":{"sha":"2157863bee59f6eb83fb2aec2c097821c37b18d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/2157863bee59f6eb83fb2aec2c097821c37b18d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/0bfcecb6c07a1b79ffcd10233ffd617f5a107c2e","verification":{"payload":"tree 2157863bee59f6eb83fb2aec2c097821c37b18d8\nparent 262e75864625012003737985e81295fdf6408c8c\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1789087348 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789087348 -0300\n\nfeat: wire order-management to the process-path Kafka catalogue (#17)\n\nAdds var.deploy_order_management_path_catalogue_kafka (default true,\nflipped after live verification below) which injects\nPATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE=kafka via order-management''s chart extraEnv.\nIndependent of var.deploy_process_path_kafka_source above: order-\nmanagement is a NEW consumer of process-path-management''s Kafka topic\n(order-management ADR-0013 / PR claudioed/order-management#45), not a\nfile-to-kafka cutover like fulfillment-execution/wes-work-planning/\nworkforce-management, so it gets its own single-service ternary rather\nthan joining their shared flag. KAFKA_BROKERS needs no separate wiring:\norder-management''s helm-values already sets config.eventPublisher=kafka\nunconditionally, so the chart already renders it regardless of this\nflag.\n\nRolled out against the live cluster, not just planned:\n- order-management''s local checkout was stale (11 commits behind\n  origin/develop, on the wrong branch) -- fast-forwarded to develop\n  before any apply, per this fleet''s \"Terraform builds from the local\n  sibling checkout\" pitfall. Same fast-forward applied to every other\n  service repo for hygiene.\n- Rebuilt+redeployed order-management with the flag still false (a\n  same-image, zero-config-change apply) first, confirmed 201 Created\n  intake behavior unchanged and the pod''s own log explicitly said\n  \"process-path catalogue source not configured; ReceiveOrder will skip\n  path validation\" -- proving the new code path defaults to a true no-op.\n- Flipped the flag to true, re-applied (scoped to\n  helm_release.service[\"order-management\"] -- 0 rebuild, 1 chart config\n  change as planned), `kubectl rollout restart` (image tag \"local\" +\n  IfNotPresent never auto-rolls, per this fleet''s known pitfall).\n- The new pod hit this fleet''s known, pre-existing \"every pod restarts\n  once at rollout\" issue harder than usual (6 restarts before settling,\n  vs. the documented single restart) -- confirmed via logs this is the\n  same \"connection reset by peer\" Postgres-dial-timing issue already\n  tracked as OPEN in the fleet skill, NOT caused by the kafkacatalog\n  consumer (its own logs show it started, ran, and reached Ready cleanly\n  every time; the crashes were all pre-database-connection).\n- Verified for real once stable: the pod''s startup log shows\n  \"process-path catalogue source configured\" / source=kafka and the\n  readiness wait completing; POST /orders against the live pod returns\n  201 with pathId=pick (PICK being genuinely ACTIVE in\n  process-path-management''s live catalogue); restart count stayed flat\n  across all probe traffic (no crash from the new validation path).\n- The FULL discriminating probe (accept -> deactivate -> confirm 400 ->\n  reactivate) was NOT run against a real path: order-management''s v1\n  PathSelectionPolicy always resolves every line to \"pick\" (attribute-\n  driven routing is an explicit, documented later phase), so the only\n  candidate for that probe is PICK itself -- and process-path-\n  management''s domain rule makes deactivation PERMANENT (a deactivated\n  path id can never be redefined), and PICK is live-depended-on by\n  wes-work-planning, fulfillment-execution, AND workforce-management\n  right now. Deliberately not risking that for a probe. A disposable\n  throwaway path (OMPROBE) was defined and cleanly deleted instead, to\n  confirm PPM''s define/list/delete cycle itself works end-to-end, but it\n  could not exercise order-management''s OWN rejection path for the\n  reason above. Revisit once order-management''s PathSelectionPolicy can\n  resolve to more than one path.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo050CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1GYQAB2oAMig6jkPz98NyliYIXmV\n/Jz+UpKgo5LkKV