s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/cdd6cc5b112979c01f0970915092f003ed6e9fed","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKGNkZDZjYzViMTEyOTc5YzAxZjA5NzA5MTUwOTJmMDAzZWQ2ZTlmZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/c4c359547dafaf4bab9f5dd94b280e88f0c78033","sha":"c4c359547dafaf4bab9f5dd94b280e88f0c78033","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/c4c359547dafaf4bab9f5dd94b280e88f0c78033"}],"sha":"cdd6cc5b112979c01f0970915092f003ed6e9fed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/cdd6cc5b112979c01f0970915092f003ed6e9fed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/c4c359547dafaf4bab9f5dd94b280e88f0c78033/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T22:55:41Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T22:55:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(infra): deploy the five MCP servers and wire them into warehouse-ops-agent (#14)\n\nBefore this, no MCP server existed in the cluster (ops-agent.tf said so:\nevery *_MCP_ENDPOINT was deliberately empty because no image built\ncmd/mcp). Each context''s own feature/mcp-deployment PR (FE #68, WES #56,\nINV #55, WFM #55, FL #54, all merged 2026-09-07) made the binary and an\n`mcp.*` chart block available; this PR turns them on.\n\n- terraform/mcp.tf: local.mcp_services, one random read key and one\n  read-write key per context (40 chars, URL-safe), local.mcp_endpoint\n  (`http://<svc>-mcp.<ns>.svc.cluster.local:8090/mcp`).\n- services.tf: `mcp = {enabled, readKey, readWriteKey}` merge entry for\n  those five charts, same-key-set on both ternary branches.\n- ops-agent.tf: `upstreams.*.endpoint` and `credentials.*ReadKey` wired\n  from the same keys (read key only -- the agent''s v1 posture is\n  read-only); stale \"deliberately left UNSET\" header replaced.\n- variables.tf: `deploy_mcp_servers` (default true; false is the rollback,\n  which removes the -mcp workloads and empties the agent''s endpoints).\n\nVerified live: five `<svc>-mcp` pods Running, `/healthz` 200, `POST /mcp`\nwithout a bearer 401, `tools/list` with the provisioned read key returns\neach context''s curated tools (4-5 each); ops-agent startup logs\n`*_endpoint_configured: true` for all five and `GET /flow-balance/pick`\nreturns a decision with WES + FE evidence in 32 ms.","tree":{"sha":"63f0cc81ebedc18c5fc4a9763e940a67e76fd5fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/63f0cc81ebedc18c5fc4a9763e940a67e76fd5fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/c4c359547dafaf4bab9f5dd94b280e88f0c78033","verification":{"payload":"tree 63f0cc81ebedc18c5fc4a9763e940a67e76fd5fe\nparent 79f4ca34d1e96e6f30cae6f870e114a5b3b66159\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788821741 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788821741 -0300\n\nfeat(infra): deploy the five MCP servers and wire them into warehouse-ops-agent (#14)\n\nBefore this, no MCP server existed in the cluster (ops-agent.tf said so:\nevery *_MCP_ENDPOINT was deliberately empty because no image built\ncmd/mcp). Each context''s own feature/mcp-deployment PR (FE #68, WES #56,\nINV #55, WFM #55, FL #54, all merged 2026-09-07) made the binary and an\n`mcp.*` chart block available; this PR turns them on.\n\n- terraform/mcp.tf: local.mcp_services, one random read key and one\n  read-write key per context (40 chars, URL-safe), local.mcp_endpoint\n  (`http://<svc>-mcp.<ns>.svc.cluster.local:8090/mcp`).\n- services.tf: `mcp = {enabled, readKey, readWriteKey}` merge entry for\n  those five charts, same-key-set on both ternary branches.\n- ops-agent.tf: `upstreams.*.endpoint` and `credentials.*ReadKey` wired\n  from the same keys (read key only -- the agent''s v1 posture is\n  read-only); stale \"deliberately left UNSET\" header replaced.\n- variables.tf: `deploy_mcp_servers` (default true; false is the rollback,\n  which removes the -mcp workloads and empties the agent''s endpoints).\n\nVerified live: five `<svc>-mcp` pods Running, `/healthz` 200, `POST /mcp`\nwithout a bearer 401, `tools/list` with the provisioned read key returns\neach context''s curated tools (4-5 each); ops-agent startup logs\n`*_endpoint_configured: true` for all five and `GET /flow-balance/pick`\nreturns a decision with WES + FE evidence in 32 ms.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn0DtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeikQABmkn3uOvWJJgcARfNNvgKkF\nGITaV8vqaN2enqEUGR