sha":"79f4ca34d1e96e6f30cae6f870e114a5b3b66159","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/79f4ca34d1e96e6f30cae6f870e114a5b3b66159"}],"sha":"c4c359547dafaf4bab9f5dd94b280e88f0c78033","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/c4c359547dafaf4bab9f5dd94b280e88f0c78033"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/79f4ca34d1e96e6f30cae6f870e114a5b3b66159/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T16:16:03Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T16:16:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(infra): wire the fleet''s synchronous HTTP edges and labor-performance''s publisher (#13)\n\nFound while verifying the outbox rollout live: every consumer binary in the\ncluster was running its *_MODE default (\"permissive\"), because nothing in\nwarehouse-infra ever set the modes or the supplier base URLs:\n\n- workforce-management INSTALLED_CAPACITY_MODE=permissive is fail-LOUD\n  (its ADR-0014): every POST /shift-plans returned 503 in the cluster.\n- wes-work-planning / fulfillment-execution PRODUCT_CLASSIFICATION_MODE\n  =permissive is fail-open: WorkReleased never carried hazmat/fragile hints.\n- workforce-management LABOR_PERFORMANCE_MODE=permissive: ProposePathPlan\n  always proposed 0 heads.\n- labor-performance''s chart never renders EVENT_PUBLISHER, so it ran the\n  log publisher; warehouse.labor-performance.analytics had offset 0 --\n  its projector/reports pair had never received an event.\n\nAdds local.sync_edge_env (consumer -> extraEnv list) and folds it into the\ncomputed extraEnv in services.tf. It has to live there: services.tf sets\nextraEnv for every service and that layer overrides helm-values/*.yaml,\nso an extraEnv entry in a values file is silently dropped (documented on\nthe local).\n\nVerified after apply + rollout: all four pods log mode=http / outbox;\nPOST /shift-plans now reaches fulfillment-execution (409 on the capacity\ninvariant instead of 503); a TaskCompleted driven through FE produced\nfulfillment.events 15->16 and labor-performance.analytics 0->1.","tree":{"sha":"121195ce7703b94d638b1976aba2f550d791e1a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/121195ce7703b94d638b1976aba2f550d791e1a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/79f4ca34d1e96e6f30cae6f870e114a5b3b66159","verification":{"payload":"tree 121195ce7703b94d638b1976aba2f550d791e1a4\nparent 67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788797763 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788797763 -0300\n\nfix(infra): wire the fleet''s synchronous HTTP edges and labor-performance''s publisher (#13)\n\nFound while verifying the outbox rollout live: every consumer binary in the\ncluster was running its *_MODE default (\"permissive\"), because nothing in\nwarehouse-infra ever set the modes or the supplier base URLs:\n\n- workforce-management INSTALLED_CAPACITY_MODE=permissive is fail-LOUD\n  (its ADR-0014): every POST /shift-plans returned 503 in the cluster.\n- wes-work-planning / fulfillment-execution PRODUCT_CLASSIFICATION_MODE\n  =permissive is fail-open: WorkReleased never carried hazmat/fragile hints.\n- workforce-management LABOR_PERFORMANCE_MODE=permissive: ProposePathPlan\n  always proposed 0 heads.\n- labor-performance''s chart never renders EVENT_PUBLISHER, so it ran the\n  log publisher; warehouse.labor-performance.analytics had offset 0 --\n  its projector/reports pair had never received an event.\n\nAdds local.sync_edge_env (consumer -> extraEnv list) and folds it into the\ncomputed extraEnv in services.tf. It has to live there: services.tf sets\nextraEnv for every service and that layer overrides helm-values/*.yaml,\nso an extraEnv entry in a values file is silently dropped (documented on\nthe local).\n\nVerified after apply + rollout: all four pods log mode=http / outbox;\nPOST /shift-plans now reaches fulfillment-execution (409 on the capacity\ninvariant instead of 503); a TaskCompleted driven through FE produced\nfulfillment.events 15->16 and labor-performance.analytics 0->1.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnuNDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0iMQAK4LqWQfXvoOUhjwVuBCFKfe\nUfYGPuQboH0VIQ7pMMVUCuabyCz2LjhzYieZPn1gi7r5c3ZxDGsv3HOYAF+CM6J5\nWGIEx2EAwouDsyLnXZXAsu0bMZ8cpyVxq5IyxU57F4+Unx5T1L1QFi/XLSuTkXIG\nyNgYSfy7WIh8Ec/1B29PiM87x0LOKVUOshMEnsBDvbBPP+ynyFtTyEW8ppDxOPJ4\nB24jwqmckzLGUzYxyqzQFrze6K87TciK8Nn8R9jQi3cvlRU43qUMFH9gwJPRqBTO\n7zxFchbzQ642ltz1vt0nJmo3oXzsn0nexSgPQ2FBKu4qcFue9LFScI4warSg3hVC\nE3Y3hYlJnAQ4x/zTSaZ7jv3ceYbsvLtCm3Rmi9m5tsUq9aX5uGvV3lqIKXvC3AeA\nwnsWqExw5J6kg/JX3iwLUieBnL8hyjWvNoPfC1PLOWnII89mKlWlJFEqefH8wOde\n+t4seWKBLHVYeVVCYAznjeRADFNnBKX5qaGO9Gc6+V1jdW5BEAR9ueCrVZkcpFDv\nB+UnUfi07Mwf+0fvCNapbXmcGSn97U3BfxF+7PKQSrDMQH26ecaw1b/+B4BTf2qS\nhH28EqFfC1G8w5oNSTyfmCHqI2BpWtYIJhDH2+Fd1KOta/pzI87GDYLVeVW9O4cf\ncMTemJMSaZGXg4Z4PkRS\n=7xS6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T16:16:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/79f4ca34d1e96e6f30cae6f870e114a5b3b66159","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDc5ZjRjYTM0ZDFlOTZlNmYzMGNhZTZmODcwZTExNGE1YjNiNjYxNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3","sha":"67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3"}],"sha":"79f4ca34d1e96e6f30cae6f870e114a5b3b66159","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/79f4ca34d1e96e6f30cae6f870e114a5b3b66159"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T04:34:49Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T04:34:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(infra): default both event-integration flags to true after the 2026-09-06 cutover (#12)\n\ndeploy_process_path_kafka_source and deploy_facility_events_integration\nwere flipped on the live cluster via TF_VAR overrides; the code defaults\nstill said false, so a plain ''terraform apply'' would have silently rolled\nthe fleet back to the static YAML catalogue and the sync HTTP location\nlookup. Make the code match reality and freeze sortable-fc.yaml as a\nrollback-only payload.\n\nterraform plan against the running cluster: No changes.","tree":{"sha":"c382b1edc6fa86e8162d9f6189083ae5f4d690c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/c382b1edc6fa86e8162d9f6189083ae5f4d690c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3","verification":{"payload":"tree c382b1edc6fa86e8162d9f6189083ae5f4d690c4\nparent 6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788755689 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788755689 -0300\n\nfeat(infra): default both event-integration flags to true after the 2026-09-06 cutover (#12)\n\ndeploy_process_path_kafka_source and deploy_facility_events_integration\nwere flipped on the live cluster via TF_VAR overrides; the code defaults\nstill said false, so a plain ''terraform apply'' would have silently rolled\nthe fleet back to the static YAML catalogue and the sync HTTP location\nlookup. Make the code match reality and freeze sortable-fc.yaml as a\nrollback-only payload.\n\nterraform plan against the running cluster: No changes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnj7pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwmoQAEW4HCjGKN5OP/Cygcv0s+RX\n9pbBij55VbR43j7/1VysB3/CpozsGeu5cWDzFbJnKCo9Ot7kPs+ILv+xmEYs5vGW\ngJK5ssBv8LVBXtxj+qTEeeEmEpYyqLAAjJBX2iv1irRimY5n+CZw5A4+TgACzQkH\nXEO9EJ2maZo3hQ+wFuE/QmhI+2x+RFRSNHtGv1NrbU5INMfuAxbPBz03qgwEbScN\nrWU9ihflNAlvZELNAkpwL/4ZMm4s13aquCTrq5hdd+P3ovhcKBXymiDzkcGGIKz3\ngBNTnXzEwoD75cL0PQ1dUYmB1r8ptT89IG3rvOOk1PulOWV8ez7VJqG45dtEZLWc\n4Pdqgzgg/6dOku3iE1Bj2Vunz3FyM9OExGikmjHmXA1Y5uYOC8QlEJ1kKkPudhhk\nUvkJ38HGYft5k/O2UcnPy2m6htS/s+M4SU2vuggH4fKe+iRDy4K1D/QahYKXuCHy\nBO1ALw1RhKDNOODm8FuWaSrX26vFGWsW/t9AqCBtOnY13Etd4FXRhDqvewYSoFrn\nbB6d7WYy21CSCLtuv6ELsV3uH3UkImErXBGJXMDywdR5rvguOiMDocaLlUW21Qaj\nAXM+4dS99JsMQySKDUCfjaaCSjIquh8sXq8Y+0S6XOwf4bB0xIGQ/PZS5roqs+DI\nGXGYI7YLHECf6o5546Uj\n=NPyW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T04:34:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDY3YzYwNDhjNDc1MThlMTliZTg3YTQ4MDYyODY2MTdhMzgwYjQwZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2","sha":"6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2"}],"sha":"67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/67c6048c47518e19be87a4806286617a380b40f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T23:15:57Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T23:15:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(facility): opt-in facility-layout -> inventory-storage event integration (#11)\n\ninventory-storage can now source location classifications from\nfacility-layout''s Kafka topic (warehouse.facility.events) instead of\ncalling that service synchronously over HTTP on every stow -- see\ninventory-storage''s ADR 0013 for the decision record and the adapter that\nimplements it.\n\nNothing in this repo enabled that yet, and it could not simply be turned on\nfrom the consumer side: facility-layout''s chart defaults\nconfig.eventPublisher to \"log\" (Postgres outbox only), so the\nwarehouse.facility.events topic did not exist at all in the cluster. A\nconsumer pointed at it would have come up ready with an empty cache and\nfailed open on every lookup.\n\nAdds var.deploy_facility_events_integration (default false, a pure no-op)\nwhich flips BOTH sides of the integration together, mirroring the existing\nvar.deploy_process_path_kafka_source pattern and for the same reason -- a\npublisher with no consumer, or a consumer whose topic is never written, are\nboth silently broken states:\n\n  * facility-layout: config.eventPublisher \"log\" -> \"kafka\" and\n    kafka.enabled=true, so the chart renders KAFKA_BROKERS and the service\n    actually publishes its Published Language.\n\n  * inventory-storage: LOCATION_LOOKUP_MODE=kafka via the chart''s own\n    extraEnv. Its chart already sets kafka.enabled (it publishes its own\n    integration events), so KAFKA_BROKERS is already present -- which the\n    consumer requires, and whose absence fails startup loudly rather than\n    degrading silently.\n\nThe two services are kept as separate merge entries rather than one block\nbecause they need different keys (a publisher switch vs a consumer-mode env\nvar). Both branches of the inventory-storage ternary declare the same key\nset, per the \"Inconsistent conditional result types\" rule the process-path\nblock above it already documents.\n\nDocumented in variables.tf: because a fresh consumer replays from the\nearliest offset, facility-layout events that predate the publisher flip live\nonly in that service''s Postgres outbox and will never reach the topic. On a\ncluster with existing layout data the layout must be re-registered or\nre-imported after flipping, or the cache is partial -- which is a fail-open\nstate (lookups report Known=false and stows are waved through unclassified),\nnot a hard failure.\n\nterraform validate passes and a plan against the live cluster state confirms\nthe flag produces exactly the two intended changes and nothing else.\nRollback is pure configuration: set it false and re-apply.","tree":{"sha":"37ea179d4797e2aa0f9c20c2dc982c6408062bc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/37ea179d4797e2aa0f9c20c2dc982c6408062bc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2","verification":{"payload":"tree 37ea179d4797e2aa0f9c20c2dc982c6408062bc0\nparent 021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788736557 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788736557 -0300\n\nfeat(facility): opt-in facility-layout -> inventory-storage event integration (#11)\n\ninventory-storage can now source location classifications from\nfacility-layout''s Kafka topic (warehouse.facility.events) instead of\ncalling that service synchronously over HTTP on every stow -- see\ninventory-storage''s ADR 0013 for the decision record and the adapter that\nimplements it.\n\nNothing in this repo enabled that yet, and it could not simply be turned on\nfrom the consumer side: facility-layout''s chart defaults\nconfig.eventPublisher to \"log\" (Postgres outbox only), so the\nwarehouse.facility.events topic did not exist at all in the cluster. A\nconsumer pointed at it would have come up ready with an empty cache and\nfailed open on every lookup.\n\nAdds var.deploy_facility_events_integration (default false, a pure no-op)\nwhich flips BOTH sides of the integration together, mirroring the existing\nvar.deploy_process_path_kafka_source pattern and for the same reason -- a\npublisher with no consumer, or a consumer whose topic is never written, are\nboth silently broken states:\n\n  * facility-layout: config.eventPublisher \"log\" -> \"kafka\" and\n    kafka.enabled=true, so the chart renders KAFKA_BROKERS and the service\n    actually publishes its Published Language.\n\n  * inventory-storage: LOCATION_LOOKUP_MODE=kafka via the chart''s own\n    extraEnv. Its chart already sets kafka.enabled (it publishes its own\n    integration events), so KAFKA_BROKERS is already present -- which the\n    consumer requires, and whose absence fails startup loudly rather than\n    degrading silently.\n\nThe two services are kept as separate merge entries rather than one block\nbecause they need different keys (a publisher switch vs a consumer-mode env\nvar). Both branches of the inventory-storage ternary declare the same key\nset, per the \"Inconsistent conditional result types\" rule the process-path\nblock above it already documents.\n\nDocumented in variables.tf: because a fresh consumer replays from the\nearliest offset, facility-layout events that predate the publisher flip live\nonly in that service''s Postgres outbox and will never reach the topic. On a\ncluster with existing layout data the layout must be re-registered or\nre-imported after flipping, or the cache is partial -- which is a fail-open\nstate (lookups report Known=false and stows are waved through unclassified),\nnot a hard failure.\n\nterraform validate passes and a plan against the live cluster state confirms\nthe flag produces exactly the two intended changes and nothing else.\nRollback is pure configuration: set it false and re-apply.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnfQtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiNMQABt64hox54vasn65aQ+vOZ1R\n6FrbtPrt32tMp1n5o/KixTWMDGXd3g0uj1MZzcHR1L0jReEW9/f4G7Biq/5feyxX\nH3v6duv+m3AJKHRZiWuNAlnTL93+CO33kOAvRPLswigbpA+HUngX1h9qBYCrrQYi\nQJnmT4BxAIt5B9SsfPuLZKOAD9AkOjlKCDXymeSQDPrn/I+KUaoiTPXOulEc4bfy\nH9WOvZj6xgP/2xnueIsE9WdjYS2kwhmWwpifOsvpa6hgKJShFmOnVI45lgwTepTG\nGHigamWvbiqsjnxLAoX4WFQLFuAWZliMe1MwKoidQ/7qNCXpfNhBgDy6gAoUj2Bi\n+7wdvxaUfr6SjTMhTHeLKVBHLy7TyARRvcYdB4VR7AwmZ+lhSboeOQKsagHsI+Ow\nP82K66/65HEe5zGwICm1fUlZLIGIC1OfYEPDOngN3xa0KBQOuIgA+mBId4d67Gzo\nH/YB7q7Vc3DUi8k41Ossqa+m54lLsf/Zs5iZyjyqZF8VLp1Gdm1AOn2TmUl6rUWf\n6xL+G8qEd2HIAV6JZiSUvEKQPERvC17MuPD0TFUm/OT2+vYirzx9PxtQ5ISWaJX2\nateSvwfddpvETSh1r/ZGaSJljRHvKbxTnEdRXfmEeUWsZYQWruEadzqMc/u/w0fS\ncOM/Mik8k1G+BMJuC4kg\n=H2pi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T23:15:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDZlZjg5M2FkOGUzYzY2Y2JjMWUzYWM1YTFmNWNkMGVlMzg3NmUzYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c","sha":"021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c"}],"sha":"6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6ef893ad8e3c66cbc1e3ac5a1f5cd0ee3876e3c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:41:54Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:41:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(process-path): seed script migrating the static catalogue into process-path-management (#10)\n\nThe three catalogue consumers (fulfillment-execution, wes-work-planning,\nworkforce-management) already ship a PATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE=file|kafka\nswitch, and var.deploy_process_path_kafka_source already flips them onto\nprocess-path-management''s Kafka topic. What was missing was the actual\nmigration of this repo''s config/process-paths/sortable-fc.yaml content\nINTO process-path-management, so the paths the building runs exist in the\nnew owner''s store and get published onto the topic the consumers replay.\n\nAdds scripts/seed-process-paths.py: a dependency-free, idempotent\nreconciler that reads the YAML and creates/revises paths via\nprocess-path-management''s REST API.\n\n  * absent            -> POST, publishes ProcessPathCreated\n  * identical         -> nothing (no spurious ProcessPathUpdated)\n  * diverging         -> PUT, publishes ProcessPathUpdated\n  * deactivated       -> reported and skipped, never silently resurrected\n\nIt parses the YAML with a small purpose-built reader rather than PyYAML so\nit runs from a bare python3 on an operator''s machine or in CI with no\nvirtualenv, and it retries writes briefly to absorb the fresh-topic\nauto-creation race (a first publish to a brand-new topic can fail with\nUnknown Topic Or Partition for ~1s).\n\nThe --republish flag addresses a divergence this fleet can genuinely\nproduce: use cases do Repo.Save THEN Publisher.Publish with no outbox, so\na path defined while the service ran with EVENT_PUBLISHER=log exists in\nPostgres but was never published to Kafka. Consumers only ever see the\ntopic, so GET /process-paths can report a path as ACTIVE that no\nconsumer''s catalogue contains. --republish forces those events out; the\ndefault path never republishes.\n\nVerified against the live `warehouse` kind cluster: the store was missing\nall four canonical paths (PICK/PACK/REBIN/SLAM) while the topic already\nhad them from earlier manual testing. After seeding, the store reconciled\nand a re-run was a clean no-op on every path.\n\nLive propagation was then proven end to end against pods that had been\nrunning for 7h40m with 0 restarts:\n\n  * defined TEST-CUTOVER, then POST /paths/test-cutover-zone-1/charge on\n    wes-work-planning passed catalogue validation (a path that did not\n    exist when the pod booted)\n  * POST /paths/never-defined-xyz/charge still returned 400\n    unknown-path-id, proving the gate is genuinely enforcing\n  * pick-zone-a passed too, exercising the matchPrefix rule against a\n    real fleet-shaped id rather than the bare canonical PICK\n  * after DELETE /process-paths/TEST-CUTOVER, test-cutover-zone-1 went\n    back to 400 — deactivation propagates live as well\n  * pod AGE and RESTARTS were unchanged throughout\n\nAlso marks config/process-paths/sortable-fc.yaml as SUPERSEDED and\nfrozen. It is deliberately kept, not deleted: it remains the rollback\ntarget for var.deploy_process_path_kafka_source = false, so its content\nmust stay accurate. Adds scripts/README-process-path-seed.md documenting\nthe store-vs-topic divergence trap, the verification recipe, and rollback.","tree":{"sha":"8141f93a4171eae6c88d060c4e0a46e1a6dd3f9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/8141f93a4171eae6c88d060c4e0a46e1a6dd3f9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c","verification":{"payload":"tree 8141f93a4171eae6c88d060c4e0a46e1a6dd3f9e\nparent 6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788734514 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788734514 -0300\n\nfeat(process-path): seed script migrating the static catalogue into process-path-management (#10)\n\nThe three catalogue consumers (fulfillment-execution, wes-work-planning,\nworkforce-management) already ship a PATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE=file|kafka\nswitch, and var.deploy_process_path_kafka_source already flips them onto\nprocess-path-management''s Kafka topic. What was missing was the actual\nmigration of this repo''s config/process-paths/sortable-fc.yaml content\nINTO process-path-management, so the paths the building runs exist in the\nnew owner''s store and get published onto the topic the consumers replay.\n\nAdds scripts/seed-process-paths.py: a dependency-free, idempotent\nreconciler that reads the YAML and creates/revises paths via\nprocess-path-management''s REST API.\n\n  * absent            -> POST, publishes ProcessPathCreated\n  * identical         -> nothing (no spurious ProcessPathUpdated)\n  * diverging         -> PUT, publishes ProcessPathUpdated\n  * deactivated       -> reported and skipped, never silently resurrected\n\nIt parses the YAML with a small purpose-built reader rather than PyYAML so\nit runs from a bare python3 on an operator''s machine or in CI with no\nvirtualenv, and it retries writes briefly to absorb the fresh-topic\nauto-creation race (a first publish to a brand-new topic can fail with\nUnknown Topic Or Partition for ~1s).\n\nThe --republish flag addresses a divergence this fleet can genuinely\nproduce: use cases do Repo.Save THEN Publisher.Publish with no outbox, so\na path defined while the service ran with EVENT_PUBLISHER=log exists in\nPostgres but was never published to Kafka. Consumers only ever see the\ntopic, so GET /process-paths can report a path as ACTIVE that no\nconsumer''s catalogue contains. --republish forces those events out; the\ndefault path never republishes.\n\nVerified against the live `warehouse` kind cluster: the store was missing\nall four canonical paths (PICK/PACK/REBIN/SLAM) while the topic already\nhad them from earlier manual testing. After seeding, the store reconciled\nand a re-run was a clean no-op on every path.\n\nLive propagation was then proven end to end against pods that had been\nrunning for 7h40m with 0 restarts:\n\n  * defined TEST-CUTOVER, then POST /paths/test-cutover-zone-1/charge on\n    wes-work-planning passed catalogue validation (a path that did not\n    exist when the pod booted)\n  * POST /paths/never-defined-xyz/charge still returned 400\n    unknown-path-id, proving the gate is genuinely enforcing\n  * pick-zone-a passed too, exercising the matchPrefix rule against a\n    real fleet-shaped id rather than the bare canonical PICK\n  * after DELETE /process-paths/TEST-CUTOVER, test-cutover-zone-1 went\n    back to 400 — deactivation propagates live as well\n  * pod AGE and RESTARTS were unchanged throughout\n\nAlso marks config/process-paths/sortable-fc.yaml as SUPERSEDED and\nfrozen. It is deliberately kept, not deleted: it remains the rollback\ntarget for var.deploy_process_path_kafka_source = false, so its content\nmust stay accurate. Adds scripts/README-process-path-seed.md documenting\nthe store-vs-topic divergence trap, the verification recipe, and rollback.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnewyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgRkQAJ6cUaczAXFGU5RNhDwqnfwe\nV/+wMArrH9QRHBpdbllk1eQUT0AvQ9lZKXHXNaNmAN9Mxv2VmRhefzvs84g968NT\n2TmQqSfQCYhd58rnGjwsDDwPizVMpcQ9uQ6OKkEhl3L6mLBQgzVVJc3YzLR9XNag\n/JeBVwN8EsL1uK/MX9UQaRzHQVvl9UR99Ex9vtvgSIx8JsHuqv160tTb8Us+rwTn\n5t9B9b8nAHUVB/FbAFEgnSongXwhP86eR4fQISvaRQwmSHEdmWatnkgqnt3DZdEu\nxDGvF3hMNHIzmybbqsmoAkmoaOMjmqdL4UVAs1kNNsT9XVQUvQs+fN7+ElaOUmXV\nqgz3Pt3t35qGnjHqMmxHlIgwljVcH7T3zn1rd56NiiADPAqEITaYi4OgFaK8FdlX\nc816RpQ1infeRFi9gbMeO/hLGc5aUd46tQiJh63eEmbEnlaKogLkvq+aBlGL9+az\nPx5IV/LhFrKCUfO37+lkbaZjfvU6gU/2ApEEGuGmiNyzcE3yiZ8dy7eg+wCCeRg8\nKbkK+32yu0AommqhRnPzVoxLAHf4VLqkpPqV3sptEEypCahwn2B0eji9RnWmkEhw\nZ3nwmGg1av6iRQk6NjnpzuRls16BiLoQNwbnFI7cW2+9Zmagyw6TRnXk3HwhY0iV\nnRxcfmEkEyrcN2D77gve\n=Mmx7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T22:41:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDAyMWJkNjlkZjUxNWI2NWZhNDliOGFjYWMwZDdmOTNhNjcwYWJhMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563","sha":"6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563"}],"sha":"021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/021bd69df515b65fa49b8acac0d7f93a670aba1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T17:53:00Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T17:53:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(process-path): deploy process-path-management + opt-in Kafka source switch (#9)\n\nAdds process-path-management as the fleet''s 8th backend service\n(local.services), plus var.deploy_process_path_kafka_source (default\nfalse) letting fulfillment-execution, wes-work-planning, and\nworkforce-management source their process-path catalogue from\nprocess-path-management''s Kafka topic instead of the static\nconfig/process-paths/sortable-fc.yaml file.\n\nTerraform changes\n------------------\n- locals.tf: registered process-path-management in local.services\n  (db/user/port/path/chart_path, same shape as every other service).\n  Documented the file''s SUPERSEDED status in the path_catalogue_*\n  comment block.\n- variables.tf: new deploy_process_path_kafka_source bool, default\n  false. Full rollout-order rationale in its description -- this is\n  deliberately independent from var.deploy_services, since\n  process-path-management is unconditionally deployed once added to\n  local.services regardless of whether any consumer has switched over.\n- services.tf: when the flag is true, each of the 3 consumers gets\n  pathCatalogue.enabled=false + PATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE=kafka via\n  extraEnv; process-path-management gets config.eventPublisher=kafka +\n  kafka.enabled=true. Both branches of every conditional expression\n  declare the SAME top-level keys (pathCatalogue, extraEnv) -- an\n  earlier version that varied which keys were present between\n  true/false branches failed `terraform validate` with \"Inconsistent\n  conditional result types\"; fixed by keeping the shape uniform and\n  varying only the values inside it.\n- helm-values/process-path-management.yaml: new static values file\n  (every other service in local.services already has one; this chart\n  install would otherwise fail at the `file(...)` read in services.tf).\n  kafka.brokers pointed at the real in-cluster broker so the value is\n  correct the moment the flag flips config.eventPublisher/kafka.enabled.\n\nVerified against the REAL warehouse cluster, not just terraform plan\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n- terraform validate / fmt: clean\n- Applied with the flag left at its default false: process-path-management\n  deployed and came up healthy (2/2, real REST API reachable via\n  http://localhost:80/process-path-management, POST /process-paths ->\n  201). All 3 existing consumers'' logs confirmed\n  \"process-path catalogue source configured\",\"source\":\"file\" with the\n  SAME 4 paths as before -- zero behavior change, as designed. Note:\n  the 3 consumers'' images were rebuilt by this apply (their Go source\n  changed in the earlier PRs merging the kafkacatalog package) but the\n  running pods did not pick up the new image until a manual\n  `kubectl rollout restart` -- image tag is always \"local\" with\n  IfNotPresent pull policy, so a rebuilt image alone does not roll\n  the deployment. Restarted by hand and reverified.\n- Applied again with -var=\"deploy_process_path_kafka_source=true\":\n  Plan: 0 to add, 4 to change, 0 to destroy (exactly the 3 consumers +\n  process-path-management, nothing structural). Pods rolled\n  automatically this time (the values change itself is what the Helm\n  release diffs on). Logs confirm all 3 consumers:\n  \"process-path catalogue source configured\",\"source\":\"kafka\", each\n  correctly replaying and reporting\n  \"process-path catalogue is ready\",\"paths\":[\"PACK\",\"REBIN\",\"SLAM\",\"PICK\"].\n  process-path-management''s own log confirms\n  \"kafka event publishing enabled\".\n- Full end-to-end proof: POST a brand-new path (STAGE) to\n  process-path-management''s REST API -> propagated over Kafka ->\n  POST /tasks on fulfillment-execution with type=\"stage\" (a path that\n  did not exist when that pod booted) succeeded, returning a real\n  PENDING task. This is the complete live proof the whole pipeline\n  works: catalogue mutation -> Kafka -> consumer cache -> real domain\n  validation, in the actual running cluster, not a unit test.\n- Pre-existing gotcha handled, not caused by this change: Postgres in\n  this cluster is already initialized (14 databases, 14h+ old), so\n  Terraform''s initdb-based role/database creation does not re-run for\n  a newly-added service. Manually ran the same CREATE ROLE / CREATE\n  DATABASE / REVOKE / GRANT statements the .tftpl template uses,\n  pulling the Terraform-generated password via `terraform state pull`\n  (documented fleet-ops pitfall) before the pod needed it.\n\nNot in this PR (deliberately deferred)\n---------------------------------------\n- Retiring config/process-paths/sortable-fc.yaml and the\n  path_catalogue_content/path_catalogue_services locals entirely --\n  kept as the default (flag=false) path until Kafka-sourcing has run\n  for a full cycle. locals.tf''s comment documents this explicitly.\n- Flipping the default itself to true -- left as an explicit, separate\n  decision for a future PR once this one is reviewed.","tree":{"sha":"bdbcf7b5d7a8a781f39afc1377fc3573b0464d4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/bdbcf7b5d7a8a781f39afc1377fc3573b0464d4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563","verification":{"payload":"tree bdbcf7b5d7a8a781f39afc1377fc3573b0464d4b\nparent 2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788717180 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788717180 -0300\n\nfeat(process-path): deploy process-path-management + opt-in Kafka source switch (#9)\n\nAdds process-path-management as the fleet''s 8th backend service\n(local.services), plus var.deploy_process_path_kafka_source (default\nfalse) letting fulfillment-execution, wes-work-planning, and\nworkforce-management source their process-path catalogue from\nprocess-path-management''s Kafka topic instead of the static\nconfig/process-paths/sortable-fc.yaml file.\n\nTerraform changes\n------------------\n- locals.tf: registered process-path-management in local.services\n  (db/user/port/path/chart_path, same shape as every other service).\n  Documented the file''s SUPERSEDED status in the path_catalogue_*\n  comment block.\n- variables.tf: new deploy_process_path_kafka_source bool, default\n  false. Full rollout-order rationale in its description -- this is\n  deliberately independent from var.deploy_services, since\n  process-path-management is unconditionally deployed once added to\n  local.services regardless of whether any consumer has switched over.\n- services.tf: when the flag is true, each of the 3 consumers gets\n  pathCatalogue.enabled=false + PATH_CATALOGUE_SOURCE=kafka via\n  extraEnv; process-path-management gets config.eventPublisher=kafka +\n  kafka.enabled=true. Both branches of every conditional expression\n  declare the SAME top-level keys (pathCatalogue, extraEnv) -- an\n  earlier version that varied which keys were present between\n  true/false branches failed `terraform validate` with \"Inconsistent\n  conditional result types\"; fixed by keeping the shape uniform and\n  varying only the values inside it.\n- helm-values/process-path-management.yaml: new static values file\n  (every other service in local.services already has one; this chart\n  install would otherwise fail at the `file(...)` read in services.tf).\n  kafka.brokers pointed at the real in-cluster broker so the value is\n  correct the moment the flag flips config.eventPublisher/kafka.enabled.\n\nVerified against the REAL warehouse cluster, not just terraform plan\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n- terraform validate / fmt: clean\n- Applied with the flag left at its default false: process-path-management\n  deployed and came up healthy (2/2, real REST API reachable via\n  http://localhost:80/process-path-management, POST /process-paths ->\n  201). All 3 existing consumers'' logs confirmed\n  \"process-path catalogue source configured\",\"source\":\"file\" with the\n  SAME 4 paths as before -- zero behavior change, as designed. Note:\n  the 3 consumers'' images were rebuilt by this apply (their Go source\n  changed in the earlier PRs merging the kafkacatalog package) but the\n  running pods did not pick up the new image until a manual\n  `kubectl rollout restart` -- image tag is always \"local\" with\n  IfNotPresent pull policy, so a rebuilt image alone does not roll\n  the deployment. Restarted by hand and reverified.\n- Applied again with -var=\"deploy_process_path_kafka_source=true\":\n  Plan: 0 to add, 4 to change, 0 to destroy (exactly the 3 consumers +\n  process-path-management, nothing structural). Pods rolled\n  automatically this time (the values change itself is what the Helm\n  release diffs on). Logs confirm all 3 consumers:\n  \"process-path catalogue source configured\",\"source\":\"kafka\", each\n  correctly replaying and reporting\n  \"process-path catalogue is ready\",\"paths\":[\"PACK\",\"REBIN\",\"SLAM\",\"PICK\"].\n  process-path-management''s own log confirms\n  \"kafka event publishing enabled\".\n- Full end-to-end proof: POST a brand-new path (STAGE) to\n  process-path-management''s REST API -> propagated over Kafka ->\n  POST /tasks on fulfillment-execution with type=\"stage\" (a path that\n  did not exist when that pod booted) succeeded, returning a real\n  PENDING task. This is the complete live proof the whole pipeline\n  works: catalogue mutation -> Kafka -> consumer cache -> real domain\n  validation, in the actual running cluster, not a unit test.\n- Pre-existing gotcha handled, not caused by this change: Postgres in\n  this cluster is already initialized (14 databases, 14h+ old), so\n  Terraform''s initdb-based role/database creation does not re-run for\n  a newly-added service. Manually ran the same CREATE ROLE / CREATE\n  DATABASE / REVOKE / GRANT statements the .tftpl template uses,\n  pulling the Terraform-generated password via `terraform state pull`\n  (documented fleet-ops pitfall) before the pod needed it.\n\nNot in this PR (deliberately deferred)\n---------------------------------------\n- Retiring config/process-paths/sortable-fc.yaml and the\n  path_catalogue_content/path_catalogue_services locals entirely --\n  kept as the default (flag=false) path until Kafka-sourcing has run\n  for a full cycle. locals.tf''s comment documents this explicitly.\n- Flipping the default itself to true -- left as an explicit, separate\n  decision for a future PR once this one is reviewed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnah8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAht4QAIJc7PP0dvYxGx/Exxz5HOpE\nYS9k5xLXaIumgo3iC4X0wZle+kRzyTn+y+q0BZtKT6U/iwf3Nab6yZAphoRUmzkN\n9B/MHEHr+rqp8yHPwJamwOd8EF9v4GWtfLjd6hsuXILIVRO9O/A/gfIB0QZtGOu3\nhJiEuzXnVfjRYKcUeaQzpaBXQEptRZkSNh+xmc22ow/FnEBSWfd1R4NEP9DNRzHO\ncXqmN4oWJkUtS73ADEUMcWYqimU5h3v4nJMGtJaXQ71bls5EGaGLACCO/Eq+JJcx\noApwI92rnDKyw9IWsS9N3tqEzHIMI3RzE2YNyv1wZoa1QwUAESx6dVZOBZM+ZH5w\nTR4fl1zA9zinuLtPEHA8FYAcZ68Lw6Q9zrLMPN0Nt0nDajF0bPHfPaii6CFg/0DO\nEIPf9FDmTbAyW6vMXNRDh4W/8Nl+pq4rSH4w4q3GqHDeOJLTZQwx15B+dDFV5qDT\nDjAfzOUBwAKTamhS0p0Dp6ttfhtPW5By9CRFFhgMgV9l3WYeYjYMNJ5kdh3kKvNU\nVYCXJMHpx7XEIpMXyWuKvVilNuTc+pkCRtma52DBy/17bKxS4/qibhpZyHvu2BAW\nW+XOxPXqpvrx+NJ8Wz0k2X2HfKgQ/5zrtfWcuMAb1l7xJPxzGDBgZZvKOvrwo/Aa\nysCUSBBfnC9Je4aLqUXP\n=VpQO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T17:53:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDZlNWMxYzdlM2EwMGU1NmMxNjc2ZjQ3NTgzZGM2NTRhZDBkYmI1NjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434","sha":"2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434"}],"sha":"6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/6e5c1c7e3a00e56c1676f47583dc654ad0dbb563"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T23:44:52Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T23:44:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(gateway-api): pilot HTTPRoute migration — RESOLVED, enabled by default (#8)\n\n* feat(gateway-api): pilot HTTPRoute migration (defaulted OFF — real KIC bug found)\n\nIntroduces the Kubernetes Gateway API as an additive, parallel routing\nmechanism to Kong''s existing Ingress-based routing, piloted on exactly one\nservice (fulfillment-execution) before any fleet-wide migration. Ships:\n\n- Gateway API v1.6.2 CRDs (standard channel), installed via a\n  null_resource + kubectl apply (kubernetes_manifest can''t be used here —\n  it needs the CRD''s schema to validate at plan time, which doesn''t exist\n  yet on a clean apply that installs the CRD and a resource using it in\n  the same run).\n- A `kong` GatewayClass and one shared `warehouse-gateway` Gateway.\n- An HTTPRoute for fulfillment-execution mirroring its existing Ingress''s\n  path-prefix + strip-path behavior exactly.\n\nBLOCKED: found a real, reproducible bug in Kong Ingress Controller 3.5''s\n(this chart''s bundled KIC version) Gateway reconciler. It processes a\nGateway object exactly once at controller startup, logs through \"Checking\ndeletion timestamp\", and never reconciles it again — on create, update,\nor any watched-resource change. Proven definitively by manually patching\nthe Gateway''s status subresource directly via `kubectl patch\n--subresource=status`: the API server accepted it instantly (ruling out\nRBAC/CRDs/admission-webhook), and it sat completely untouched for 10+\nminutes, meaning the controller genuinely never revisits the object.\nReal functional consequence, not cosmetic: HTTPRoute traffic 404s (\"no\nRoute matched\") while the same service''s untouched Ingress route returns\n200 on the same cluster. Reproduced identically on KIC 3.5 and the latest\n3.5.13 patch (ruling out a stale-image issue). GatewayClass reconciliation\nworks fine in the same controller process; only Gateway/HTTPRoute are\naffected. Could not find a matching upstream Kong issue for this exact\nsignature via GitHub''s issue search.\n\ndeploy_gateway_api defaults to FALSE as a result — the platform pieces are\ncomplete and correct (verified via terraform validate, terraform plan\nidempotency, and a full destroy/apply rebuild with fulfillment-execution''s\nIngress route confirmed restored to HTTP 200), but nothing here actually\nroutes traffic yet. Re-enable once either a KIC fix ships or this repo\nadopts ingressController.gatewayDiscovery.enabled=true (a bigger topology\nchange splitting Kong Gateway and KIC into separate releases).\n\nAlso fixes a real orphaning bug this pilot surfaced: null_resource with\nonly an apply-time local-exec provisioner has no destroy-time\ncounterpart, so flipping deploy_gateway_api from true to false left the\nGateway API CRDs, GatewayClass, Gateway, and HTTPRoute completely\norphaned in the live cluster — Terraform reported them destroyed while\n`kubectl get` showed all four objects still present, 20+ minutes old,\nuntracked by any state. Added `when = destroy` provisioners (using\nself.triggers, the only values available at destroy time) to all four\ngateway-api.tf resources.\n\n* fix(gateway-api): the \"unmanaged\" GatewayClass annotation — real fix found\n\nThe Gateway API pilot''s Gateway/HTTPRoute controllers appeared to go\npermanently idle after one reconcile pass at controller startup —\nverified via kubectl patch --subresource=status, reproduced across two\nKIC patch versions (3.5, 3.5.13) and two Helm deployment topologies\n(single-release, gatewayDiscovery split-release). Turns out this was not\na bug — it''s a real, documented KIC requirement this fleet''s config never\nsatisfied.\n\nRoot cause: `GatewayClass` objects need the annotation\n`konghq.com/gatewayclass-unmanaged: \"true\"` to be reconciled when Kong''s\ndataplane is deployed via `deployment.kong.enabled=true` (this fleet''s\nsetup, and the vast majority of self-managed Kong-on-Kubernetes\ndeployments) rather than provisioned dynamically per-Gateway by KIC or\nKong Gateway Operator. Without the annotation, KIC''s `Gateway` controller\nhas no code path at all for this topology and silently does nothing past\nits first pass — no error, no useful log line, nothing to point at the\nmissing annotation. Found by reading KIC''s actual CHANGELOG.md (not\nguessing) for prior fixes mentioning \"GatewayReconciler falls into a\nloop\" and \"unmanaged Gateway mode\", which led to the annotation.\n\nVerified live before touching Terraform: applying a GatewayClass with the\nannotation immediately flips a Gateway to `Accepted: True` /\n`Programmed: True` with the message \"this unmanaged gateway has been\npicked up by the controller and will be processed\" — and a curl through\na resulting HTTPRoute on a path that only existed via that route (not any\npre-existing Ingress) returned a real 200.\n\nRe-enables the pilot (`deploy_gateway_api` back to `true` — see its\nupdated variable doc for the full resolution). Verified end-to-end on a\nfull destroy/apply rebuild via Terraform, not just the live experiment:\n- Apply complete, 55 resources added, 42/42 pods healthy, 0 restarts\n- `warehouse-gateway` shows `PROGRAMMED: True` in the standard\n  `kubectl get gateway` column\n- `fulfillment-execution`''s HTTPRoute shows Accepted/ResolvedRefs/\n  Programmed all True\n- No Ingress object exists for fulfillment-execution anymore (correctly\n  suppressed by services.tf''s pilot-scoping) — its 200 response is\n  genuinely routed through the new HTTPRoute, no ambiguity possible\n- The other 6 services'' Ingress-based routes all still return 200,\n  confirming the pilot''s scoping didn''t touch anything else\n- scripts/smoke-test.sh PASSED (fulfillment-execution''s healthcheck\n  explicitly listed and green)\n- terraform plan -detailed-exitcode -> No changes (idempotent)\n\n* feat(gateway-api): fan out to all 8 services (Ingress fully retired)\n\nFollow-up to the fulfillment-execution pilot and the real KIC\n\"gatewayclass-unmanaged\" fix (previous commit on this branch): every\nservice in local.services, plus warehouse-ops-agent, now migrates from\nIngress to HTTPRoute, chart-rendered via each service''s own `gatewayApi`\nvalues block -- the same `httproute.yaml` chart template pattern\nfulfillment-execution''s pilot validated, since fanned out to all 8\nservice repos (each its own PR, independently verified: helm lint, a\nreal enabled-render, a real default-is-a-no-op render, CI green, then\nmerged):\n\n  inventory-storage #49, wes-work-planning #50, workforce-management #51,\n  order-management #31, facility-layout #49, labor-performance #14,\n  warehouse-ops-agent #33, fulfillment-execution #63 (this repo''s own\n  chart, added after the fact since the pilot originally used a raw\n  kubectl-applied HTTPRoute rather than a chart template).\n\nChanges here:\n- services.tf: local.gateway_api_pilot_services now covers every key in\n  local.services (was just fulfillment-execution). The computed\n  `gatewayApi` values block mirrors the `ingress` block it replaces --\n  same path prefix, same strip-prefix behavior via HTTPRoute''s own\n  `filters`, so this is a like-for-like routing swap, not a behavior\n  change.\n- ops-agent.tf: same swap for warehouse-ops-agent, which isn''t in\n  local.services (no database) so it gets its own gatewayApi block\n  rather than going through local.gateway_api_pilot_services.\n- gateway-api.tf: removed the now-superseded raw-kubectl\n  null_resource.fulfillment_execution_httproute (its job is done by\n  fulfillment-execution''s own chart now); rewrote the file header to\n  document the full pilot history load-bearing for a future Kong/KIC\n  upgrade (the gatewayclass-unmanaged requirement is easy to re-trip).\n\nVerified via a full destroy/apply rebuild, not incremental live edits:\n- Apply complete, 54 resources added, 42/42 pods healthy, 0 restarts\n- `kubectl get gateway` shows PROGRAMMED: True\n- Zero Ingress objects anywhere in the cluster (kubectl get ingress -A)\n- 8/8 HTTPRoute objects present, one per service\n- curl through every one of the 8 services'' /healthz returns 200 --\n  unambiguously via HTTPRoute, since no Ingress exists as a fallback path\n  for any of them\n- scripts/smoke-test.sh PASSED\n- terraform plan -detailed-exitcode -> No changes (idempotent)\n\n* fix(gateway-api): restore Loki variables dropped during rebase conflict resolution\n\nThe rebase onto develop (after PR #7/Loki merged) hit a real merge\nconflict in variables.tf -- both branches append new variable blocks to\nthe same location. Resolving it manually dropped 3 of the 4 Loki\nvariables (deploy_logging, loki_chart_version, alloy_chart_version),\nkeeping only loki_retention_period, which broke terraform validate with\n3 \"undeclared input variable\" errors referencing logging.tf. Caught\nimmediately by re-running terraform validate after the rebase rather\nthan assuming a clean rebase meant a correct one.","tree":{"sha":"ef1e7f5bbc09733ef8fd0282a44272fac80d43e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/ef1e7f5bbc09733ef8fd0282a44272fac80d43e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434","verification":{"payload":"tree ef1e7f5bbc09733ef8fd0282a44272fac80d43e2\nparent d15f688e3b3511b186bc26787bab709cefd1b79e\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788651892 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788651892 -0300\n\nfeat(gateway-api): pilot HTTPRoute migration — RESOLVED, enabled by default (#8)\n\n* feat(gateway-api): pilot HTTPRoute migration (defaulted OFF — real KIC bug found)\n\nIntroduces the Kubernetes Gateway API as an additive, parallel routing\nmechanism to Kong''s existing Ingress-based routing, piloted on exactly one\nservice (fulfillment-execution) before any fleet-wide migration. Ships:\n\n- Gateway API v1.6.2 CRDs (standard channel), installed via a\n  null_resource + kubectl apply (kubernetes_manifest can''t be used here —\n  it needs the CRD''s schema to validate at plan time, which doesn''t exist\n  yet on a clean apply that installs the CRD and a resource using it in\n  the same run).\n- A `kong` GatewayClass and one shared `warehouse-gateway` Gateway.\n- An HTTPRoute for fulfillment-execution mirroring its existing Ingress''s\n  path-prefix + strip-path behavior exactly.\n\nBLOCKED: found a real, reproducible bug in Kong Ingress Controller 3.5''s\n(this chart''s bundled KIC version) Gateway reconciler. It processes a\nGateway object exactly once at controller startup, logs through \"Checking\ndeletion timestamp\", and never reconciles it again — on create, update,\nor any watched-resource change. Proven definitively by manually patching\nthe Gateway''s status subresource directly via `kubectl patch\n--subresource=status`: the API server accepted it instantly (ruling out\nRBAC/CRDs/admission-webhook), and it sat completely untouched for 10+\nminutes, meaning the controller genuinely never revisits the object.\nReal functional consequence, not cosmetic: HTTPRoute traffic 404s (\"no\nRoute matched\") while the same service''s untouched Ingress route returns\n200 on the same cluster. Reproduced identically on KIC 3.5 and the latest\n3.5.13 patch (ruling out a stale-image issue). GatewayClass reconciliation\nworks fine in the same controller process; only Gateway/HTTPRoute are\naffected. Could not find a matching upstream Kong issue for this exact\nsignature via GitHub''s issue search.\n\ndeploy_gateway_api defaults to FALSE as a result — the platform pieces are\ncomplete and correct (verified via terraform validate, terraform plan\nidempotency, and a full destroy/apply rebuild with fulfillment-execution''s\nIngress route confirmed restored to HTTP 200), but nothing here actually\nroutes traffic yet. Re-enable once either a KIC fix ships or this repo\nadopts ingressController.gatewayDiscovery.enabled=true (a bigger topology\nchange splitting Kong Gateway and KIC into separate releases).\n\nAlso fixes a real orphaning bug this pilot surfaced: null_resource with\nonly an apply-time local-exec provisioner has no destroy-time\ncounterpart, so flipping deploy_gateway_api from true to false left the\nGateway API CRDs, GatewayClass, Gateway, and HTTPRoute completely\norphaned in the live cluster — Terraform reported them destroyed while\n`kubectl get` showed all four objects still present, 20+ minutes old,\nuntracked by any state. Added `when = destroy` provisioners (using\nself.triggers, the only values available at destroy time) to all four\ngateway-api.tf resources.\n\n* fix(gateway-api): the \"unmanaged\" GatewayClass annotation — real fix found\n\nThe Gateway API pilot''s Gateway/HTTPRoute controllers appeared to go\npermanently idle after one reconcile pass at controller startup —\nverified via kubectl patch --subresource=status, reproduced across two\nKIC patch versions (3.5, 3.5.13) and two Helm deployment topologies\n(single-release, gatewayDiscovery split-release). Turns out this was not\na bug — it''s a real, documented KIC requirement this fleet''s config never\nsatisfied.\n\nRoot cause: `GatewayClass` objects need the annotation\n`konghq.com/gatewayclass-unmanaged: \"true\"` to be reconciled when Kong''s\ndataplane is deployed via `deployment.kong.enabled=true` (this fleet''s\nsetup, and the vast majority of self-managed Kong-on-Kubernetes\ndeployments) rather than provisioned dynamically per-Gateway by KIC or\nKong Gateway Operator. Without the annotation, KIC''s `Gateway` controller\nhas no code path at all for this topology and silently does nothing past\nits first pass — no error, no useful log line, nothing to point at the\nmissing annotation. Found by reading KIC''s actual CHANGELOG.md (not\nguessing) for prior fixes mentioning \"GatewayReconciler falls into a\nloop\" and \"unmanaged Gateway mode\", which led to the annotation.\n\nVerified live before touching Terraform: applying a GatewayClass with the\nannotation immediately flips a Gateway to `Accepted: True` /\n`Programmed: True` with the message \"this unmanaged gateway has been\npicked up by the controller and will be processed\" — and a curl through\na resulting HTTPRoute on a path that only existed via that route (not any\npre-existing Ingress) returned a real 200.\n\nRe-enables the pilot (`deploy_gateway_api` back to `true` — see its\nupdated variable doc for the full resolution). Verified end-to-end on a\nfull destroy/apply rebuild via Terraform, not just the live experiment:\n- Apply complete, 55 resources added, 42/42 pods healthy, 0 restarts\n- `warehouse-gateway` shows `PROGRAMMED: True` in the standard\n  `kubectl get gateway` column\n- `fulfillment-execution`''s HTTPRoute shows Accepted/ResolvedRefs/\n  Programmed all True\n- No Ingress object exists for fulfillment-execution anymore (correctly\n  suppressed by services.tf''s pilot-scoping) — its 200 response is\n  genuinely routed through the new HTTPRoute, no ambiguity possible\n- The other 6 services'' Ingress-based routes all still return 200,\n  confirming the pilot''s scoping didn''t touch anything else\n- scripts/smoke-test.sh PASSED (fulfillment-execution''s healthcheck\n  explicitly listed and green)\n- terraform plan -detailed-exitcode -> No changes (idempotent)\n\n* feat(gateway-api): fan out to all 8 services (Ingress fully retired)\n\nFollow-up to the fulfillment-execution pilot and the real KIC\n\"gatewayclass-unmanaged\" fix (previous commit on this branch): every\nservice in local.services, plus warehouse-ops-agent, now migrates from\nIngress to HTTPRoute, chart-rendered via each service''s own `gatewayApi`\nvalues block -- the same `httproute.yaml` chart template pattern\nfulfillment-execution''s pilot validated, since fanned out to all 8\nservice repos (each its own PR, independently verified: helm lint, a\nreal enabled-render, a real default-is-a-no-op render, CI green, then\nmerged):\n\n  inventory-storage #49, wes-work-planning #50, workforce-management #51,\n  order-management #31, facility-layout #49, labor-performance #14,\n  warehouse-ops-agent #33, fulfillment-execution #63 (this repo''s own\n  chart, added after the fact since the pilot originally used a raw\n  kubectl-applied HTTPRoute rather than a chart template).\n\nChanges here:\n- services.tf: local.gateway_api_pilot_services now covers every key in\n  local.services (was just fulfillment-execution). The computed\n  `gatewayApi` values block mirrors the `ingress` block it replaces --\n  same path prefix, same strip-prefix behavior via HTTPRoute''s own\n  `filters`, so this is a like-for-like routing swap, not a behavior\n  change.\n- ops-agent.tf: same swap for warehouse-ops-agent, which isn''t in\n  local.services (no database) so it gets its own gatewayApi block\n  rather than going through local.gateway_api_pilot_services.\n- gateway-api.tf: removed the now-superseded raw-kubectl\n  null_resource.fulfillment_execution_httproute (its job is done by\n  fulfillment-execution''s own chart now); rewrote the file header to\n  document the full pilot history load-bearing for a future Kong/KIC\n  upgrade (the gatewayclass-unmanaged requirement is easy to re-trip).\n\nVerified via a full destroy/apply rebuild, not incremental live edits:\n- Apply complete, 54 resources added, 42/42 pods healthy, 0 restarts\n- `kubectl get gateway` shows PROGRAMMED: True\n- Zero Ingress objects anywhere in the cluster (kubectl get ingress -A)\n- 8/8 HTTPRoute objects present, one per service\n- curl through every one of the 8 services'' /healthz returns 200 --\n  unambiguously via HTTPRoute, since no Ingress exists as a fallback path\n  for any of them\n- scripts/smoke-test.sh PASSED\n- terraform plan -detailed-exitcode -> No changes (idempotent)\n\n* fix(gateway-api): restore Loki variables dropped during rebase conflict resolution\n\nThe rebase onto develop (after PR #7/Loki merged) hit a real merge\nconflict in variables.tf -- both branches append new variable blocks to\nthe same location. Resolving it manually dropped 3 of the 4 Loki\nvariables (deploy_logging, loki_chart_version, alloy_chart_version),\nkeeping only loki_retention_period, which broke terraform validate with\n3 \"undeclared input variable\" errors referencing logging.tf. Caught\nimmediately by re-running terraform validate after the rebase rather\nthan assuming a clean rebase meant a correct one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnKl0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlooQAB44lZzKXRF8Aj3q9OIlZWvE\nkgy3XNZF3XXsSkEs82/3kJUuXYdKPLynh44TCDP6RdyH13NJ0AHowx/0auy9ZL5g\nZ94Tbzi6AgvZ1wZ+ySvzf7eqGemicvauGltNicFkljNVsIUHFVv1C+PCcyE+6h4Z\nXWSPadGqn/wNyl1M7RFD3oTnh23uUeZcJMWOWul/k4mV8eMnu7AiVnHibsedz73g\nETItwXOoxqWkkZBaDvpantln9IoJqMMeAcODbzjIzZzk+IKgZYFDcBT4d1kGdihM\n4McADz3McqgPSFfEPmgv9yUun5M5VyDvZuA7ai0X4XyuDNh7Kia03kMGizw76twm\nT2QoY7JEe1SAJTBH21W4JiSg3Y87XK/WgatZJQBRyJGQcKKB4MIj0ZGq4P6bIIu2\nn3f5z4bnkjzvLXaZIZWGnOemmVfq6y/NQJdMnYeDYgVyIAtB8J17OewI8MsF3Y0c\n+YISF/AwUBuiwqmTvPDBgtJqXfWea3u+IUNrjPSV4jIRhUUnHbjsGJ9/3OLhGdOl\nEXKZyWWIJ7o/R4zB11KTYln/Mg1TA1X2NDgTmebbDjFL9BWGM9kaVMl9uMNK1ykl\nn2SVDz7UlW6NX/g+F/KqZf5BjEITAxIebd/Id3M5FNQOKDq5hqlvQso5SdoeQEHv\nx4BABCWvaNUgWPBzT7KZ\n=RG4Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T23:44:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDJlYmJkZDA0NGJiYjczMjk2YWE3ZWU5NmY5NmYwMjRkYzlhYWQ0MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/d15f688e3b3511b186bc26787bab709cefd1b79e","sha":"d15f688e3b3511b186bc26787bab709cefd1b79e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/d15f688e3b3511b186bc26787bab709cefd1b79e"}],"sha":"2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/2ebbdd044bbb73296aa7ee96f96f024dc9aad434"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/d15f688e3b3511b186bc26787bab709cefd1b79e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:10:33Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T22:10:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(observability): add Loki + Alloy log aggregation (#7)\n\nThe OTel Collector''s config declared logs = null with the comment \"no logs\nbackend in this stack\" -- every service already writes structured JSON to\nstdout via log/slog with the active trace/span ID stamped into each record\n(telemetry.WithTraceContext), but the ONLY way to read any of it was\n`kubectl logs <pod>`: no cross-service search, no retention past whatever\nthe container runtime keeps, nothing survives a pod restart.\n\nAdds Loki (storage/query, SingleBinary mode, filesystem chunk storage, 24h\nretention matching Prometheus) + Alloy (log-tailing DaemonSet, one pod per\nnode) to the observability namespace, gated behind a new deploy_logging\nvariable. Collection tails container stdout directly rather than routing\nthrough the OTel Collector''s OTLP pipeline -- every service already emits\nJSON to stdout, so this needs ZERO application code changes across all\neight repos, and trace correlation still works because the trace_id is\nalready a field inside the JSON body Alloy tails.\n\nGrafana gets a third datasource (Loki, alongside Prometheus/Jaeger) with a\nderivedFields regex that turns a log line''s trace_id into a click-through\nto the matching Jaeger trace.\n\nTwo real bugs found and fixed via the actual container, not just the\nchart''s values.yaml comments:\n1. `compactor.retention_enabled=true` requires `delete_request_store` to be\n   set or Loki refuses to start (\"CONFIG ERROR: invalid compactor config\").\n   Set to \"filesystem\" to match loki.storage.type.\n2. Unlike Postgres/Prometheus, this chart does NOT fall back to an emptyDir\n   when singleBinary.persistence.enabled=false -- it mounts nothing at\n   /var/loki at all, crashing with \"mkdir /var/loki: read-only file\n   system\". Added explicit extraVolumes/extraVolumeMounts.\n\nVerified on a full destroy/apply rebuild:\n- helm template + `alloy validate` run against the real binary before\n  ever touching the cluster (config is valid, syntax is valid)\n- Apply complete, 44/44 pods Running across the whole cluster, 0 restarts\n- Loki actually has every one of the fleet''s 18 `app` label values\n  (confirmed via /loki/api/v1/label/app/values), not just a subset\n- A real log line from inventory-storage queried back via\n  /loki/api/v1/query_range, complete with trace_id/span_id fields\n- All three Grafana datasources (Prometheus/Jaeger/Loki) provisioned with\n  the trace_id derived-field link wired in\n- scripts/smoke-test.sh PASSED\n- terraform plan -detailed-exitcode -> No changes (idempotent)\n\nSee docs/observability/log-aggregation.md for the full design rationale\n(collection-path choice, SingleBinary vs SimpleScalable, Alloy vs Promtail).","tree":{"sha":"3f38bed5fc2f3bf7fa6bd860b911bff4fcda9a79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/3f38bed5fc2f3bf7fa6bd860b911bff4fcda9a79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/d15f688e3b3511b186bc26787bab709cefd1b79e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f38bed5fc2f3bf7fa6bd860b911bff4fcda9a79\nparent e9f17306c0c82725938d6e1b947d679c7494c677\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788646233 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788646233 -0300\n\nfeat(observability): add Loki + Alloy log aggregation (#7)\n\nThe OTel Collector''s config declared logs = null with the comment \"no logs\nbackend in this stack\" -- every service already writes structured JSON to\nstdout via log/slog with the active trace/span ID stamped into each record\n(telemetry.WithTraceContext), but the ONLY way to read any of it was\n`kubectl logs <pod>`: no cross-service search, no retention past whatever\nthe container runtime keeps, nothing survives a pod restart.\n\nAdds Loki (storage/query, SingleBinary mode, filesystem chunk storage, 24h\nretention matching Prometheus) + Alloy (log-tailing DaemonSet, one pod per\nnode) to the observability namespace, gated behind a new deploy_logging\nvariable. Collection tails container stdout directly rather than routing\nthrough the OTel Collector''s OTLP pipeline -- every service already emits\nJSON to stdout, so this needs ZERO application code changes across all\neight repos, and trace correlation still works because the trace_id is\nalready a field inside the JSON body Alloy tails.\n\nGrafana gets a third datasource (Loki, alongside Prometheus/Jaeger) with a\nderivedFields regex that turns a log line''s trace_id into a click-through\nto the matching Jaeger trace.\n\nTwo real bugs found and fixed via the actual container, not just the\nchart''s values.yaml comments:\n1. `compactor.retention_enabled=true` requires `delete_request_store` to be\n   set or Loki refuses to start (\"CONFIG ERROR: invalid compactor config\").\n   Set to \"filesystem\" to match loki.storage.type.\n2. Unlike Postgres/Prometheus, this chart does NOT fall back to an emptyDir\n   when singleBinary.persistence.enabled=false -- it mounts nothing at\n   /var/loki at all, crashing with \"mkdir /var/loki: read-only file\n   system\". Added explicit extraVolumes/extraVolumeMounts.\n\nVerified on a full destroy/apply rebuild:\n- helm template + `alloy validate` run against the real binary before\n  ever touching the cluster (config is valid, syntax is valid)\n- Apply complete, 44/44 pods Running across the whole cluster, 0 restarts\n- Loki actually has every one of the fleet''s 18 `app` label values\n  (confirmed via /loki/api/v1/label/app/values), not just a subset\n- A real log line from inventory-storage queried back via\n  /loki/api/v1/query_range, complete with trace_id/span_id fields\n- All three Grafana datasources (Prometheus/Jaeger/Loki) provisioned with\n  the trace_id derived-field link wired in\n- scripts/smoke-test.sh PASSED\n- terraform plan -detailed-exitcode -> No changes (idempotent)\n\nSee docs/observability/log-aggregation.md for the full design rationale\n(collection-path choice, SingleBinary vs SimpleScalable, Alloy vs Promtail).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnJNZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApOUQADiApHYWkE/7ksb/8C/GnUUT\nmtqzYr9BQ5duoGme1uD3rViocWGnEZNqZYNF3tV2RU9WUA4W+UuSK0HJVS1Ai9B5\nj99BFeSDvHVlG4TGvtKDRBjCG44JIx4Rz0uEDVdHp/gqbz1omiNWaCcLz5cb7KPM\n9OCRqSg8uy0GkFbbBasOGk+teKKeX+z2v1jEjGEhYCRIhDYc15X6tzoOOnWNmywd\nuKGs9zufLslLWw5OV1cp+Y052zZLUh/z6lLys5Gb2ZN4/1E0ZcCVyOsS9aPAOEWh\nxeUBNG7N0lNpT6Wbixgt1pB/EL6zewM/J6yHMY3Vx600KOk6ODnW2Q3LpVjbxe3d\nQ/a1B2ihos9nvG+5av2MNOUXhUginls2tU4guNLkZYkigz5kFS4oSLohgJdqcYKd\n2Z9uNGtn02Lb5Y9pNHrIfzc2evDpZ4oQ682zGoZwdKHgL7Zxxj+UJALX2CEMSdrI\n5aSMsKS+7h3sJbFwo4blgLQVf73RHCtuVIUfZjiaFyXsrZVSjAGK56R40Q8sU0rD\nH9wiMXEQLzIi0b2lCEDvJKfu0tVCvq0q