/a30dc419524bef52ba4ffbd1121e0d86b266cac4"}],"sha":"4b6d5d715323d7e1fb12fb5e3bb241963a36007a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/4b6d5d715323d7e1fb12fb5e3bb241963a36007a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/a30dc419524bef52ba4ffbd1121e0d86b266cac4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T11:37:11Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T11:37:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: register labor-performance analytics + wire BFF reports URLs (#4)\n\nTwo real deploy gaps closed:\n\n1. labor-performance was excluded from analytics_services -- its chart\n   shipped no projector/reports templates at all (a different, earlier\n   gap than fulfillment-execution''s Dockerfile CrashLoopBackOff issue),\n   closed by labor-performance''s own feature/analytics-chart-wiring PR.\n   Adding it here to analytics_services auto-wires its analytics DB,\n   role, and Helm analytics.* values via the existing generic\n   for_each -- no new Terraform logic needed.\n\n2. warehouse-ops-agent''s console-bff gained a WMS/WES dashboard fan-out\n   (PR #27) reading 7 new *_REPORTS_REST_URL env vars, but this repo''s\n   ops-agent.tf never templated them -- every dashboard section would\n   silently degrade to available:false in a real cluster deploy despite\n   the code being live. Wires all 7 to the real in-cluster\n   ''<service>-reports'' Service DNS names (the analytics reports Service\n   every analytics-enabled chart''s reportsFullname helper creates).\n\nNote: terraform validate/plan/apply for this change must run from the\nactual warehouse-infra checkout (not this worktree) -- the config''s\n../../<name> sibling-repo paths only resolve correctly when\nwarehouse-infra sits directly alongside the other repos under\n~/warehouse-systems, which a git worktree subdirectory breaks. Verified\nterraform fmt is clean; full validate/plan run from the main checkout.","tree":{"sha":"63d166df81060ec0ecaa5c2bf19f9f76b8986a26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/63d166df81060ec0ecaa5c2bf19f9f76b8986a26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/a30dc419524bef52ba4ffbd1121e0d86b266cac4","verification":{"payload":"tree 63d166df81060ec0ecaa5c2bf19f9f76b8986a26\nparent 13a08bd1ae5bc2ba99804603a476e70ce48c062a\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1788608231 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788608231 -0300\n\nfeat: register labor-performance analytics + wire BFF reports URLs (#4)\n\nTwo real deploy gaps closed:\n\n1. labor-performance was excluded from analytics_services -- its chart\n   shipped no projector/reports templates at all (a different, earlier\n   gap than fulfillment-execution''s Dockerfile CrashLoopBackOff issue),\n   closed by labor-performance''s own feature/analytics-chart-wiring PR.\n   Adding it here to analytics_services auto-wires its analytics DB,\n   role, and Helm analytics.* values via the existing generic\n   for_each -- no new Terraform logic needed.\n\n2. warehouse-ops-agent''s console-bff gained a WMS/WES dashboard fan-out\n   (PR #27) reading 7 new *_REPORTS_REST_URL env vars, but this repo''s\n   ops-agent.tf never templated them -- every dashboard section would\n   silently degrade to available:false in a real cluster deploy despite\n   the code being live. Wires all 7 to the real in-cluster\n   ''<service>-reports'' Service DNS names (the analytics reports Service\n   every analytics-enabled chart''s reportsFullname helper creates).\n\nNote: terraform validate/plan/apply for this change must run from the\nactual warehouse-infra checkout (not this worktree) -- the config''s\n../../<name> sibling-repo paths only resolve correctly when\nwarehouse-infra sits directly alongside the other repos under\n~/warehouse-systems, which a git worktree subdirectory breaks. Verified\nterraform fmt is clean; full validate/plan run from the main checkout.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqm/7nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWogQAAICmq1k0SOLrOE4rOC5uB1+\n2Ps06PgUpFwUl54CTo0GHXgPQtDGS/QsAo/i0VJJoonc4z1Hts8/ZSym3BPmVc+b\nyoqaHkSivsL9EyACPZ3lQDu0plmn7OOstrEQqPHA7dkJ1wD48flgyNqoDsmhqgkx\n4zOxPToxZBD6L03rah+vrL0PCyEZRLyLqtV85rv0eLiKNLzZagLvNrSC81aoK6dg\nzvByar0KGIJAFQNO0wF/eKoqmeYmntLZsV8+4yWr5GMm8bWaQfDTyV53svr7iDfF\nj+RlaftRmv8/Xf8A93hQ6S1280Gn5xnqBT/EmNEWfKLQiI6iQ7LXR5T9eTetP6i0\nUx7Diupr723vW/2VAyWkOIdLSjhezTHqRn6sBXMfIxm5U4/qnUft5EKZ9stkK/4Z\na0oZvAJLlUsSpJAu2K9nTpsLiWRl1qrIs85OEWt7S+RNHoR7tU7TQ+aIPQ/qNJbF\nDx8fvjsXsYDnHEK/NBcHnwyjhYnGnFlmr3VD3skFmEUBjQZANhjss3KpjWcW7Gpg\nh0/7VX6zCxni4kO3IeYI1OXIQ7CpFiKPwK7YR9Xxjz5nv6n6LyfCriC2jirfN0G0\nrlvXAh5GCiM/c7NzROrOnYoLzZue1e7XZfQ1UvbIkoORtW4TLtp+HVWN0LSrdvvu\nv2FTChd4F68n3zubBnKk\n=Pvp0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T11:37:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.github