,"repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/50063dc1e2ac768b9c5191ed17dc424d7682366f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T23:50:56Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T23:50:56Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"feat: re-include fulfillment-execution in the analytics rollout\n\nIts Dockerfile deploy gap (missing projector/reports binaries) merged\nas PR #47 (https://github.com/claudioed/fulfillment-execution/pull/47)\non 2026-08-30. Re-adds it to terraform/locals.tf''s analytics_services\nset and flips analytics.enabled: true in its helm-values.\n\nNOT YET applied to the live cluster: REPOS_ROOT/fulfillment-execution\n(what build-and-load.sh actually builds the image from) currently has\nunrelated uncommitted work on feature/gift-wrap-handling-flag. Running\nterraform apply against that dirty checkout would bake those\nin-progress changes into the live image alongside the Dockerfile fix.\nClean/fast-forward that checkout (or build+load from a disposable\norigin/develop worktree, the same approach used to verify PR #47''s fix\nitself) before the next terraform apply picks this back up.","tree":{"sha":"a6f35da53c7fc7da056b9b4ce8a8fca070c7f174","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/a6f35da53c7fc7da056b9b4ce8a8fca070c7f174"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/50063dc1e2ac768b9c5191ed17dc424d7682366f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/50063dc1e2ac768b9c5191ed17dc424d7682366f","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDUwMDYzZGMxZTJhYzc2OGI5YzUxOTFlZDE3ZGM0MjRkNzY4MjM2NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/9e05c636656948c15d0b96600c3bc85c1fdd162c","sha":"9e05c636656948c15d0b96600c3bc85c1fdd162c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/9e05c636656948c15d0b96600c3bc85c1fdd162c"}],"sha":"50063dc1e2ac768b9c5191ed17dc424d7682366f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/50063dc1e2ac768b9c5191ed17dc424d7682366f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/9e05c636656948c15d0b96600c3bc85c1fdd162c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T23:47:50Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T23:48:31Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"feat: register order-management/facility-layout/labor-performance, live Kafka, live analytics data-mesh\n\nThree prior-session infra changes now committed together (all already\napplied to the live ''warehouse'' kind cluster, verified running):\n\n1. Fleet growth: order-management, facility-layout, labor-performance\n   registered in terraform/locals.tf''s local.services (order-management,\n   facility-layout) and terraform/ops-agent.tf (warehouse-ops-agent, a\n   different shape -- no database, REST-fan-out only). New helm-values\n   files for all three.\n\n2. Live Kafka: terraform/kafka.tf -- single-broker Bitnami Kafka release\n   (KRaft mode), replication factor forced to 1 to match the single-broker\n   topology (fixes the offsets/transaction-state default of 3, which\n   crash-loops any consumer-group service like labor-performance).\n   EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka + kafka.enabled=true flipped live for every\n   service that supports it (inventory-storage, wes-work-planning,\n   fulfillment-execution, workforce-management, order-management,\n   facility-layout).\n\n3. Live analytics data-mesh (ADR-0010): the projector+reports \"report\n   part\" turned on (analytics.enabled: true) for 5 of the 6\n   analytics-chart-capable services -- wes-work-planning,\n   order-management, inventory-storage, workforce-management,\n   facility-layout. fulfillment-execution is DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED for\n   now: its Dockerfile had (has, pending review) a real deploy gap --\n   never built/copied the projector/reports binaries its own chart\n   references -- fix out for review at\n   https://github.com/claudioed/fulfillment-execution/pull/47.\n   terraform/postgres.tf provisions one additional \"<svc>_analytics\"\n   database + role per analytics-enabled service (random_password.\n   service_analytics_db, fed through init-databases.sql.tftpl and\n   terraform/services.tf''s per-service analytics.database.projectorUrl/\n   reportsUrl). labor-performance is excluded (pure Kafka consumer, no\n   analytics chart of its own).\n\n   A SECOND real deploy gap was found and already fixed live (fix out\n   for review at https://github.com/claudioed/wes-work-planning/pull/40):\n   wes-work-planning''s own Dockerfile had the identical\n   projector/reports-binaries-never-built gap, caught only because its\n   pods crash-looped after the database/role existed (all 4 other\n   services'' images already had the binaries).\n\nVerified against the live cluster, not just planned: \"terraform apply\"\nconverged (root-caused and worked through a \"pending-upgrade\"-locked\nHelm state stuck under a foreground timeout via \"helm rollback\" --\ndocumented as a real operational hazard, not a config bug); all 5\n\"<svc>_analytics\" databases/roles created by hand against the live,\nalready-initialized Postgres instance (initdb only runs on an empty\ndata directory, so a running cluster''s new roles/databases from a\nchanged init script are never auto-applied -- same category as\nwes-work-planning''s existing OLTP by-hand-migration note); all 10\nprojector+reports pods are 2/2 Running with zero restarts after the\nwes-work-planning image reload; all 5 reports services answer a real\nin-cluster GET /healthz with {\"status\":\"ok\"}; all 5 projector logs\nshow a real Kafka consumer connected to their own analytics topic,\nnot just \"started\".","tree":{"sha":"251fdc666fcb8ad2af0d33c06b3a8ae39e7d3931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/trees/251fdc666fcb8ad2af0d33c06b3a8ae39e7d3931"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/git/commits/9e05c636656948c15d0b96600c3bc85c1fdd162c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/9e05c636656948c15d0b96600c3bc85c1fdd162c","node_id":"C_kwDOUEmPD9oAKDllMDVjNjM2NjU2OTQ4YzE1ZDBiOTY2MDBjM2JjODVjMWZkZDE2MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commit/0f613ccee05cc1e0184755e66e62af5faec75e3e","sha":"0f613ccee05cc1e0184755e66e62af5faec75e3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-infra/commits/0f613ccee05cc1e0184755e66e62af5faec75e3e"}],